1
00:00:00,668 --> 00:00:02,537
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:05,773
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:05,807 --> 00:00:08,610
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:08,643 --> 00:00:12,113
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:12,147 --> 00:00:14,982
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:18,453
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:18,487 --> 00:00:20,988
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:21,022 --> 00:00:22,790
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:22,823 --> 00:00:25,227
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:30,665
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:33,868
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:33,902 --> 00:00:36,738
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:36,772 --> 00:00:39,940
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:42,977
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:46,180
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:49,417
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:52,387
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:54,055 --> 00:00:55,923
LET'S GO.

19
00:00:55,957 --> 00:00:57,225
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:00:57,258 --> 00:00:58,527
HI, GIRL.

21
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,395
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:00,428 --> 00:01:01,963
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:01,997 --> 00:01:04,965
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:07,802
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:07,835 --> 00:01:10,838
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:14,208
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:14,242 --> 00:01:16,945
♪ FOR... ♪

28
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:31,192
DID-- DID I SHOW
YOU GUYS MY MAGICAL,

29
00:01:31,225 --> 00:01:32,627
WHIMSICAL
SQUIRTING FLOWER?

30
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:34,228
YES! ABOUT
A GAZILLION TIMES.

31
00:01:34,262 --> 00:01:36,965
OH. WELL,
DID I SHOW YOU MY RASH?

32
00:01:36,998 --> 00:01:38,733
[ALL SHOUT, GROAN]

33
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:40,033
DON'T DO IT, PLEASE!

34
00:01:40,067 --> 00:01:41,702
HI EVERYBODY, WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

35
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:43,872
MY NAME'S JOEL ROBINSON.
ABOUT THREE WEEKS AGO,

36
00:01:43,905 --> 00:01:45,407
I SET UP THIS
HOLO-CLOWN SEQUENCE.

37
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,175
IT WOULD CHEER UP THE BOTS,
BUT NOW I CAN'T

38
00:01:47,208 --> 00:01:48,877
GET IT TO TURN OFF,
AND IT'S GETTING HARD

39
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:51,178
TO SLEEP AT NIGHT,
AND I'M TASTING METAL.

40
00:01:51,212 --> 00:01:53,982
HEY, LITTLE GIRL. WOULD YOU
LIKE A SALTED NUT ROLL?

41
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:55,783
AAH! JOEL, JOEL--

42
00:01:55,817 --> 00:01:57,718
[CLOWN SCREAMS]

43
00:01:57,752 --> 00:01:59,420
WHY ARE YOU YELLING?
SHUT UP! SHUT UP!

44
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:01,688
YOU THINK I LIKE IT,
BEING STUCK IN LIMBO WITH YOU?

45
00:02:01,722 --> 00:02:03,525
NO! GET ON YOUR
ORANGE AND YELLOW KNEES

46
00:02:03,558 --> 00:02:06,193
AND KISS MY CLOWN FEET
THAT I HAVEN'T KILLED YOU.

47
00:02:06,227 --> 00:02:08,062
JOEL, THIS IS GETTING WEIRD.
YOU GOTTA DO SOMETHING.

48
00:02:08,095 --> 00:02:09,930
I'M WORKING ON IT.

49
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:11,265
[MAGIC VOICE]
JOEL, DO SOMETHING.

50
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:13,000
I HATE THOSE CLOWNS,
AND I DON'T EVEN EXIST.

51
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:14,135
THAT'S THE ONE.
THAT'S THE ONE.

52
00:02:14,168 --> 00:02:15,403
JOEL ROBINSON!
DON'T YOU DO THAT!

53
00:02:15,437 --> 00:02:17,605
- DON'T YOU DO THAT!
- I HAVE TO DO IT!

54
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:21,542
[ALL SCREAM OVER EACH OTHER]

55
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,882
- COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.
- WELL. LET'S NOT

56
00:02:26,915 --> 00:02:28,517
- DO THAT AGAIN.
- OH BOY.

57
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:29,717
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

58
00:02:37,692 --> 00:02:39,460
[SERVO AS BEAT POET]
CLOWNS ARE RAINING DOWN.

59
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:41,128
HEAR THE SCREAM
OF THE GREASE PAINT.

60
00:02:41,162 --> 00:02:44,065
DANGER. CLOWN PUDDLES.

61
00:02:44,098 --> 00:02:46,800
NICE HAIKU, TOM. VERY GOOD.
CROW, YOU'RE NEXT.

62
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:50,638
OH, THE CAPTAIN
AND TENNILLE ARE CALLING.

63
00:02:50,672 --> 00:02:54,575
AH. ROBINSON. SERVO.
MR. T. ROBOT.

64
00:02:54,608 --> 00:02:56,010
OUR INVENTION THIS WEEK

65
00:02:56,043 --> 00:02:58,078
IS INSPIRED BY
TODAY'S EXPERIMENT,

66
00:02:58,112 --> 00:03:00,113
ATTACK OF
THE GIANT LEECHES.

67
00:03:00,147 --> 00:03:02,117
IN YE OLDEN TIMES,

68
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:05,320
ALCHEMISTS BELIEVED THAT LEECHES
SERVED MEDICINAL PURPOSES.

69
00:03:05,353 --> 00:03:07,355
- SO DO WE.
- YES,

70
00:03:07,388 --> 00:03:10,792
AND WE'VE FOUND THAT
THE COMMON FRESHWATER LEECH

71
00:03:10,825 --> 00:03:13,728
CAN SERVE THE SAME PURPOSE
AS A NICOTINE PATCH.

72
00:03:13,762 --> 00:03:16,030
AND BEING NEITHER
FOOD NOR DRUG,

73
00:03:16,063 --> 00:03:18,933
THERE'S NO PESKY
FDA REGULATION

74
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:20,302
TO IMPEDE YOUR PROGRESS.

75
00:03:20,335 --> 00:03:22,303
AND I CAN
EXPERIMENT AT WILL.

76
00:03:22,337 --> 00:03:24,572
- FRANK?
- AT YOUR SERVICE.

77
00:03:24,605 --> 00:03:26,908
OUR SUBJECT, FRANK,

78
00:03:26,942 --> 00:03:29,510
HAS BEEN TRYING TO QUIT SMOKING
FOR QUITE SOME TIME.

79
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:31,512
HE'S A THREE-PACK-A-DAY MAN.

80
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:33,815
- NO, I'M NOT.
- YES, YOU ARE. SHUT UP.

81
00:03:33,848 --> 00:03:35,417
- [FRANK MOUTHS WORDS]
- NOW, THIS LEECH--

82
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:37,952
- WE'LL CALL HIM PATCHES.
- AAH!

83
00:03:37,985 --> 00:03:41,455
UH, WHEN APPLIED
TO THE NECK AND HEAD AREA,

84
00:03:41,488 --> 00:03:44,292
- WILL SUCK
ANY DESIRE TO SMOKE--
- NO, NO, NO.

85
00:03:44,325 --> 00:03:47,195
- OUT OF FRANK.
- NO! NO! NO! NO!

86
00:03:47,228 --> 00:03:48,830
I'M THE SUM OF MY VICES!

87
00:03:48,863 --> 00:03:52,300
I HAVE MY PAIN, MY HAPPINESS,
MY LOSSES, MY LOVE!

88
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:54,802
MY STRUGGLES!
MY HOBBIES! MYLANTA!

89
00:03:54,835 --> 00:03:57,005
I WANT TO LIVE!
I WANT TO LIVE!

90
00:03:57,038 --> 00:03:59,740
I WANT TO LIVE AND LOVE
AND LEARN AND LIVE!

91
00:03:59,773 --> 00:04:01,075
BUT THIS WON'T HURT A BIT.

92
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:03,310
OKAY.

93
00:04:03,343 --> 00:04:05,245
THERE YOU GO.
NOW, PATCHES,

94
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:08,082
I'M DEPENDING ON YOU,
YOU SLUG.

95
00:04:08,115 --> 00:04:10,485
HEY, THIS IS THE MOST
ACTION I'VE GOTTEN--

96
00:04:10,518 --> 00:04:13,722
FRANK. BACK TO YOU, JOEL.

97
00:04:13,755 --> 00:04:15,957
WELL, SIRS, AS YOU KNOW,

98
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:18,292
PUBERTY IS THAT TIME
WHEN CHILDHOOD

99
00:04:18,325 --> 00:04:20,193
CROSSES THAT
MIGHTY THRESHOLD

100
00:04:20,227 --> 00:04:21,895
- TO ADULTHOOD.
- MM-HMM.

101
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:23,665
KIDS CAN'T WAIT
FOR IT TO START.

102
00:04:23,698 --> 00:04:25,933
AND GROWN-UPS CAN'T WAIT
FOR IT TO LEAVE.

103
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:27,935
- [BOTS CHUCKLE]
- IT'S SPRINGTIME FOR YOUR BODY,

104
00:04:27,968 --> 00:04:30,872
AND YOU'RE ABOUT TO BLOOM
INTO BEAUTIFUL FLORA.

105
00:04:30,905 --> 00:04:33,140
BUT AS YOU KNOW,
BEING AN ADOLESCENT

106
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:34,875
IS TIME-CONSUMING.

107
00:04:34,908 --> 00:04:36,577
AND THAT'S WHY
WE CAME UP WITH THIS.

108
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,145
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE

109
00:04:38,178 --> 00:04:40,615
INSTY ADOLESCENT KIT.

110
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:43,250
YEAH. WHY WASTE YOUR TEENDOM
IN TORTUOUS FLUX

111
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,252
WHEN THOSE
FUNNY FEELINGS DOWNSTAIRS

112
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,122
CAN BE TAKEN CARE OF
IN A JIFFY?

113
00:04:47,155 --> 00:04:48,790
GET READY.
YOU'LL HAVE TO START

114
00:04:48,823 --> 00:04:50,057
SHOWERING DAILY

115
00:04:50,090 --> 00:04:51,392
- AS SEBACEOUS BILE--
- OH, NO, NO, NO!

116
00:04:51,425 --> 00:04:52,727
INCLUDED IN THE KIT

117
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,695
DOES DOUBLE-DUTY
ON YOUR SCALP,

118
00:04:54,728 --> 00:04:56,097
FACE, AND UNDERARMS.

119
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:57,898
EW, AND MY BACK TOO.

120
00:04:57,932 --> 00:05:00,902
YEAH, AND DON'T FORGET
THE OCTAVES YOU'LL ENCOMPASS

121
00:05:00,935 --> 00:05:02,437
WHEN YOU FINALLY ENCOUNTER

122
00:05:02,470 --> 00:05:05,973
OUR MINTY-FRESH
HORMONAL SPRAY.

123
00:05:06,007 --> 00:05:07,875
[VOICE CRACKING]
HELLO, SUZIE. WANNA GO

124
00:05:07,908 --> 00:05:10,010
TO THE SNOW DAYS DANCE
WITH ME?

125
00:05:10,043 --> 00:05:11,878
AND THAT'S WHEN YOUR FACE
TURNS BEET-RED.

126
00:05:11,912 --> 00:05:13,848
BUT IT'S OKAY,
'CAUSE SUZIE WON'T NOTICE.

127
00:05:13,882 --> 00:05:15,850
BECAUSE YOU'LL BE
COVERED WITH PIMPLES.

128
00:05:15,883 --> 00:05:18,252
YOU GUYS JUST
DON'T UNDERSTAND ME!

129
00:05:18,285 --> 00:05:20,087
THAT'S RIGHT.
NOW THAT YOU'RE A TEEN,

130
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,190
THE MOST INNOCENT REMARKS
BY FRIENDS AND FAMILY

131
00:05:22,223 --> 00:05:24,025
WILL BE CONSTRUED
AS PERSONAL ATTACKS.

132
00:05:24,058 --> 00:05:26,493
OH, AND WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

133
00:05:26,527 --> 00:05:28,328
WELL, FORTUNATELY,
EACH KIT COMES

134
00:05:28,362 --> 00:05:30,898
WITH ITS OWN
PERSONAL RETORT CARDS.

135
00:05:30,932 --> 00:05:33,935
WITH COMEBACKS LIKE,
"YOU JUST HAVE NO CLUE!"

136
00:05:33,968 --> 00:05:35,603
"WHO WAS IN MY ROOM?"

137
00:05:35,637 --> 00:05:37,672
AND "YOU GUYS ARE
SO PHONY!"

138
00:05:37,705 --> 00:05:39,140
YOU'RE NOT THE BOSS OF ME!

139
00:05:39,173 --> 00:05:40,542
HEY, BUT THERE'S MORE.

140
00:05:40,575 --> 00:05:41,808
- [SERVO MUTTERS]
- FOOD PILLS.

141
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:43,845
YES, YOU'LL SPAN
THE EMOTIONAL GLOBE

142
00:05:43,878 --> 00:05:45,178
WHEN YOU EXPERIENCE
EVERYTHING FROM

143
00:05:45,212 --> 00:05:47,115
MILD NAUSEA
AND PERSISTENT DREAD

144
00:05:47,148 --> 00:05:49,350
TO ECSTATIC FEELINGS
OF IMMORTALITY.

145
00:05:49,383 --> 00:05:51,252
--THINK I'M STUPID
OR SOMETHING?

146
00:05:51,285 --> 00:05:52,720
ALL THIS IN ONE AFTERNOON.

147
00:05:52,753 --> 00:05:54,455
I DON'T CARE ANYMORE.

148
00:05:54,488 --> 00:05:56,123
GREAT, BUT I STILL
DON'T HAVE MY LICENSE.

149
00:05:56,157 --> 00:05:57,592
OH, LISTEN, MISTER.
IF YOU DON'T LIKE IT,

150
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,593
YOU CAN STAY IN A HOTEL
DOWN THE STREET.

151
00:05:59,627 --> 00:06:01,262
- WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?
- JERK.

152
00:06:01,295 --> 00:06:03,130
VERY AMUSING, JOEL.

153
00:06:03,163 --> 00:06:06,400
BUT LET'S NOT FORGET
WHY YOU'RE UP THERE.

154
00:06:06,433 --> 00:06:08,870
TO WATCH REALLY BAD MOVIES.

155
00:06:08,903 --> 00:06:10,405
AND NOW,

156
00:06:10,438 --> 00:06:13,040
A DR. CLAYTON FORRESTER
PRESENTATION.

157
00:06:13,073 --> 00:06:15,342
ATTACK OF THE GIANT
LEECHES.

158
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:17,478
OH, YOU'RE DOING HOMEWORK,
ALL RIGHT.

159
00:06:17,512 --> 00:06:19,247
- OH YEAH, YOU ARE--
- I DON'T CARE.
YOU GUYS ARE SO LAME--

160
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,282
- [ALARM BLARES]
- OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

161
00:06:21,315 --> 00:06:24,052
I DON'T CARE!
I DON'T CARE! I DON'T CARE!

162
00:06:32,193 --> 00:06:33,862
YOU'RE NOT MY FATHER,
YOU KNOW.

163
00:06:33,895 --> 00:06:35,763
OH YEAH?

164
00:06:35,797 --> 00:06:37,832
♪ BEHOLD...
KING OF THE SEA ♪

165
00:06:37,865 --> 00:06:40,568
♪ FOR FABLED ATLANTIS'S
PRINCE OF THE DEEP ♪

166
00:06:40,602 --> 00:06:43,237
OH LOOK, IT'S THE UNDERSEA
FOOTBALL ALL-STARS!

167
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:46,507
THEY PLAYED U.S.C. TODAY.

168
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:48,042
[ALL]
♪ HEY ♪

169
00:06:48,075 --> 00:06:49,610
♪ IT'S THE UNDERSEA
KINGDOM ♪

170
00:06:49,643 --> 00:06:50,945
♪ FOR YOU AND FOR ME ♪

171
00:06:50,978 --> 00:06:53,313
♪ AND IT'S FUN ♪

172
00:06:53,347 --> 00:06:55,783
[SERVO HUMS 1812 OVERTURE]

173
00:06:55,817 --> 00:06:58,418
LOOKS LIKE RUSH HOUR
ON SPAGHETTI JUNCTION.

174
00:06:58,452 --> 00:07:00,922
OOH, IT'S ALL
WHIRLY-TWIRLY.

175
00:07:02,723 --> 00:07:04,158
- OH--
- HUH?

176
00:07:04,192 --> 00:07:05,960
OH, IT'S BEN-HUR.
I'VE SEEN THIS BEFORE.

177
00:07:05,993 --> 00:07:07,695
OH.

178
00:07:07,728 --> 00:07:09,663
HEY! HEY, YOU GUYS!

179
00:07:09,697 --> 00:07:11,598
DO WE KNOW WHERE WE'RE--
OH, I THOUGHT SO.

180
00:07:11,632 --> 00:07:14,035
- COME ON. COME ON!
- BACK THIS WAY.

181
00:07:14,068 --> 00:07:17,838
THEY HAVE NO CLUE, DO THEY?

182
00:07:17,872 --> 00:07:20,475
G. HEILEMAN BREWING COMPANY,
LA CROSSE, WISCONSIN.

183
00:07:20,508 --> 00:07:22,910
WHEN IN LAS VEGAS,
VISIT EXCALIBUR.

184
00:07:22,943 --> 00:07:26,847
OOH.

185
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,450
[SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

186
00:07:30,485 --> 00:07:31,818
BENEATH THE OCEAN FLOOR,

187
00:07:31,852 --> 00:07:33,855
IT'S ALL FULL OF MILDEW
DOWN THERE.

188
00:07:33,888 --> 00:07:36,057
LET'S GO GATHER AROUND
THE WATER COOLER.

189
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:38,225
- WE ARE THE WATER COOLER.
- OH.

190
00:07:38,258 --> 00:07:41,628
I LOVE THAT ONE.

191
00:07:41,662 --> 00:07:43,197
ANNAPOLIS A DAY

192
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:44,965
KEEPS THE DOCTORIS AWAY.

193
00:07:44,998 --> 00:07:48,368
[BOTS LAUGH]

194
00:07:48,402 --> 00:07:50,103
[ALL]
♪ WE'RE WALKIN'
REALLY REALLY FAST♪

195
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:51,905
♪ WE'RE WALKIN'
REALLY REALLY FAST ♪

196
00:07:51,938 --> 00:07:54,908
♪ AND THEN WE'RE WALK... ♪

197
00:07:54,942 --> 00:07:57,178
CONGRATULATIONS, SOLDIERS.
GO OUT AND KILL.

198
00:07:57,212 --> 00:07:58,445
OH. HERE. ONE FOR YOU.

199
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,180
CONGRATULATIONS.
GO OUT AND KILL.

200
00:08:00,213 --> 00:08:02,417
OOH-- OH.

201
00:08:02,450 --> 00:08:04,218
HOW ABOUT IT, DOC?
DO YOU THINK I'LL LIVE?

202
00:08:04,252 --> 00:08:05,953
YOU LOOK KIND OF
WEAK AND PUNY,

203
00:08:05,987 --> 00:08:07,955
- BUT I THINK
YOU'LL PULL THROUGH.
- I'M KIDDING, OF COURSE!

204
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,923
YOU'RE ONE OF
THE FINEST SPECIMENS
TO EVER COME THROUGH HERE.

205
00:08:09,957 --> 00:08:12,058
THANK YOU, SIR.

206
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:13,427
NEXT.

207
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,495
GREAT CHAPS. I WISH
WE HAD MORE LIKE HIM--

208
00:08:15,530 --> 00:08:16,763
AH, KEEP YOUR MIND
ON YOUR WORK.

209
00:08:16,797 --> 00:08:18,265
YOU'RE IN ENOUGH TROUBLE
AS IT IS.

210
00:08:18,298 --> 00:08:20,602
--TOO BAD
THIS IS THE LAST YEAR.

211
00:08:20,635 --> 00:08:22,102
HE'LL MAKE A GRAND
NAVAL OFFICER.

212
00:08:22,135 --> 00:08:23,503
HE'LL MAKE SEVERAL OF THEM.

213
00:08:23,537 --> 00:08:25,807
HEY, HE'S POSING
FOR A WHEATIES BOX.

214
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:28,642
[ALL SCREAM]

215
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,745
[SERVO HUMS, RASPBERRIES]

216
00:08:33,047 --> 00:08:35,650
I AM THE GOD OF HELLFIRE!

217
00:08:35,683 --> 00:08:37,952
ALL THESE PEOPLE ARE DEAD NOW.
ISN'T THAT WEIRD?

218
00:08:37,985 --> 00:08:40,453
THINK ABOUT IT--
OH NO, A FOOTBALL GAME

219
00:08:40,487 --> 00:08:41,855
HAS BROKEN OUT,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN!

220
00:08:41,888 --> 00:08:42,857
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO MAKE OF IT!

221
00:08:42,890 --> 00:08:44,125
THIS MAKES ME LONESOME FOR

222
00:08:44,158 --> 00:08:45,860
MY OLD ELECTRIC
FOOTBALL GAME.

223
00:08:45,893 --> 00:08:49,063
[BOTS]
AWW.

224
00:08:49,097 --> 00:08:51,332
IT'S GOOD PLUMBER MAN DAY
TODAY.

225
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:54,035
WHAT'RE THOSE LAB TECHNICIANS
DOING ON THE FIELD?

226
00:08:54,068 --> 00:08:55,268
THE BALL'S BACK FROM CENTER.
GOES TO SMITH

227
00:08:55,302 --> 00:08:56,737
AND REVERTS TO CORRIGAN.
CORRIGAN--

228
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:58,072
OH LOOK.

229
00:08:58,105 --> 00:09:01,075
GETS THE FULLBACK,
KNOCKS HIM DOWN!

230
00:09:01,108 --> 00:09:02,477
LOOKS LIKE THEY'RE PLAYING
IN CHOCOLATE.

231
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:04,545
IT'S THE HERSHEY BOWL.

232
00:09:04,578 --> 00:09:06,813
--ARE COMING IN!
HE HITS BACK, KNOCKS HIM OVER!

233
00:09:06,847 --> 00:09:09,250
[SERVO MIMICS MUD SQUELCHING]

234
00:09:09,283 --> 00:09:11,552
[SERVO RASPBERRIES]

235
00:09:11,585 --> 00:09:14,222
--CRASH CORRIGAN,
CAPTAIN OF THE NAVY TEAM.

236
00:09:14,255 --> 00:09:15,890
YOU KNOW, IN THE FUTURE,
PEOPLE WILL PAY

237
00:09:15,923 --> 00:09:18,258
- TO SEE WOMEN DO THIS.
- OOH.

238
00:09:18,292 --> 00:09:21,662
TAKE IT BACK! MY SISTER DOES NOT
SWIM TOWARDS TUBE SHIPS!

239
00:09:21,695 --> 00:09:22,997
OH, SMOOTH. SMOOTH--

240
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:25,032
[CLEARS THROAT]

241
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:26,833
[ALL]
♪ WELL, I'D LIKE
TO KNOW WHERE ♪

242
00:09:26,867 --> 00:09:28,937
♪ YOU GOT THE NOTION ♪

243
00:09:28,970 --> 00:09:30,570
♪ OH, I'D LIKE
TO KNOW WHERE ♪

244
00:09:30,605 --> 00:09:32,072
♪ YOU GOT THE NOTION ♪

245
00:09:32,105 --> 00:09:34,008
♪ --LIKE TO KNOW WHERE
YOU GOT THE NOTION ♪

246
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:35,743
WAIT A MINUTE, SON.
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

247
00:09:35,777 --> 00:09:37,812
I'VE GOTTA SEE
LIEUTENANT CORRIGAN RIGHT AWAY.

248
00:09:37,845 --> 00:09:39,547
YOU CAN'T GO IN THERE.
IT'S AGAINST ORDERS.

249
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,682
BUT I TELL YA, I GOTTA SEE HIM.
IT'S IMPORTANT!

250
00:09:41,715 --> 00:09:45,653
I'M HIS SON. HE DOESN'T
KNOW ABOUT ME YET.

251
00:09:45,687 --> 00:09:47,020
EVEN IF I LET YOU IN,
YOU COULDN'T

252
00:09:47,053 --> 00:09:49,157
TALK TO THE LIEUTENANT NOW.
HE'S BUSY.

253
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:51,692
- NICE SHOES.
- ALL RIGHT.

254
00:09:51,725 --> 00:09:53,060
[CROW CHUCKLES]

255
00:09:53,093 --> 00:09:54,828
LITTLE JERK.

256
00:09:54,862 --> 00:09:56,163
HMM.

257
00:09:56,197 --> 00:09:58,665
WOW, JEEPERS, HOT DOG!

258
00:09:58,698 --> 00:10:02,268
AND EVERYWHERE, THE SMELL OF MEN
ENJOYING THEMSELVES.

259
00:10:02,303 --> 00:10:05,472
OOH. OOH!

260
00:10:05,505 --> 00:10:07,342
UH-OH.

261
00:10:07,375 --> 00:10:10,010
I'LL SHOW THEM.
I'M GONNA JUMP OFF!

262
00:10:10,043 --> 00:10:13,547
NO! DON'T DO IT!

263
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:16,150
AND NOW BACK TO
MEN WITH LITTLE PANTS.

264
00:10:16,183 --> 00:10:18,018
[BOTS GRUNT]

265
00:10:20,822 --> 00:10:24,525
♪ OH, SHE CAME IN THROUGH
THE BATHROOM WINDOW ♪

266
00:10:28,062 --> 00:10:31,998
UH-OH, HE'S HAVING
AN EPISODE.

267
00:10:32,032 --> 00:10:33,833
- GOOD WORK, JIMMY!
- JIMMY SMITS.

268
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:36,203
- DON'T LET HIM PIN YA, SON--
- GIVE HIM A WEDGIE!

269
00:10:36,237 --> 00:10:38,238
- YOU ALMOST HAD HIM THAT TIME--
- TRIPLE HERMAN!

270
00:10:38,272 --> 00:10:39,507
WHOO! WET WILLY!

271
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:41,208
IT WAS.

272
00:10:41,242 --> 00:10:43,643
THE TIN DRUM.

273
00:10:45,847 --> 00:10:47,715
- OOH.
- LET'S GO DOWN THE SLIDE
LIKE THIS!

274
00:10:47,748 --> 00:10:49,517
[BOTS]
WHEE!

275
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:50,918
HOLD HIM!

276
00:10:50,952 --> 00:10:53,320
YOU KNOW, THERE'S SOMETHING
SICK ABOUT THIS, JOEL.

277
00:10:53,353 --> 00:10:55,022
YEAH. I CALL IT
HISTORY, TOM.

278
00:10:55,055 --> 00:10:57,358
- MM-HMM.
- VICTORY AT SEA.

279
00:10:57,392 --> 00:10:59,993
NOW YOU GOT HIM, CRASH!
GIVE HIM THE AIRPLANE SPIN!

280
00:11:00,027 --> 00:11:02,497
GOOD IDEA, KID.
WHY DIDN'T I THINK OF THAT?

281
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:05,432
[BOTS]
HUH?

282
00:11:05,465 --> 00:11:07,802
- BENNY!
- DON'T BE A HERO!

283
00:11:07,835 --> 00:11:09,270
- HOLD TIGHT!

284
00:11:09,303 --> 00:11:12,038
- DON'T NEED THAT.
- HEY.

285
00:11:12,072 --> 00:11:14,342
- HOLD IT!
- WHOOP!

286
00:11:14,375 --> 00:11:16,310
[MONKEY CHIRPS, SCREAMS]

287
00:11:19,213 --> 00:11:21,748
AH, JUST SAVE THE KID.
STOP SHOWING OFF.

288
00:11:24,085 --> 00:11:25,352
YEAH, THAT'S WHAT HAPPENS
WHEN YOU SPEND A LOT OF TIME

289
00:11:25,385 --> 00:11:28,255
AROUND SAILORS, YOU KNOW.

290
00:11:28,288 --> 00:11:31,592
THANK GOD THEY BUILT THIS PLACE
LIKE A JUNGLE GYM.

291
00:11:31,625 --> 00:11:33,760
HOLD ON, LET ME
CLOSE THE WINDOW FIRST.

292
00:11:33,793 --> 00:11:36,163
LET'S GO, COME ON.
I GOT YOU.

293
00:11:36,197 --> 00:11:40,133
- HOORAY!
- GIVE US BARABBAS!

294
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:41,502
EH, CATCH HIM, YOU MUGS.

295
00:11:41,535 --> 00:11:44,372
[SERVO SCREAMS]

296
00:11:44,405 --> 00:11:46,973
AAH, YOU GOT ACNE
ALL OVER YOUR BACK-- YUCK!

297
00:11:47,007 --> 00:11:48,908
- [CROW MONKEY-CHIRPS]
- HEY KID, FEEL FREE

298
00:11:48,942 --> 00:11:52,178
TO DIG YOUR HEEL
INTO MY GROIN.

299
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:53,813
NOW SOMEBODY'S
GOTTA SAVE ME.

300
00:11:53,847 --> 00:11:55,883
[BOTS CHUCKLE]

301
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:02,222
THANKS, FRIEND.

302
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:03,757
- HOLD TIGHT, BILLY.
- OKAY.

303
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:07,160
[CROW HUMS, STRAINS]

304
00:12:07,193 --> 00:12:09,730
YAY! WHOO!

305
00:12:09,763 --> 00:12:11,165
- TA-DA!
- [ALL WHISTLE]

306
00:12:11,198 --> 00:12:12,398
I THOUGHT
THE KID WAS A GONER.

307
00:12:12,433 --> 00:12:13,867
WHAT WERE YOU
DOING UP THERE?

308
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,203
DAD SENT ME OVER TO GET YOU,
BUT THEY WOULDN'T LET ME IN.

309
00:12:16,237 --> 00:12:17,538
HAS HE HAD ANOTHER
EARTHQUAKE WARNING?

310
00:12:17,572 --> 00:12:19,640
YEAH. HE WANTS YOU
TO COME RIGHT OVER.

311
00:12:19,673 --> 00:12:21,075
WELL, WAIT UNTIL
I GET INTO MY CLOTHES.

312
00:12:21,108 --> 00:12:23,043
I'M GOING OVER TO
PROFESSOR NORTON'S LABORATORY.

313
00:12:23,077 --> 00:12:26,147
PUT ON A SARONG.
THAT'LL BE ALL YOU NEED.

314
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:28,248
WHAT YOU SAY IS VERY
INTERESTING, PROFESSOR NORTON--

315
00:12:28,282 --> 00:12:29,717
- BUT STUPID.
- BUT I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE

316
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:32,418
THAT THIS LITTLE MACHINE
CAN PREDICT EARTHQUAKES.

317
00:12:32,453 --> 00:12:34,288
NOT ONLY PREDICTS,
BUT PREVENTS THEM.

318
00:12:34,322 --> 00:12:37,725
- AND IT MAKES TOAST.
- IF YOU GET CLOSE ENOUGH
TO THE SOURCE.

319
00:12:37,758 --> 00:12:39,393
- HMM?
- OH, THERE YOU ARE,
LIEUTENANT.

320
00:12:39,427 --> 00:12:40,862
THE SIGNALS ARE
COMING IN MUCH STRONGER.

321
00:12:40,895 --> 00:12:43,797
OOH, THE EARTH
JUST MOVED FOR ME.

322
00:12:43,830 --> 00:12:46,333
THIS IS MS. COMPTON,
STAFF WRITER OF THE TIMES.

323
00:12:46,367 --> 00:12:48,502
WELL, EVERYBODY KNOWS
CRASH CORRIGAN.

324
00:12:48,535 --> 00:12:51,172
EVERYBODY DIGS BILL EVANS. SO?

325
00:12:51,205 --> 00:12:53,307
ANSWER UNCLEAR. ASK AGAIN.

326
00:12:55,242 --> 00:12:56,743
- POPCORN'S READY.
- AND IT MAKES

327
00:12:56,777 --> 00:12:58,045
THREE DIFFERENT KINDS
OF GELATI.

328
00:12:58,078 --> 00:12:59,313
--THE SIGNAL, AGAIN.

329
00:12:59,347 --> 00:13:01,715
THEY'VE BEEN SENDING IT
EVERY FIVE MINUTES.

330
00:13:01,748 --> 00:13:03,983
"THEY?" JUST WHO
DO YOU MEAN BY "THEY?"

331
00:13:04,017 --> 00:13:05,820
- COMEDY CENTRAL.
- PROFESSOR NORTON MAINTAINS

332
00:13:05,853 --> 00:13:08,722
THAT THESE SIGNALS MUST BE
THE WORK OF SOME HUMAN AGENCY.

333
00:13:08,755 --> 00:13:10,790
APPARENTLY COMING FROM
THE BOTTOM OF THE OCEAN.

334
00:13:10,825 --> 00:13:12,960
OH, THE WILLIAM MORRIS
AGENCY-- HUH?

335
00:13:12,993 --> 00:13:16,197
--FANTASTIC YARN ABOUT
THE LOST CONTINENT OF ATLANTIS.

336
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:19,667
EXACTLY. ONLY NOW I HAVE
SOME DEFINITE EVIDENCE.

337
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,935
LET ME GET IN MY COSTUME
AND TELL YOU ABOUT IT.

338
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:23,570
NOW, PRETEND
I'M A SWARTHY PIRATE.

339
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:25,973
- THIS IS PURE AURICHALCUM.
- NO, I'M NOT.

340
00:13:26,007 --> 00:13:28,142
A METAL MADE BY FUSING
GOLD AND COPPER.

341
00:13:28,175 --> 00:13:29,710
- GOPPER.
- THE SECRET OF THIS PROCESS

342
00:13:29,743 --> 00:13:31,445
WAS LOST FOR THE ATLANTEANS.

343
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:32,913
WHAT DOES THAT PROVE?

344
00:13:32,947 --> 00:13:34,348
WELL, ACCORDING
TO EVERY TEST,

345
00:13:34,382 --> 00:13:36,850
THE IDOL COULDN'T BE MORE THAN
A COUPLE OF YEARS OLD.

346
00:13:36,883 --> 00:13:38,285
SOMETHING MADE RECENTLY.

347
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:41,422
I FOUND IT DURING A RECENT TRIP
I MADE IN MY ROCKET SUBMARINE

348
00:13:41,455 --> 00:13:43,490
IN THIS GENERAL LOCATION.

349
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:45,325
YOU HAVE A RICH INNER LIFE,
DON'T YOU?

350
00:13:45,358 --> 00:13:47,027
--WHERE THE ANCIENT
CONTINENT OF ATLANTIS

351
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:49,397
WAS REPORTED TO HAVE SUNK
THOUSANDS OF YEARS AGO.

352
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:51,198
CONTRARY TO POPULAR BELIEF,

353
00:13:51,232 --> 00:13:53,100
ATLANTIS DID NOT
SINK OVERNIGHT,

354
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:54,702
BUT DURING
A PERIOD OF YEARS.

355
00:13:54,735 --> 00:13:56,470
THAT'S GREAT, GRAMPS--
GET THE MEDICATION.

356
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:58,472
--AMPLE OPPORTUNITY
TO CONSTRUCT

357
00:13:58,505 --> 00:14:00,273
A ROOF OF AURICHALCUM
OVER THE CITY

358
00:14:00,307 --> 00:14:01,642
AND KEEP OUT THE OCEAN--

359
00:14:01,675 --> 00:14:03,243
- AAH! THE FILM'S MELTING.
- OH-- OOH.

360
00:14:03,277 --> 00:14:04,878
IT'S A BETTER WORLD.

361
00:14:04,912 --> 00:14:08,815
XANADU. STATELY UNDERWATER HOME
OF CHARLES FOSTER KANE.

362
00:14:08,882 --> 00:14:11,452
COST? NO FISH CAN SAY.

363
00:14:14,755 --> 00:14:17,925
IT'S A DENVER PYLE STATUE.

364
00:14:17,958 --> 00:14:19,493
I BEG OF YOU TO TAKE SAFETY
IN THE CITADEL.

365
00:14:19,527 --> 00:14:23,263
- HEY-- OH.
- POSEIDON, GOD OF ATLANTIS,

366
00:14:23,297 --> 00:14:25,598
HAS NEVER FORSAKEN HIS PEOPLE
IN TIME OF NEED.

367
00:14:25,632 --> 00:14:26,733
JIFFY POP'S READY.

368
00:14:26,767 --> 00:14:30,337
I PROMISE YOU,
HE WILL NOT DO SO NOW.

369
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:33,773
[JOEL MIMICS TRUMPET]
IMPERIAL.

370
00:14:33,807 --> 00:14:37,510
--UNTIL WE HAVE BROKEN
THE POWER OF THIS EVIL USURPER,

371
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,980
UNGA KHAN.

372
00:14:40,013 --> 00:14:41,582
OH NO! THE KING'S MAD!
HE'S GONNA

373
00:14:41,615 --> 00:14:43,217
MAKE US PRETEND
WE'RE THE ROCKETTES AGAIN!

374
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:45,752
RUN!

375
00:14:45,785 --> 00:14:48,355
[SERVO MIMICS TRUMPET]

376
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:51,125
IT'S THE 1968
CHRYSLER MERRIMAC.

377
00:14:54,428 --> 00:14:57,497
- FONDUE.
- [ALL] MMM.

378
00:14:57,530 --> 00:15:00,567
OUR MEN ARE OUTNUMBERED.
THE CITY IS ABOUT TO FALL.

379
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:03,570
YOU KNOW, MAYOR DINKINS
JUST AIN'T CUTTIN' IT, IS HE?

380
00:15:07,173 --> 00:15:08,508
[SERVO HUMS]

381
00:15:08,542 --> 00:15:11,245
SAY.

382
00:15:11,278 --> 00:15:13,413
♪ ME AND MY SHADOW ♪

383
00:15:13,447 --> 00:15:15,315
♪ WALKING DOWN THE AVENUE ♪

384
00:15:18,218 --> 00:15:21,122
EH, MUST BE A MONDAY.

385
00:15:21,155 --> 00:15:22,388
[SERVO MIMICS TRUMPET]

386
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:23,990
TRAFFIC LIGHTS MUST BE OUT.

387
00:15:24,023 --> 00:15:26,060
- YEP.
- [SERVO MIMICS HORSE WHINNY]

388
00:15:26,093 --> 00:15:29,195
CAN YOU BELIEVE THIS CRAP?

389
00:15:29,228 --> 00:15:31,165
HEY, LOOK, DUNG BEETLES.

390
00:15:35,335 --> 00:15:37,037
I DON'T WANT THAT!

391
00:15:39,307 --> 00:15:41,575
[SERVO MIMICS SPRING]

392
00:15:41,608 --> 00:15:43,910
HE WAS MY FAVORITE.

393
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,445
OOH.

394
00:15:45,478 --> 00:15:47,715
KEN JUST EXPLODED, SIR.

395
00:15:49,850 --> 00:15:53,020
THEY BOMB HORSES,
DON'T THEY?

396
00:15:53,053 --> 00:15:55,188
[SERVO MIMICS BEEPING]

397
00:15:55,222 --> 00:15:56,890
BACKING UP.

398
00:15:56,923 --> 00:15:59,158
THERE'S THE BOMB
GOING INTO THE AIR SHAFT.

399
00:15:59,192 --> 00:16:01,828
OOH.

400
00:16:01,862 --> 00:16:04,398
THIS PLACE LOOKS LIKE
A BOMB JUST HIT IT.

401
00:16:04,432 --> 00:16:06,767
[BOTS GROAN]

402
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:10,003
[SERVO MIMICS TINY ENGINE]

403
00:16:10,037 --> 00:16:12,205
JANE, I'M HOME!

404
00:16:12,238 --> 00:16:13,907
DAVID CROSBY, NO!

405
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:15,875
I AM PLEASED TO REPORT
THAT SHARAD'S ARMY

406
00:16:15,908 --> 00:16:18,778
HAS BEEN DRIVEN WITHIN
THE WALLS OF THE SACRED CITY.

407
00:16:18,812 --> 00:16:20,847
GOOD. RECALL THE TROOPS.

408
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,050
WITH THOSE RELIGIOUS FANATICS
UNDER CONTROL,

409
00:16:23,083 --> 00:16:25,285
I'LL HAVE NO MORE INTERFERENCE
WITH MY PLANS

410
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,420
TO DESTROY THE UPPER WORLD.

411
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:29,188
[CROW CHUCKLES]
YOU ARE REALLY SOMETHING, BOSS.

412
00:16:29,222 --> 00:16:32,125
I THINK THIS IS YOUR YEAR.

413
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:35,228
YOUR HAT'S VERY CREATIVE
TODAY, KYLE.

414
00:16:35,262 --> 00:16:36,930
WHEN YOU DO SUCCEED
IN SENDING HIM

415
00:16:36,963 --> 00:16:38,365
TO THE BOTTOM OF THE SEA,

416
00:16:38,398 --> 00:16:41,302
ATLANTIS WILL RISE ONCE MORE
TO ITS FORMER PLACE IN THE SUN,

417
00:16:41,335 --> 00:16:43,203
AND YOU WILL BE
RULER OF ALL THINGS.

418
00:16:43,237 --> 00:16:45,172
START THE DISINTEGRATOR.

419
00:16:45,205 --> 00:16:47,975
D'AH, OKAY.

420
00:16:48,008 --> 00:16:49,577
[SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

421
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:51,678
GOTTA FINISH A GIANT ROLAID
FIRST, SIR.

422
00:16:51,712 --> 00:16:53,313
[CROW GROANS]

423
00:16:53,347 --> 00:16:55,048
OH LOOK, HERE'S DANIEL
IN THE LION'S DEN.

424
00:16:55,082 --> 00:16:57,683
- OH.
- THIS CLOWN'S MAKING CHANGE.

425
00:16:57,718 --> 00:16:59,653
THIS IS A GIANT
WELCH'S GRAPE JELLY MACHINE,

426
00:16:59,687 --> 00:17:01,020
AND I'M OUTTA HERE!
THANK YOU VERY MUCH,

427
00:17:01,055 --> 00:17:03,490
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.
GOOD NIGHT NOW.

428
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:06,227
- CAMERA CREW FROM REAL LIFE.
- OOH.

429
00:17:09,295 --> 00:17:10,597
SET IT FOR STUN.

430
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:13,200
LET'S PLAY SOME METAL! WHOO!

431
00:17:13,233 --> 00:17:17,170
YOU CLINKING, CLANKING,
CLATTERING COLLECTION
OF CALIGINOUS JUNK!

432
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:21,975
OH LOOK, HE'S PACKING
A TUMMY-SIZER.

433
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:24,210
♪ THE NIGHT CHICAGO DIED ♪

434
00:17:24,243 --> 00:17:25,878
♪ NA-NA-NA, NA-NA-NA ♪

435
00:17:25,912 --> 00:17:27,347
♪ CHICAGO DIED ♪

436
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,382
♪ BROTHER, WHAT A NIGHT
THE PEOPLE SAW ♪

437
00:17:29,417 --> 00:17:31,918
--COMMUNICATION CUT OFF.
RED CROSS IS APPEALING
FOR DOCTORS.

438
00:17:31,952 --> 00:17:33,387
SPECIAL TEAMS ARE RUNNING
SUPPLIES TO THE STRICKEN AREA.

439
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:35,888
- HMM. YOU IN THERE?
- SOLD AMERICAN.

440
00:17:35,922 --> 00:17:37,723
RUSHING THE MILITIA
TO THE SCENES OF THE DISASTER.

441
00:17:37,758 --> 00:17:39,760
BUT NOW ON
THE LIGHTER SIDE OF THE NEWS.

442
00:17:39,793 --> 00:17:41,328
SAINT CLAIRE?

443
00:17:41,362 --> 00:17:43,230
THAT'S ONLY
300 MILES FROM HERE.

444
00:17:43,263 --> 00:17:45,065
YES, AND ACCORDING
TO MY CALCULATIONS,

445
00:17:45,098 --> 00:17:47,533
ANOTHER SEVERE SHOCK
WILL OCCUR ANY MOMENT.

446
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:49,302
- BANG.
- --PUT THAT
COUNTERACTING MACHINE

447
00:17:49,335 --> 00:17:50,903
- ABOARD THE SUBMARINE
RIGHT AWAY.
- D'AH, OKAY.

448
00:17:50,937 --> 00:17:52,940
YOU MEAN YOU'RE GOING DOWN
TO TRY AND STOP THIS PLACE?

449
00:17:52,973 --> 00:17:55,508
WHAT A STORY THIS WILL MAKE
FOR MY PAPER.

450
00:18:02,983 --> 00:18:06,220
TROY TEMPEST, PHONES,
EQUALS STINGRAY.

451
00:18:06,253 --> 00:18:09,288
GRAY LADY DOWN, FOR CONTEL.

452
00:18:09,322 --> 00:18:11,858
PROFESSOR NORTON. NORTON!

453
00:18:11,892 --> 00:18:13,660
GET IN HERE.
OH, YOU'RE GETTING IN HERE.

454
00:18:13,693 --> 00:18:15,328
I DON'T KNOW.
WE'RE ON A LEVEL KEEL,

455
00:18:15,362 --> 00:18:17,497
BUT WE'RE BEING DRAGGED DOWN
BY SOME MYSTERIOUS FORCE.

456
00:18:17,530 --> 00:18:21,268
THE PLOT?

457
00:18:21,302 --> 00:18:22,803
WE'RE OUT OF
BAKING SODA, SIR.

458
00:18:22,837 --> 00:18:25,838
THIS SUB IS POWERED
BY FIZZIES.

459
00:18:29,643 --> 00:18:33,347
[CROW AS JAMES MASON]
I WANT TO TAKE US DOWN
TO 20,000 LEAGUES.

460
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:35,815
MEANWHILE,
IN YOUNG BILLY'S BATHTUB.

461
00:18:35,848 --> 00:18:37,783
YEAH, BILLY BATHTUB.
WHAT A TERRIBLE MOVIE.

462
00:18:37,818 --> 00:18:39,720
NO NO, NO, CROW.

463
00:18:39,753 --> 00:18:41,788
CHECK IT OUT,
THERE ARE FISH OUT THERE!

464
00:18:41,822 --> 00:18:44,257
SEE.

465
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:47,627
HEY, THEY GOT
♪ A GENIE AUTOMATIC
GARAGE DOOR ♪

466
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,428
- ♪ PICKER-UPPER ♪
- THAT'S A SWISS-ARMY JOKE.

467
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:52,867
SORRY.

468
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,702
THEY'RE IN THE TUNNEL.

469
00:18:54,735 --> 00:18:57,270
BRING THEM UP
TO THE ATLANTIC SEA.

470
00:18:57,303 --> 00:19:00,873
DO YOU THINK
I'M LOSING WEIGHT, SIR?

471
00:19:00,907 --> 00:19:02,408
[SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

472
00:19:02,442 --> 00:19:03,810
WHEN IN CORAL GABLES,
FLORIDA,

473
00:19:03,843 --> 00:19:07,513
VISIT CRASH CORRIGAN COVE.

474
00:19:07,547 --> 00:19:09,282
WE'RE AT THE SURFACE.
I CAN SEE LAND.

475
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:10,450
CAPTAIN BILLY.

476
00:19:10,483 --> 00:19:12,385
IMPOSSIBLE! ACCORDING
TO THE DEPTH INDICATOR,

477
00:19:12,418 --> 00:19:14,053
WE'RE STILL SOME
10,000 FEET DOWN.

478
00:19:14,087 --> 00:19:16,088
YOU KNOW, I THINK THEY GIVE
THAT KID TOO MUCH FREEDOM.

479
00:19:16,122 --> 00:19:17,290
THAT'S LAND, ALL RIGHT.

480
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:18,525
WE'RE MOVING INTO A SMALL--

481
00:19:18,558 --> 00:19:20,627
YEP, THAT'S LAND.
I'VE SEEN IT BEFORE.

482
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,662
YEP, DEFINITELY.

483
00:19:22,695 --> 00:19:24,197
WAIT A MINUTE.
I THINK WE'RE ON

484
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:27,633
THE PIRATES
OF THE CARIBBEAN RIDE.

485
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:30,170
- BIG SUB.
- GEE, WE'RE ON THE SURFACE.

486
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,410
I KNEW COLONEL KURTZ
WAS CLOSE.

487
00:19:36,443 --> 00:19:38,145
HE WAS REAL CLOSE.

488
00:19:38,178 --> 00:19:42,482
HE KNOWS SCOTTY.

489
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:46,220
[ALL GUFFAW]

490
00:19:46,253 --> 00:19:47,787
[SERVO RASPBERRIES]

491
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:49,723
--OUT THE IMPERIAL GUARDS,

492
00:19:49,757 --> 00:19:51,558
AND KILL THE DORKY GUY!
I HATE COMIC RELIEF.

493
00:19:51,592 --> 00:19:53,493
- [SIREN BEEPS]
- IS THAT YOUR BEEPER?

494
00:19:53,527 --> 00:19:54,962
- NOPE.
- THAT'S NOT ME,
I DON'T THINK.

495
00:19:54,995 --> 00:19:57,430
OH.

496
00:19:57,463 --> 00:19:59,132
I COMMAND THAT
HIS SUPREME MAJESTY

497
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:00,400
- UNGA KHAN--
- WHO'S HE LOOKING AT?

498
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:01,735
--A DETACHMENT
OF THE IMPERIAL GUARD

499
00:20:01,768 --> 00:20:03,537
WILL PROCEED AT ONCE
TO THE INLAND SEA

500
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:06,273
AND CAPTURE THE STRANGER
FROM THE UPPER WORLD.

501
00:20:06,307 --> 00:20:07,607
PUT YOUR SKIRT DOWN.

502
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:09,308
--MY HORSE, QUICKLY!

503
00:20:09,342 --> 00:20:10,877
NUMBER ONE PATROL, NOW.

504
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:12,812
NUMBER ONE PATROL,
PREPARE TO MOVE OUT.

505
00:20:12,845 --> 00:20:14,147
THAT'S US, BOYS.
COME ON! IT'S TIME

506
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:15,315
FOR THE BIG
HAWAIIAN NUMBER.

507
00:20:15,348 --> 00:20:16,483
HEY! COME ON, EVERYBODY!

508
00:20:16,517 --> 00:20:18,852
WHOO.

509
00:20:18,885 --> 00:20:20,753
HEY, IT'S THE PODEROSA
UNDER THE SEA.

510
00:20:20,787 --> 00:20:22,990
YOU KNOW WHAT? I THINK
THAT'S A MATTE PAINTING.

511
00:20:23,023 --> 00:20:25,792
- CHECK IT-- YOU SEE?
- YEAH.

512
00:20:25,825 --> 00:20:28,762
WE NOW JOIN FITZCARRALDO,
ALREADY IN PROGRESS.

513
00:20:28,795 --> 00:20:30,463
[MEN SCREAM]

514
00:20:30,497 --> 00:20:32,632
OOH. THEY RUNNING OVER
SOMEBODY?

515
00:20:32,665 --> 00:20:34,300
YEE-HAH!

516
00:20:34,333 --> 00:20:35,968
THIS LOOKS LIKE
A FINE PLACE TO SET DOWN

517
00:20:36,002 --> 00:20:37,403
MY PASTY WHITE BOTTOM.

518
00:20:37,437 --> 00:20:39,438
WELL, THEY'RE CERTAINLY
WELL-DRESSED FOR ADVENTURE.

519
00:20:39,472 --> 00:20:41,608
- MM-HMM.
- HERE WE ARE, 10,000 FEET

520
00:20:41,642 --> 00:20:43,877
- BELOW SEA LEVEL.
- AND ME WITHOUT MY RUBBERS.

521
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:47,080
--IN ANOTHER WORLD.

522
00:20:47,113 --> 00:20:48,682
HEY, HE'S BEING FOLLOWED
BY MICHAEL NESMITH.

523
00:20:48,715 --> 00:20:52,618
HEY, DID YOU KNOW
MY MOM INVENTED LIQUID PAPER?

524
00:20:52,652 --> 00:20:54,587
- [PARROT SQUAWKS]
- TOOKIE! TOOKIE!

525
00:20:54,622 --> 00:20:56,122
YOU'D BETTER
SUBMERGE THE SUBMARINE

526
00:20:56,155 --> 00:20:58,225
WHILE WE INVESTIGATE
THIS PLACE.

527
00:20:58,258 --> 00:20:59,927
ALL RIGHT.

528
00:21:03,163 --> 00:21:05,298
HEY, DID YOU REMEMBER
TO CLOSE THE HATCH?

529
00:21:05,332 --> 00:21:07,433
- D'OH!
- OH!

530
00:21:07,467 --> 00:21:09,068
WELL, REMEMBER WHERE
WE PARKED, EVERYONE.

531
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:11,237
- WE'RE IN THE GIRAFFE LOT.
- WE HAVE TO HIDE
THE CONTROL BOX.

532
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,540
- UP THERE'S A GOOD PLACE.
- YES, THAT'LL DO.

533
00:21:13,573 --> 00:21:16,175
DO YOU THINK WE'D BETTER WAIT
FOR BRINEY AND SALTY?

534
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,910
BRINEY AND SALTY?
THE PRETZEL TWINS!

535
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:21,213
--SINBAD THE PARROT.

536
00:21:21,247 --> 00:21:23,217
HI, EVERYBODY.
HERE'S WHERE THOSE TWO ROADS

537
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:25,452
DIVERGE INTO A YELLOW WOOD!

538
00:21:25,485 --> 00:21:27,920
TAKE THE ONE LESS TRAVELED.

539
00:21:30,023 --> 00:21:31,658
THAT IS ONE SWEET CHARIOT.

540
00:21:31,692 --> 00:21:34,193
SHIRLEY MacLAINE.

541
00:21:34,227 --> 00:21:37,430
- NO, WE ARE LOST, R2.
- [CROW AND JOEL WHISTLE]

542
00:21:39,165 --> 00:21:41,768
OWIE! OW-OW-OW-OUCH!...

543
00:21:41,802 --> 00:21:44,237
SHOULDN'T THEY BE RIDING
SIDE-SADDLE IN THOSE SKIRTS?

544
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:47,473
SOME OF THEM ARE.

545
00:21:47,507 --> 00:21:49,943
- [SERVO WHISTLES]
- NO, YOU GO THAT WAY.

546
00:21:49,977 --> 00:21:51,845
YOU'LL BE BREAKING DOWN
IN NO TIME.

547
00:21:51,878 --> 00:21:54,715
[SERVO WHISTLES]

548
00:21:54,748 --> 00:21:56,583
HEY, IT'S THE 34 HORSEMEN
OF THE APOCALYPSE.

549
00:21:56,617 --> 00:21:58,452
OW. OW OW OW. OW OW.

550
00:21:58,485 --> 00:22:00,787
OUCH, THAT BURNS, OUCH.

551
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:03,557
HEY, CHECK IT OUT. IT SAYS,
"BILL SHATNER WAS HERE."

552
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:06,225
GREAT. THEY'RE LETTING
JAY NORTH LEAD THE PACK HERE.

553
00:22:06,258 --> 00:22:08,895
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

554
00:22:08,928 --> 00:22:11,732
- LOOK, DAD.
- HOW COME THEY ALL TURNED
WHEN HE SAID "DAD?"

555
00:22:11,765 --> 00:22:13,567
UNLESS MY CALCULATIONS
ARE WRONG,

556
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:15,668
WE'VE COME ACROSS
THE LOST CONTINENT OF ATLANTIS.

557
00:22:15,702 --> 00:22:18,105
I'D SAY YOUR CALCULATIONS
ARE WRONG.

558
00:22:18,138 --> 00:22:19,773
IT MUST BE A MIRAGE.

559
00:22:19,807 --> 00:22:21,875
NO, THE MIRAGE
IS ON THE STRIP.

560
00:22:21,908 --> 00:22:24,077
LISTEN.

561
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:25,312
AND AROUND
THE CLUBHOUSE TURN,

562
00:22:25,345 --> 00:22:26,880
IT'S APARTMENT HOUSE
WITH PLENTY OF ROOM

563
00:22:26,913 --> 00:22:30,883
WITH BIRD DROPPINGS ON THE RAIL
COMING AROUND THE BEND.

564
00:22:30,917 --> 00:22:32,618
UH, LOOK, THIS IS WHAT STARTS
THOSE CHAIN ACCIDENTS.

565
00:22:32,652 --> 00:22:34,020
THAT'S NO ILLUSION--

566
00:22:34,053 --> 00:22:37,623
IT'S A WORLD OF ILLUSION.

567
00:22:37,657 --> 00:22:40,160
LOOK! SOLDIERS.

568
00:22:41,828 --> 00:22:44,630
WAIT THERE! WE'RE COMING
TO ATTACK YOU!

569
00:22:44,663 --> 00:22:46,467
JUST KEEP OUT OF SIGHT.

570
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,435
LET'S FIND OUT IF
THEY'RE FRIENDS OR ENEMIES.

571
00:22:48,468 --> 00:22:50,503
IF THEY KILL ME,
THEY'RE PROBABLY ENEMIES.

572
00:22:55,442 --> 00:22:57,043
UH, TAXI, I SAY--

573
00:22:57,077 --> 00:22:59,678
- TAXI!
- HEY!

574
00:23:02,782 --> 00:23:04,550
AFTER 'EM!

575
00:23:04,583 --> 00:23:06,420
AAH. HE'S A REAL DIPLOMAT.

576
00:23:08,822 --> 00:23:10,757
[SERVO HUMS]

577
00:23:10,790 --> 00:23:14,527
GET HIM, GIRLS.
HE HIT BUDDY!

578
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:17,097
[SERVO GRUNTS, STRAINS]

579
00:23:18,965 --> 00:23:22,068
HEY, GET THIS. I CAN SEE UP
TRENT'S SKIRT FROM HERE.

580
00:23:22,102 --> 00:23:25,138
OKAY. HAND ME UP THAT HORSE.

581
00:23:29,708 --> 00:23:31,612
UH-OH.

582
00:23:31,645 --> 00:23:34,547
I GOT A CRAZY IDEA,
BUT IT JUST MIGHT WORK!

583
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:37,350
NO WAY THEY'RE GONNA
PANTS ME AND MAKE ME-- AAH!

584
00:23:39,618 --> 00:23:41,822
WHOO.

585
00:23:41,855 --> 00:23:44,190
WELL, I NEVER
RID A HORSEY BEFORE.

586
00:23:44,223 --> 00:23:45,758
HE'S ESCAPED.

587
00:23:45,792 --> 00:23:47,093
SEND OUT THE JUGGERNAUT!

588
00:23:47,127 --> 00:23:49,930
'NUFF SAID. LIVE TO SERVE.

589
00:23:49,963 --> 00:23:52,998
[ALL HUM]

590
00:23:58,672 --> 00:24:00,840
WAIT, WE NEED THAT HORSE!

591
00:24:00,873 --> 00:24:03,075
- IDIOT.
- YOU SURE FOOLED 'EM
THIS TIME, CRASH.

592
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:04,243
LET'S GET BACK
TO THE SUBMARINE.

593
00:24:04,277 --> 00:24:05,578
BUT THE SOLDIERS!
WHAT ABOUT THEM?

594
00:24:05,612 --> 00:24:07,080
I'LL TELL YOU LATER.
WE'VE NO TIME TO LOSE!

595
00:24:07,113 --> 00:24:10,183
- [ALL SCREAM]
- WELL, RIGHT ABOUT THAT TIME,

596
00:24:10,217 --> 00:24:13,353
THE BOYS DID A LITTLE BODY WORK
ON THE OLD GENERAL LEE.

597
00:24:14,387 --> 00:24:17,857
HOT-BLOODED,
CHECK IT AND-- HUH?

598
00:24:17,890 --> 00:24:20,627
[ALL HUM '60s BATMAN THEME]

599
00:24:23,630 --> 00:24:25,232
SOME SORT OF A WAR TANK.

600
00:24:25,265 --> 00:24:29,202
[ALL]
OH, I CAN SEE-- A WAR TANK?!

601
00:24:29,235 --> 00:24:31,337
EXCUSE ME, HAVE YOU SEEN
ANY EARTHLINGS?

602
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:33,673
- OH. OH.
- STEADY.

603
00:24:33,707 --> 00:24:35,842
- HOLD ME.
- STEADY.

604
00:24:35,875 --> 00:24:37,877
OKAY BOYS, DE-LOUSE THEM.

605
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,982
OOH, RIGHT IN THE NOSTRIL.

606
00:24:45,085 --> 00:24:46,520
[JOEL WHISPERS]
FISHER. FISHER.

607
00:24:46,553 --> 00:24:49,455
- THEY'RE NOT HUMAN!
- YEAH, WE NOTICED.

608
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,990
STOP. WAIT. COME BACK.

609
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:56,597
[CROW MIMICS PLANE CRASH]

610
00:24:56,630 --> 00:24:59,432
--THAT CREVICE.

611
00:24:59,465 --> 00:25:01,300
♪ I'M A LITTLE TEAPOT ♪

612
00:25:01,333 --> 00:25:02,735
♪ SHORT AND STOUT ♪

613
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,238
♪ THIS IS MY HANDLE ♪

614
00:25:06,272 --> 00:25:07,940
♪ THIS IS MY GUN ♪

615
00:25:07,973 --> 00:25:10,577
♪ ONE IS FOR POURING,
ONE IS FOR FUN ♪

616
00:25:10,610 --> 00:25:13,613
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
PRETTY GOOD.

617
00:25:13,647 --> 00:25:16,082
D'OH!

618
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:23,857
- SILLY STRING!
- [DIANA SCREAMS]

619
00:25:23,890 --> 00:25:26,258
GEE, LADY, SCREAM
IN SOMEONE ELSE'S EAR.

620
00:25:26,292 --> 00:25:27,960
- REALLY.
- EVERYBODY DOWN!

621
00:25:27,993 --> 00:25:29,028
YOU TWO GET
BEHIND THAT ROCK.

622
00:25:29,062 --> 00:25:31,030
COUNT OFF BY ONES, EVERYONE!

623
00:25:31,063 --> 00:25:34,333
[ALL]
ONE! ONE! ONE!

624
00:25:34,367 --> 00:25:35,735
HERE, BILLY.
YOU DRAW THEIR FIRE.

625
00:25:35,768 --> 00:25:37,637
- DIANE!
- OOH, THE STRANGERS HAVE

626
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:39,605
- ESCAPED THE VOLKITES--
- AH, I HATE WHEN THEY TALK

627
00:25:39,638 --> 00:25:40,973
DURING THE MOVIE.

628
00:25:41,007 --> 00:25:43,943
OH.

629
00:25:43,977 --> 00:25:46,278
HMM.

630
00:25:46,312 --> 00:25:47,613
[SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

631
00:25:47,647 --> 00:25:49,148
FAST!
THE INVISIBLE RAY GUN

632
00:25:49,182 --> 00:25:52,518
WILL SOON STOP THEM.

633
00:25:52,552 --> 00:25:54,020
IT'S NOT VERY INVISIBLE.

634
00:25:54,053 --> 00:25:57,857
I CAN SEE IT.

635
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,425
ALL RIGHT, BILLY,
WHEN I THROW YOU OFF HERE,

636
00:25:59,458 --> 00:26:01,027
FLAP YOUR ARMS LIKE CRAZY.

637
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:04,497
LAUNCH THE DISINTEGRATOR!

638
00:26:04,530 --> 00:26:07,467
G.E. WE BRING
GOOD THINGS TO DEATH.

639
00:26:14,407 --> 00:26:18,512
YOU KNOW, I LIKED MEG RYAN
IN THIS ROLE BETTER.

640
00:26:18,545 --> 00:26:20,413
WELP, THIS IS IT.
LOOKS LIKE I'M GONNA

641
00:26:20,447 --> 00:26:21,982
BE FORCED TO
PUSH YOU OFF, DAVIS.

642
00:26:22,015 --> 00:26:25,218
- --THE MOUNTAIN.
- HIT HIM IN THE MOUTH?

643
00:26:25,252 --> 00:26:27,187
OH NO, THEY'RE SHOOTING
HOT DOGS AT HIM.

644
00:26:27,220 --> 00:26:28,922
- [CROW LAUGHS]
- NO!

645
00:26:28,955 --> 00:26:30,457
HOLD THE MUSTARD
ON THAT ONE.

646
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:33,058
ADMIRAL,
DEPLOY THE CHEDDARWURST.

647
00:26:33,092 --> 00:26:35,228
OH NO!

648
00:26:35,262 --> 00:26:36,697
OOH.

649
00:26:49,342 --> 00:26:52,345
OH WOW.
BLINDSIDED BY ANOTHER SHORT.

650
00:26:52,378 --> 00:26:54,580
- ARE YOU GUYS OKAY?
- OH, DON'T WORRY, JOEL.

651
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,415
I'M FEELING
NO UNUSUAL EFFECTS FROM IT.

652
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:57,783
ISN'T THAT RIGHT, BILLY?

653
00:26:57,817 --> 00:26:59,685
[CROW AFFECTS VOICE]
THAT'S RIGHT, CROW.

654
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:02,222
THAT'S REALLY NICE, CROW.
THAT'S...

655
00:27:02,255 --> 00:27:04,290
YOU KNOW, JOEL,
FOR THE LIFE OF ME,

656
00:27:04,323 --> 00:27:07,127
I CAN'T UNDERSTAND
THE APPEAL OF THESE OLD SERIALS.

657
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:09,528
WELL, THAT'S NO BIG MYSTERY,
MY LITTLE FIREPLUG.

658
00:27:09,562 --> 00:27:12,432
YOU SEE, THEY ACTUALLY HAVE
KIND OF A HISTORIC QUALITY.

659
00:27:12,465 --> 00:27:14,133
YOU KNOW,
IF IT'S IN THE 1930'S,

660
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:16,535
AND YOU'RE INTERESTED
IN TAKING OVER THE WORLD,

661
00:27:16,568 --> 00:27:18,638
YOU GOTTA GET GUSSIED UP
TO BEAT THE BAND.

662
00:27:18,672 --> 00:27:19,972
HAH. NO KIDDING.

663
00:27:20,007 --> 00:27:22,075
JUST LOOK AT THE ELABORATELY
FLAMBOYANT COSTUMES

664
00:27:22,108 --> 00:27:24,077
THE BAD GUYS
WERE GADDING ABOUT IN.

665
00:27:24,110 --> 00:27:27,413
TOGAS. ELECTRIC HELMETS.
DANCE BELTS.

666
00:27:27,447 --> 00:27:30,117
- FASCIST UNDEROOS.
- RIGHT. RIGHT, EXACTLY.

667
00:27:30,150 --> 00:27:32,585
AND I THOUGHT IT'D BE FUN
AS A THOUGHT EXPERIMENT

668
00:27:32,618 --> 00:27:35,255
FOR YOU GUYS TO TELL ME
HOW YOU WOULD DRESS UP

669
00:27:35,288 --> 00:27:36,857
IF YOU WERE GONNA
TAKE OVER THE WORLD.

670
00:27:36,890 --> 00:27:39,058
HMM. OH, YOU KNOW,
I'D BRONZE MY SKIN,

671
00:27:39,092 --> 00:27:41,260
PUT ON 40 POUNDS,
AND DRESS LIKE BEA ARTHUR.

672
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:43,295
- SMART.
- I'D WEAR
A LONE RANGER MASK

673
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:45,332
AND A SWIMSUIT
MADE OF STRING CHEESE.

674
00:27:45,365 --> 00:27:46,833
GOOD IDEA,
VERY THOUGHTFUL.

675
00:27:46,867 --> 00:27:48,835
OKAY, UH...

676
00:27:48,868 --> 00:27:51,237
SAY YOU'VE GOT YOUR COSTUME.
WHAT WOULD YOUR CAPER BE?

677
00:27:51,270 --> 00:27:53,640
I MEAN, WHAT WOULD YOU DO
TO TAKE OVER THE WORLD?

678
00:27:53,673 --> 00:27:55,442
OH, I'D FREEZE
ALL THE WORLD'S OCEANS.

679
00:27:55,475 --> 00:27:57,143
BUT THEN I GUESS THAT MEANS

680
00:27:57,177 --> 00:27:58,578
I'D HAVE TO DRESS LIKE
DICK BUTTON.

681
00:27:58,612 --> 00:28:01,213
YEAH. I'D SEND CALIFORNIA
TUMBLING INTO THE OCEAN.

682
00:28:01,247 --> 00:28:02,682
THE ATLANTIC OCEAN.

683
00:28:02,715 --> 00:28:04,750
AFTER SHOWERING, TALC,
AND CHANGING INTO

684
00:28:04,783 --> 00:28:06,618
MY FRITO BANDITO COSTUME.

685
00:28:06,652 --> 00:28:08,220
- I SEE. WELL...
- NICE TOUCH.

686
00:28:08,253 --> 00:28:09,988
ONCE YOU'VE
TAKEN OVER THE WORLD,

687
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:11,758
- WHAT WOULD YOU DO THEN?
- OOH!

688
00:28:11,792 --> 00:28:13,158
I'D TURN ALL THOSE
WHO OPPOSE ME

689
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:14,860
INTO THE BOY
IN THE PLASTIC BUBBLE.

690
00:28:14,893 --> 00:28:16,195
FOR OBVIOUS REASONS.

691
00:28:16,228 --> 00:28:18,330
I'D DECLARE MARCH
"LIZA MONTH!"

692
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:19,532
[BOTS]
WHOO!

693
00:28:19,565 --> 00:28:21,300
WELL, IT'S FUN TO DREAM,
YOU KNOW.

694
00:28:21,333 --> 00:28:23,035
BUT YOU CAN BET THAT

695
00:28:23,068 --> 00:28:25,838
ANYBODY SERIOUSLY INTERESTED
IN WORLD DOMINATION

696
00:28:25,872 --> 00:28:28,742
IS GONNA END UP LOOKING
LIKE A REAL SNICKERDOODLE.

697
00:28:28,775 --> 00:28:30,477
WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

698
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:32,178
I'LL DEAL WITH YOU LATER.

699
00:28:32,212 --> 00:28:33,813
BACK TO THE DRILL, FRANK.

700
00:28:33,847 --> 00:28:36,215
YOU WILL BOW DOWN
BEFORE ME, SON OF JOR-EL.

701
00:28:36,248 --> 00:28:37,583
BOW DOWN.

702
00:28:45,858 --> 00:28:48,193
[ALL, WITH SCORE]
♪ OF THE GIANT LEECHES ♪

703
00:28:48,227 --> 00:28:51,630
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

704
00:28:51,663 --> 00:28:53,900
LOOKS LIKE
AN E.E. CUMMINGS BOOK COVER.

705
00:28:53,933 --> 00:28:56,535
YEAH.

706
00:28:58,438 --> 00:28:59,972
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

707
00:29:00,005 --> 00:29:02,242
TYPE SETTING
BY SMITH CORONA.

708
00:29:02,275 --> 00:29:03,643
[SERVO, WITH SCORE]
♪ ORIGINAL STORY ♪

709
00:29:03,677 --> 00:29:05,645
♪ AND SCREENPLAY
BY LEO GORDON ♪

710
00:29:05,678 --> 00:29:06,880
♪ LEO GORDON LEO GORDON ♪

711
00:29:06,913 --> 00:29:08,748
♪♪ [SERVO SCATS]

712
00:29:08,782 --> 00:29:11,450
OOH!

713
00:29:11,483 --> 00:29:13,385
NEAT, HUH?

714
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:15,087
WELL, I'LL HAVE
A DICK RUBIN.

715
00:29:15,122 --> 00:29:16,622
HOLD THE SAUERKRAUT.

716
00:29:16,655 --> 00:29:20,025
RYDER RENTS SOUND SERVICES.

717
00:29:20,058 --> 00:29:22,362
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

718
00:29:22,395 --> 00:29:24,830
LASZLO, ALSO BRINGING YOU
A FINE LINE OF COSMETICS

719
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:28,768
FOR AGING SOCIALITES
AND SOCIAL X-RAYS.

720
00:29:28,802 --> 00:29:30,203
- HEY!
- ROGER CORMAN!

721
00:29:30,237 --> 00:29:32,105
[ALL CHEER]

722
00:29:32,138 --> 00:29:34,207
- HUH?
- WONDER IF THEY'RE RELATED?

723
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:38,978
OH, NO.

724
00:29:39,012 --> 00:29:41,647
MM. A TITLE SEQUENCE
NAMED DESIRE.

725
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:44,350
STELLA!

726
00:29:46,218 --> 00:29:47,720
THEN FOLKS STARTED

727
00:29:47,753 --> 00:29:49,655
PAYING FOR THEIR GROCERIES
WITH OLD CARS.

728
00:29:49,688 --> 00:29:51,123
NOTHING YOU COULD
DO ABOUT IT.

729
00:29:51,157 --> 00:29:52,658
NOPE.

730
00:29:52,692 --> 00:29:54,993
THIS LOOKS THE RIGHT SIDE
OF THE WRONG SIDE OF THE TRACKS.

731
00:29:55,027 --> 00:29:57,630
MM-HMM.

732
00:29:57,663 --> 00:29:59,298
[ALL]
NORM!

733
00:29:59,332 --> 00:30:01,835
- [ALL LAUGH]
- NOW WAIT A MINUTE,
WAIT A MINUTE.

734
00:30:01,868 --> 00:30:03,637
THE HEE-HAW WRITING SESSION.

735
00:30:03,670 --> 00:30:05,938
SO I WAS THINKING LULU COULD
POP UP BEHIND SOME CORN!

736
00:30:05,972 --> 00:30:08,575
NOW THAT'S FUNNY!

737
00:30:08,608 --> 00:30:11,410
- LIZ!
- IS MORE!

738
00:30:11,443 --> 00:30:12,978
DO YOU HEAR ME, GIRL?

739
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:16,115
TELL LITTLE JERRY LEE
TO HOLD IT DOWN IN THERE.

740
00:30:17,783 --> 00:30:21,120
HEY. WHO'S THE NEW GIRL?

741
00:30:21,153 --> 00:30:22,455
LOLITA.

742
00:30:22,488 --> 00:30:24,557
WHAT DO YOU WANT NOW?

743
00:30:24,590 --> 00:30:26,292
ARE YOU THINKING
WHAT I'M THINKING?

744
00:30:26,325 --> 00:30:28,060
YEAH. CRABS.

745
00:30:28,093 --> 00:30:30,263
YOU GOTTA PLAY
THAT THING SO LOUD?

746
00:30:30,297 --> 00:30:34,000
WHAT'D YOU COME OUT
LIKE THIS FOR?

747
00:30:34,033 --> 00:30:36,668
- ORAL... HYGIENE.
- OH, DON'T BOSS ME.

748
00:30:36,702 --> 00:30:37,970
- LIZ?
- I WONDER IF THEY HAVE

749
00:30:38,003 --> 00:30:39,338
A BACK PORCH ON THAT PLACE.

750
00:30:39,372 --> 00:30:41,073
OOH.

751
00:30:41,107 --> 00:30:43,075
SOMEDAY I'M GONNA
GIVE THAT SHE-CAT

752
00:30:43,108 --> 00:30:44,577
THE WHOPPIN'
SHE'S BEEN ASKING FOR.

753
00:30:44,610 --> 00:30:46,212
[ALL]
BOO!

754
00:30:46,245 --> 00:30:47,947
--BRING THE LAW
DOWN TO HER.

755
00:30:47,980 --> 00:30:49,848
LET HER KNOW WHO WEARS
THE PANTS AROUND HERE.

756
00:30:49,882 --> 00:30:52,052
YEAH, AND WHO WEARS
THE STUPID-LOOKIN' HAT.

757
00:30:52,085 --> 00:30:53,587
BE BACK IN A MINUTE.

758
00:30:53,620 --> 00:30:56,355
THAT'S A GOOD ONE, EB.
I GOTTA GIVE YOU THAT ONE.

759
00:30:56,388 --> 00:30:59,392
--HE'S DONE BACK THERE,
I'LL...

760
00:30:59,425 --> 00:31:01,895
SHE'LL BE DOING IT.

761
00:31:01,928 --> 00:31:03,462
HA-HA, I SOILED MYSELF.

762
00:31:03,495 --> 00:31:05,232
GO ON, LEM, AND TELL US ABOUT
THAT THING YOU KILLED

763
00:31:05,265 --> 00:31:06,498
OUT THERE AT THE SWAMP.

764
00:31:06,532 --> 00:31:08,167
YEAH, LEM, LET'S HEAR
THE REST OF THAT.

765
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,535
MAYBE WE SHOULD HAVE
SUBTITLES FOR THIS.

766
00:31:09,568 --> 00:31:11,603
I PUT FIVE SLUGS

767
00:31:11,637 --> 00:31:13,472
INTO THAT CRITTER
BEFORE IT WENT UNDER.

768
00:31:13,505 --> 00:31:15,207
THEN I HAD
A FEW SLUGS MYSELF.

769
00:31:15,242 --> 00:31:17,177
AND THEN I WENT UNDER.

770
00:31:17,210 --> 00:31:19,012
--HAD REGULAR ARMS ON IT,
LIKE A MAN.

771
00:31:19,045 --> 00:31:20,347
BUT MADE FOR A WOMAN.

772
00:31:20,380 --> 00:31:22,148
SORT OF DIFFERENT LOOKIN'.

773
00:31:22,182 --> 00:31:23,683
HAD SUCKERS ON 'EM.

774
00:31:23,717 --> 00:31:25,285
TOOTSIE POP, I THINK.

775
00:31:25,318 --> 00:31:27,220
LIKE ONE OF THEM...

776
00:31:27,253 --> 00:31:29,322
LIKE ONE OF THEM
OCTOPUS THINGS.

777
00:31:29,355 --> 00:31:33,092
NO, THAT'S OCTOPI, ACTUALLY.

778
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:36,328
LEM, YOU SURE
THAT CRITTER WASN'T PINK?

779
00:31:36,362 --> 00:31:38,297
- SHUT UP, BRUCE.
- NO.

780
00:31:38,330 --> 00:31:41,067
I TOLD YOU BEFORE,
IT WAS SORT OF GRAY LOOKING.

781
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:43,068
WHAT, YOU GOTTA CHECK
WITH STRING BEAN TO LAUGH?

782
00:31:43,102 --> 00:31:45,037
WELL, LAUGH IF YOU WANT.

783
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,438
- HAH.
- BUT THAT THING

784
00:31:46,472 --> 00:31:48,742
WEREN'T NOTHING
NATURE PUT OUT THERE.

785
00:31:48,775 --> 00:31:50,510
NO, SIR.
AND IT WEREN'T

786
00:31:50,543 --> 00:31:52,178
NO FREAK GATOR NEITHER.

787
00:31:52,212 --> 00:31:54,113
MAYBE IT WAS THE ROCKET FUEL
YOU'VE BEEN DRINKING.

788
00:31:54,147 --> 00:31:55,548
--THIS COUNTRY FOR 40 YEARS,

789
00:31:55,582 --> 00:31:58,417
AND I AIN'T NEVER SEEN
NOTHING LIKE IT--

790
00:31:58,450 --> 00:31:59,752
THAT'S A DOUBLE-NEGATIVE.

791
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:01,053
--TOO BAD YOU DIDN'T
BRING IT BACK.

792
00:32:01,087 --> 00:32:02,722
STEVE BENTON'D
PROBABLY PAY A FAIR BOUNTY

793
00:32:02,755 --> 00:32:04,690
FOR WHATEVER IT WAS.

794
00:32:04,723 --> 00:32:08,027
BOUNTY? I WOULDN'T
TOUCH THAT CRITTER

795
00:32:08,060 --> 00:32:10,228
FOR ALL THE MONEY
EVER MADE.

796
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:12,132
- TEN BUCKS?
- AND IF YOU'D SEEN IT,

797
00:32:12,165 --> 00:32:13,498
YOU WOULDN'T NEITHER.

798
00:32:13,532 --> 00:32:15,402
YOU'D BETTER
TAKE IT EASY ON THE STUFF.

799
00:32:15,435 --> 00:32:16,668
YOU'RE LOOKING
KIND OF PINKERED.

800
00:32:16,702 --> 00:32:18,403
OH, THIS IS
AN INTERVENTION.

801
00:32:18,437 --> 00:32:20,038
SHUCKS, IT'S JUST
TOBACCO JUICE.

802
00:32:20,072 --> 00:32:22,642
--GONNA CLEAN MY OTTER LINES
OUT BEFORE MORNING.

803
00:32:22,675 --> 00:32:23,943
OH, NO NO,
NOT IN FRONT OF US, PLEASE.

804
00:32:23,977 --> 00:32:25,912
LEM, I THINK
THAT CRITTER'S A...

805
00:32:25,945 --> 00:32:27,813
GHOST OF ONE OF THOSE OTTERS
YOU'VE BEEN POACHING

806
00:32:27,847 --> 00:32:30,683
ALL THESE YEARS
COME BACK TO HAUNT YOU.

807
00:32:30,717 --> 00:32:32,418
OUR JOY GROWS, FRIEND.

808
00:32:32,452 --> 00:32:34,787
WELL, IF THAT'S SO,

809
00:32:34,820 --> 00:32:36,388
YOU FELLAS'LL

810
00:32:36,422 --> 00:32:39,558
SEE IT RIGHT QUICK
YOURSELVES.

811
00:32:39,592 --> 00:32:41,260
YEAH, THAT'S GREAT.
WHEN YOU GET NEAR A SENTENCE,

812
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:45,197
LET US KNOW.

813
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,765
DO YOU REALLY THINK
THIS LOITERING

814
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:50,703
IS GOOD FOR BUSINESS?

815
00:32:50,737 --> 00:32:54,340
THIS SITTIN' AROUND
PLUM WORE ME OUT.

816
00:32:54,373 --> 00:32:57,810
THE HOOVERVILLE SEVEN.

817
00:32:57,843 --> 00:33:01,780
I THINK SHE KNOWS
HOW TO SCRATCH AN ITCH.

818
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:04,617
ORDINARY PANTYHOSE
ARE OKAY UNDER FUNKY CLOTHES,

819
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:06,752
BUT GENTLEMEN PREFER HANES.

820
00:33:06,785 --> 00:33:09,588
HUH, PETE FOUNTAIN.

821
00:33:09,622 --> 00:33:12,225
[MEN IN OTHER ROOM LAUGH]

822
00:33:12,258 --> 00:33:16,195
QUIT WEARING MY THINGS.

823
00:33:16,228 --> 00:33:18,030
BOSS HOG, AFTER DARK.

824
00:33:18,063 --> 00:33:20,600
LOOK. IT'S NOT LIKE
I WANNA BE MEAN

825
00:33:20,633 --> 00:33:22,602
OR ANYTHING LIKE THAT,
LIZ BABY.

826
00:33:22,635 --> 00:33:24,503
I GOT A REPUTATION
AROUND HERE.

827
00:33:24,537 --> 00:33:26,038
AS A BIG, FAT,
INSENSITIVE GUY?

828
00:33:26,072 --> 00:33:27,373
THESE FOLKS HAVE NO RESPECT
FOR A MAN WHO LETS

829
00:33:27,407 --> 00:33:28,975
HIS WOMAN BOSS HIM.

830
00:33:29,008 --> 00:33:30,643
WELL, NEXT THING I KNOW,
THEY'LL BE LAUGHING AT ME.

831
00:33:30,677 --> 00:33:32,212
THEN I'D HAVE TO GO
ON A SHOOTING SPREE.

832
00:33:32,245 --> 00:33:33,578
--THE REST OF THEM--

833
00:33:33,612 --> 00:33:35,715
WON'T YOU PLEASE
LISTEN TO ME, LIZ BABY?

834
00:33:35,748 --> 00:33:37,383
[JOEL HUMS]

835
00:33:37,417 --> 00:33:39,552
- LIZ?
- I'M NOT HEARING YOU.

836
00:33:39,585 --> 00:33:41,353
♪ LA-LA-LA-LA
LA-LA-LA-LA ♪

837
00:33:41,387 --> 00:33:42,955
♪ HOT CHILD IN THE CITY ♪

838
00:33:42,988 --> 00:33:45,458
MY NAME'S NOT LIZ.
IT'S BLANCHE.

839
00:33:47,293 --> 00:33:49,695
HMM.

840
00:33:52,165 --> 00:33:53,933
OH, I LOVE IT
WHEN SHE PUTS IT ON THERE.

841
00:33:53,967 --> 00:33:56,868
I JUST LIKE THE SMELL.

842
00:33:56,902 --> 00:33:59,505
LIZ, HONEY, YOU THINK
YOU COULD LOSE SOME WEIGHT?

843
00:34:01,807 --> 00:34:04,143
YOU KNOW, SHE'S GONNA
SHORTEN THOSE CALF MUSCLES

844
00:34:04,177 --> 00:34:07,613
- WITH THOSE HEELS.
- YEP, YOU'RE RIGHT.

845
00:34:07,647 --> 00:34:10,650
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

846
00:34:10,683 --> 00:34:12,818
STOP LOOKING AT ME
LIKE THAT.

847
00:34:12,852 --> 00:34:15,387
I'LL LOOK AT YOU ANY WAY I WANT.
YOU'RE MY WIFE.

848
00:34:15,422 --> 00:34:16,922
MAN, I DO WONDER
WHAT IT'D BE LIKE

849
00:34:16,955 --> 00:34:19,192
TO MAKE LOVE TO YOU,
THOUGH.

850
00:34:19,225 --> 00:34:20,893
NO-- NO,
DON'T DO THAT, LADY!

851
00:34:20,927 --> 00:34:23,162
- OH--
- IT'S OKAY.

852
00:34:25,465 --> 00:34:26,698
OH, MOMMY!

853
00:34:26,732 --> 00:34:29,068
HONEY WEST!

854
00:34:29,102 --> 00:34:30,603
JOEL, I THOUGHT UNDERWEAR
WAS SUPPOSED TO MATCH.

855
00:34:30,637 --> 00:34:31,837
IT DOESN'T HAVE TO.

856
00:34:31,870 --> 00:34:33,405
--WHO DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE TALKING TO?

857
00:34:33,438 --> 00:34:35,207
"DON'T TOUCH ME?"
YOU'RE MY WIFE.

858
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:36,775
I'LL TOUCH YOU
ANY TIME I FEEL LIKE IT.

859
00:34:36,808 --> 00:34:39,878
HE MUST HAVE
A REALLY GOOD PERSONALITY.

860
00:34:39,912 --> 00:34:42,582
CAN I CALL YOU SOMETIME?

861
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:47,453
WHERE ARE YOU GOING?

862
00:34:47,487 --> 00:34:50,088
A FELLA NAMED HUMBERT HUMBERT
WANTS TO SEE ME.

863
00:34:50,122 --> 00:34:52,992
WHERE ARE YOU GOING?

864
00:34:53,025 --> 00:34:55,562
- I'M GOING OUT.
- TO CHURCH.

865
00:34:55,595 --> 00:34:57,430
MAYBE I'LL BE BACK.

866
00:34:57,463 --> 00:34:58,865
AND MAYBE I WON'T.

867
00:34:58,898 --> 00:35:00,933
- LIZ, BABY--
- DO I HAVE TO GUESS?

868
00:35:00,967 --> 00:35:03,268
DO I GET A PRIZE IF-- I--

869
00:35:03,302 --> 00:35:05,805
CAN I EAT YOUR DINNER THEN?

870
00:35:05,838 --> 00:35:08,407
SHOULDN'T'VE MARRIED HER,
KNOWING THAT SHE LOATHED ME.

871
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:10,843
HEY.

872
00:35:15,782 --> 00:35:19,452
HOW COME WE'RE NOT MOVING?

873
00:35:19,485 --> 00:35:21,687
[ALL GRUNT, STRAIN]

874
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:24,790
OKAY, ALL DONE.

875
00:35:24,823 --> 00:35:27,227
HEY, IT'S JIM FROM
WILD KINGDOM.

876
00:35:30,228 --> 00:35:31,863
WELL, THERE WAS THE YOUNG ONE
IN THAT LAST TRAP.

877
00:35:31,897 --> 00:35:33,665
- I HAD TO KILL IT.
- OH, POOR THING.

878
00:35:33,698 --> 00:35:34,933
YEAH, BOO-HOO.

879
00:35:34,967 --> 00:35:36,335
TOLD YOU
YOU SHOULDN'T'VE COME ALONG.

880
00:35:36,368 --> 00:35:39,072
SO, LET'S HAVE SOME KIDS.

881
00:35:39,105 --> 00:35:41,907
BUT I LOVE SITTING IN
THE SMELLY PICKUP TRUCK.

882
00:35:41,940 --> 00:35:43,542
I CAN UNDERSTAND
HUNTING AN ANIMAL,

883
00:35:43,575 --> 00:35:46,845
BUT MAKING IT SUFFER
IN THOSE TRAPS.

884
00:35:46,878 --> 00:35:48,613
HEY, I SUFFER IN
THE TRAP OF LOVE.

885
00:35:48,647 --> 00:35:50,482
POACHERS KNOW THE SWAMP
LIKE THE BACKS OF THEIR HANDS.

886
00:35:50,517 --> 00:35:52,685
BUT I'LL CATCH ONE OF THEM
IN THE ACT SOME NIGHT

887
00:35:52,718 --> 00:35:54,120
AND PUT HIM AWAY
FOR SIX MONTHS.

888
00:35:54,153 --> 00:35:55,588
- MY, HE'S RUGGED.
- IN THE MEANTIME,

889
00:35:55,622 --> 00:35:57,757
I'LL HAVE TO BE SATISFIED
CONFISCATING THEIR TRAP LINES.

890
00:35:57,790 --> 00:35:59,425
- THAT'S REWARD ENOUGH.
- THERE'S ENOUGH TRAPS,

891
00:35:59,458 --> 00:36:00,727
IT WON'T PAY 'EM
TO KEEP TRYING.

892
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,195
BE CAREFUL, DARLING.

893
00:36:02,228 --> 00:36:04,297
THESE PEOPLE AREN'T
LIKE OTHER FOLKS.

894
00:36:04,330 --> 00:36:05,765
YOU KNOW, THEY'LL TRY
AND GET BACK AT YOU.

895
00:36:05,798 --> 00:36:07,933
AND THEY'VE GOT
SEVEN TOES ON EACH FOOT.

896
00:36:07,967 --> 00:36:09,902
STEVE,
YOU'RE A STRANGER HERE.

897
00:36:09,935 --> 00:36:12,205
THEY'VE LIVED THIS WAY
FOR GENERATIONS.

898
00:36:12,238 --> 00:36:14,040
ONE MAN ISN'T GOING
TO CHANGE THEM OVERNIGHT.

899
00:36:14,073 --> 00:36:15,507
YEAH, THEY GOTTA
WANT TO CHANGE.

900
00:36:15,542 --> 00:36:18,110
--A REAL WORRYWART.
- WELL, I'M SERIOUS, STEVE.

901
00:36:18,143 --> 00:36:19,545
THEY CAN BE DANGEROUS.

902
00:36:19,578 --> 00:36:22,147
OKAY. I'LL BE CAREFUL.

903
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:23,748
YOU JUST STOP WORRYING.

904
00:36:23,782 --> 00:36:25,585
UH-HUH.

905
00:36:25,618 --> 00:36:27,253
OH, HE'S THE KILLER LEECH.

906
00:36:27,287 --> 00:36:30,388
NO, "LECH." IT'S THE ATTACK
OF THE KILLER LECH.

907
00:36:30,422 --> 00:36:32,858
OH, STEVE, I LOVE YOU.

908
00:36:32,892 --> 00:36:34,793
I LOVE YOU SO MUCH.

909
00:36:34,827 --> 00:36:37,430
♪ I DON'T KNOW HOW TO-- ♪

910
00:36:37,463 --> 00:36:38,830
♪♪ [MUFFLED]

911
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:41,200
- [DISTANT SCREAM]
- WHAT WAS THAT?

912
00:36:41,233 --> 00:36:44,003
I DON'T KNOW. YOU GET IN
THAT TRUCK AND LOCK IT UP.

913
00:36:44,037 --> 00:36:45,303
SOUNDED LIKE HEE HAW.

914
00:36:45,337 --> 00:36:48,440
COULD YOU LEAVE
THE MAD DOG HERE?

915
00:36:48,473 --> 00:36:50,877
SHE DRESSED PRETTY FORMALLY
FOR A LEECH HUNT.

916
00:36:50,910 --> 00:36:53,345
MM-HMM.

917
00:36:53,378 --> 00:36:55,815
[WOMAN SCREAMS]

918
00:36:55,848 --> 00:36:59,285
OH, RICKY, WE WERE
JUST PLAYING A LITTLE GAME.

919
00:37:03,122 --> 00:37:06,125
OH! THANKS FOR
COMFORTING ME WITH A GUN.

920
00:37:10,963 --> 00:37:12,732
OH, HE'S A MESS.

921
00:37:12,765 --> 00:37:14,933
A CHOCOLATE MESS.

922
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:24,877
MM. BREAKFAST BEANS.

923
00:37:24,910 --> 00:37:27,045
OH, THIS GUY'S
THE SHERIFF OF EVERYTHING.

924
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:29,615
--RULED THAT SAWYER DIED
IN A MISADVENTURE.

925
00:37:29,648 --> 00:37:31,183
NOW, AS FAR AS
THIS OFFICE IS CONCERNED,

926
00:37:31,217 --> 00:37:33,252
- THAT'S THE END OF IT.
- THAT'S A COMMON CAUSE
OF DEATH.

927
00:37:33,285 --> 00:37:35,722
LOOK, IF LEM WAS KILLED
BY ANYTHING HUMAN,

928
00:37:35,755 --> 00:37:37,657
I WOULDN'T NEED YOU
TO TELL ME MY JOB.

929
00:37:37,690 --> 00:37:39,425
AH, SHUT UP
AND FINISH YOUR KABOOM.

930
00:37:39,458 --> 00:37:42,060
--STOMPIN' THROUGH THE SWAMP,
LOOKING FOR AN OVERGROWN GATOR.

931
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:43,462
WHAT DO I LOOK LIKE, A COP?

932
00:37:43,495 --> 00:37:44,997
SAWYER WASN'T KILLED
BY AN ALLIGATOR.

933
00:37:45,030 --> 00:37:46,132
IS THAT SO?

934
00:37:46,165 --> 00:37:47,667
DID YOU HEAR THAT, MORTON?

935
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:51,037
GAME WARDEN BENTON SAYS
THAT WASN'T A GATOR KILLED LEM.

936
00:37:51,070 --> 00:37:52,372
WELL THEN, WHAT WAS IT?

937
00:37:52,405 --> 00:37:53,872
YOU KNOW SO MUCH,
GO ON, TELL ME.

938
00:37:53,905 --> 00:37:55,775
- WHAT KILLED HIM?
- IT WAS LOW-LEVEL STRESS, TROY.

939
00:37:55,808 --> 00:37:57,510
--DEFENSIVE WOUNDS
WERE THE KIND A SQUID

940
00:37:57,543 --> 00:37:59,312
OR A LARGE OCTOPUS
MIGHT CAUSE.

941
00:37:59,345 --> 00:38:00,813
- I LOVE SQUID!
- OH, SURE.

942
00:38:00,847 --> 00:38:03,482
AND DID GREYSON EXPLAIN
HOW A SALT WATER CREATURE

943
00:38:03,515 --> 00:38:06,752
HAPPENED TO BE 30 MILES INLAND
LIVING IN CLEAR WATER?

944
00:38:06,785 --> 00:38:08,220
STRANGER THINGS
HAVE HAPPENED, I KNOW--

945
00:38:08,253 --> 00:38:10,957
LOOK HERE, BENTON.
YOU WORK FOR THE STATE.

946
00:38:10,990 --> 00:38:12,458
- THE STATE OF CONFUSION.
- NOW, WHY DON'T YOU

947
00:38:12,492 --> 00:38:14,093
KEEP YOUR NOSE
OUT OF COUNTY BUSINESS?

948
00:38:14,127 --> 00:38:17,128
IS THAT CLEAR ENOUGH
FOR YOU?

949
00:38:17,162 --> 00:38:18,998
AH, GO SOAK YOUR FAT HEAD.

950
00:38:19,032 --> 00:38:21,067
OKAY THEN. WELL,
I'LL GO GET SOME SOAP AND--

951
00:38:21,100 --> 00:38:22,502
HEY! WAIT A MINUTE.

952
00:38:22,535 --> 00:38:23,768
WHAT WAS THAT YOU SAID?

953
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:25,772
I SAID,
"GO SOAK YOUR FAT HEAD."

954
00:38:25,805 --> 00:38:27,607
IS THAT EXACTLY
HOW YOU PHRASED IT?

955
00:38:27,640 --> 00:38:31,177
WASN'T THERE MORE
OF A LILTING QUALITY-- AH.

956
00:38:31,210 --> 00:38:33,312
BOY, IF I WASN'T
SO STUCK WITH--

957
00:38:33,345 --> 00:38:35,547
BOY'S LOOKING
FOR BAD TROUBLE.

958
00:38:35,580 --> 00:38:36,882
AND HE'S SURE GONNA GET IT.

959
00:38:36,915 --> 00:38:38,150
[SERVO BELCHES]

960
00:38:38,183 --> 00:38:39,618
YOU CAN BET ON THAT.

961
00:38:39,652 --> 00:38:42,355
I THOUGHT
IT WAS FUNNY, SHERIFF.

962
00:38:42,388 --> 00:38:43,688
GARY BUSEY,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

963
00:38:43,722 --> 00:38:45,958
GARY BUSEY.

964
00:38:45,992 --> 00:38:47,693
LOOK, I SNEEZED
ON MY DICTIONARY.

965
00:38:47,727 --> 00:38:49,962
SO YOU SEE, THE OCTOPI
USES ITS SUCTION DISCS

966
00:38:49,995 --> 00:38:51,363
TO HOLD ITS PREY--

967
00:38:51,397 --> 00:38:52,698
LIKE I HOLD A SANDWICH.

968
00:38:52,732 --> 00:38:54,600
--THIS WILL NOT
INFLICT A WOUND.

969
00:38:54,633 --> 00:38:56,335
SAME IS TRUE OF THE SQUID.

970
00:38:56,368 --> 00:38:58,537
NOW BOTH CREATURES HAVE
A PARROT-LIKE BEAK

971
00:38:58,570 --> 00:39:01,473
AS THEIR PRIMARY OFFENSIVE
AND DEFENSIVE WEAPON.

972
00:39:01,507 --> 00:39:02,942
WELL, MAYBE THE SHERIFF
WAS RIGHT, DAD.

973
00:39:02,975 --> 00:39:04,877
I THINK I KNOW
WHERE THE DRAPES WENT.

974
00:39:04,910 --> 00:39:07,647
IT COULD BE A FREAK
OR A MALFORMED ALLIGATOR.

975
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:08,947
THANKS FOR THE COFFEE,
MRS.--

976
00:39:08,980 --> 00:39:12,752
NO. NO,
I'M AFRAID IT WASN'T.

977
00:39:12,785 --> 00:39:14,553
WELL, WHERE DOES THAT
LEAVE US, DOC?

978
00:39:14,587 --> 00:39:17,457
- IN THE LIVING ROOM.
- WISH I KNEW.

979
00:39:17,490 --> 00:39:19,023
YOU KNOW, I'M BEGINNING
TO THINK LEM WAS

980
00:39:19,058 --> 00:39:21,360
TELLING THE TRUTH
IN WALTER'S STORE.

981
00:39:21,393 --> 00:39:23,995
HE DID SEE SOMETHING
THAT NIGHT.

982
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,732
SOMETHING THAT HAD
INTELLIGENCE ENOUGH

983
00:39:25,765 --> 00:39:27,700
TO SEEK HIM OUT
AND DESTROY HIM LATER.

984
00:39:27,733 --> 00:39:29,033
- THAT WAS SMART.
- SAWYER CLAIMS

985
00:39:29,068 --> 00:39:30,302
TO HAVE KILLED
THE THING HE SAW.

986
00:39:30,335 --> 00:39:32,705
PUT A HALF A DOZEN
RIFLE BULLETS INTO IT.

987
00:39:32,738 --> 00:39:34,773
I'VE SEEN
THAT OLD .44-40 HE USED.

988
00:39:34,807 --> 00:39:36,775
NOTHING COULD LIVE AFTER
BEING HIT WITH THOSE SLUGS.

989
00:39:36,808 --> 00:39:39,112
ONLY HALF A CUP?
DON'T I LIKE MY COFFEE?

990
00:39:39,145 --> 00:39:42,415
CONCEDING THE POSSIBILITY
OF ONE SUCH CREATURE,

991
00:39:42,448 --> 00:39:45,317
WE MUST ALSO CONCEDE
THE POSSIBILITY OF OTHERS.

992
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:47,987
OH, SORRY, YOU LOST ME.
YOU KNOW, THIS COFFEE'S
WONDERFUL.

993
00:39:48,020 --> 00:39:49,888
--ONE SURE WAY
OF FINDING OUT.

994
00:39:49,922 --> 00:39:51,790
GO IN AND SEARCH
EVERY BACKWATER CHANNEL

995
00:39:51,823 --> 00:39:54,260
- AND WET SPOT IN THE SWAMP.
- ANY VOLUNTEERS?

996
00:39:54,293 --> 00:39:55,627
IF IT'S THERE, I'LL FIND IT.

997
00:39:55,660 --> 00:39:57,095
IT ALL POINTS
TO ONE THING, DRAKE.

998
00:39:57,128 --> 00:40:01,033
THIS COFFEE'S GRAND.

999
00:40:01,067 --> 00:40:03,568
♪ FROM THE LAND
OF SKY-BLUE WATERS ♪

1000
00:40:03,602 --> 00:40:05,872
[JOEL AND CROW]
♪ WATER ♪

1001
00:40:09,142 --> 00:40:10,910
AH, HECK, HONEY.
I GOT A MOTOR ON THIS THING.

1002
00:40:10,943 --> 00:40:14,045
I JUST REMEMBERED.

1003
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:16,515
HMM, DO YOU KNOW
ANY OTHER CAMP SONGS?

1004
00:40:16,548 --> 00:40:19,352
UH, LET'S SEE.
"BARNACLE BILL?"

1005
00:40:19,385 --> 00:40:21,387
YEAH, WHATEVER YOU DO,
DON'T HELP ME PADDLE,

1006
00:40:21,420 --> 00:40:23,655
MS. DEAD WEIGHT.

1007
00:40:23,688 --> 00:40:27,425
WELL, YOU KNOW,
A VISOR MIGHT'VE BEEN HELPFUL.

1008
00:40:27,460 --> 00:40:28,927
OH, IT'S A SWAMPER.

1009
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:31,297
SHOULD WE BRING
OUR EVIL IN HERE?

1010
00:40:38,437 --> 00:40:41,707
[SERVO AS HEPBURN]
CHARLIE, THERE'S LEECHES
ALL OVER YOUR BACK.

1011
00:40:41,740 --> 00:40:44,777
SURE IS QUIET AROUND HERE.

1012
00:40:44,810 --> 00:40:48,780
WHAT, IS SHE ON HER LUNCH BREAK
FROM WENDY'S?

1013
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:51,483
♪ THE WRECK OF
THE EDMUND FITZGERALD ♪

1014
00:40:51,517 --> 00:40:54,853
♪♪ [BOTS HUM]

1015
00:40:54,887 --> 00:40:57,155
HERE, LEECHY-LEECHY-
LEECHY-LEECHY.

1016
00:40:57,188 --> 00:41:01,193
COME ON, NICE LEECHY-LEECHY-
LEECHY-LEECHY-LEECHY.

1017
00:41:01,227 --> 00:41:02,562
WELL, I'LL TELL YOU
ONE THING RIGHT NOW.

1018
00:41:02,595 --> 00:41:05,130
I AM NOT GOING
TO PORTAGE THIS THING.

1019
00:41:05,163 --> 00:41:06,365
YOU KNOW,
MAYBE THIS ISN'T

1020
00:41:06,398 --> 00:41:07,667
THE RIGHT TIME
TO TALK ABOUT THIS,

1021
00:41:07,700 --> 00:41:09,067
BUT I LOVE MUFFINS,
YOU KNOW?

1022
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:12,103
THOSE REAL FANCY
NUT AND FRUIT MUFFINS THEY GOT?

1023
00:41:12,137 --> 00:41:13,705
FULL OF WHOLE GRAINS--

1024
00:41:13,738 --> 00:41:15,673
KERMIT, NO!

1025
00:41:15,707 --> 00:41:17,375
THE HECK?

1026
00:41:17,408 --> 00:41:18,877
- DID YOU HEAR SOMETHING?
- YES.

1027
00:41:18,910 --> 00:41:21,080
I HEARD YOU SAY,
"DID YOU HEAR SOMETHING."

1028
00:41:24,350 --> 00:41:26,118
WELL, WHATEVER IT WAS,
IT'S NOT HERE ANYMORE.

1029
00:41:26,152 --> 00:41:29,888
EH, PROBABLY
OVER THE STATE LINE BY NOW.

1030
00:41:29,922 --> 00:41:31,923
BE QUIET.
PHIL HARRIS AND CURT GOWDY

1031
00:41:31,957 --> 00:41:33,625
ARE DUCK-HUNTING BACK THERE.

1032
00:41:33,658 --> 00:41:35,127
DID YOU WANT SOME COFFEE?

1033
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:36,362
- AGAIN WITH THE COFFEE.
- OH, THANKS, HON.

1034
00:41:36,395 --> 00:41:40,298
WELL, IT IS
VERY GOOD COFFEE.

1035
00:41:40,332 --> 00:41:42,802
AN ARMY COULD HIDE IN HERE
AND NEVER BE NOTICED.

1036
00:41:42,835 --> 00:41:45,770
- NO ONE DID.
- WHAT?

1037
00:41:45,803 --> 00:41:47,707
THE SEMINOLES
UNDER OSCEOLA IN THE 1830'S.

1038
00:41:47,740 --> 00:41:49,208
AH GEE, I WAS JUST
TRYING TO BREAK THE ICE.

1039
00:41:49,242 --> 00:41:50,508
I DON'T NEED
A HISTORY LESSON.

1040
00:41:50,542 --> 00:41:52,043
--TO ROUND 'EM UP.
- I REMEMBER

1041
00:41:52,077 --> 00:41:54,112
READING ABOUT OSCEOLA
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

1042
00:41:54,145 --> 00:41:56,782
YEAH, THOSE SEMINOLES.
BOY, THEY DRINK A LOT OF COFFEE.

1043
00:41:56,815 --> 00:41:58,150
MM-HMM.

1044
00:41:58,183 --> 00:42:01,053
WE'VE ONLY BEEN AT IT TWO DAYS,
AND I FEEL WORN OUT.

1045
00:42:01,087 --> 00:42:02,420
PROBABLY
'CAUSE OF MY STORIES.

1046
00:42:02,453 --> 00:42:06,225
MIGHT AS WELL
KEEP ON LOOKING AROUND.

1047
00:42:06,258 --> 00:42:07,693
OKAY, WELL THEN.

1048
00:42:07,727 --> 00:42:09,662
LIKE SOME MORE COFFEE?
I'LL GET YOU SOME MORE COFFEE.

1049
00:42:09,695 --> 00:42:11,463
DINNER'S READY BACK HERE.

1050
00:42:11,497 --> 00:42:14,198
DO YOU WANT RICE-A-RONI?
THERE'S SOME STEAK TARTAR.

1051
00:42:14,233 --> 00:42:15,968
AND SOME LITTLE
O'BRIEN POTATOES.

1052
00:42:16,002 --> 00:42:18,703
HEY, WHAT'S THIS
HOLE IN THE-- AAH!

1053
00:42:24,277 --> 00:42:26,645
- I FEEL LIKE
LEWIS AND CLARK.
- REALLY?

1054
00:42:26,678 --> 00:42:28,880
YOU BE JERRY LEWIS.
I'LL BE PETULA CLARK.

1055
00:42:28,913 --> 00:42:30,950
[SERVO MIMICS RIMSHOT]

1056
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:36,722
WELL, I GUESS WE MAY AS WELL
GIVE UP FOR THE DAY.

1057
00:42:36,755 --> 00:42:38,823
WELL, YOU WON'T GET
ANY ARGUMENTS FROM ME.

1058
00:42:38,857 --> 00:42:40,927
- OKAY. LET'S GO.
- BUT I DON'T WANNA GO NOW.

1059
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:42,193
WHAT?

1060
00:42:42,227 --> 00:42:44,797
WILL THE LEECH SURVIVE?
WILL THEY DRINK MORE COFFEE?

1061
00:42:44,830 --> 00:42:47,298
AND WILL THE FAT GUY'S WIFE
EVER TOUCH HIM?

1062
00:42:47,332 --> 00:42:48,467
AND WHAT ABOUT NAOMI?

1063
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:51,637
HI THERE.

1064
00:42:51,670 --> 00:42:54,373
LOOK, EITHER PICK UP A PADDLE
OR SIT STILL.

1065
00:42:56,108 --> 00:42:58,577
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

1066
00:42:58,610 --> 00:43:00,645
IS IT ASKING TOO MUCH
TO PULL OVER TO A STATION

1067
00:43:00,678 --> 00:43:02,280
AND ASK FOR DIRECTIONS?
MEN.

1068
00:43:02,313 --> 00:43:05,083
NO. NO.

1069
00:43:05,117 --> 00:43:07,052
CAN WE DO SOMETHING DIFFERENT
NEXT TIME WE GO OUT?

1070
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:09,555
LIKE GO TO A RESTAURANT
OR SOMETHING?

1071
00:43:09,588 --> 00:43:11,190
HELLO AGAIN.
I'M THE LEECH.

1072
00:43:11,223 --> 00:43:14,360
SEE YOU LATER.

1073
00:43:14,393 --> 00:43:15,660
WELL, LET'S SEE.
THAT'LL HOLD ME UNTIL

1074
00:43:15,693 --> 00:43:17,495
I GET TO THE OFFICE,
ANYWAY.

1075
00:43:17,528 --> 00:43:19,432
♪ DOIN' THE BIG FIG NEWTON ♪

1076
00:43:19,465 --> 00:43:22,635
♪ HERE'S THE TRICKY PART,
THE BIG FIG NEWTON ♪

1077
00:43:22,668 --> 00:43:25,070
I'M ASKING YOU FOR
THE LAST TIME, DAVE WALKER.

1078
00:43:25,103 --> 00:43:26,805
DID YOU EAT
THE LAST MOON PIE?

1079
00:43:26,838 --> 00:43:28,407
WILL YOU ANSWER ME,
YOU DIRTY OLD MAN?

1080
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,842
DIRTY OLD MAN? THE ROPERS
GET MORE ACTION THAN US.

1081
00:43:30,875 --> 00:43:32,712
I AIN'T DIRTY, LIZ BABY.

1082
00:43:32,745 --> 00:43:34,513
"LIZ BABY."

1083
00:43:34,547 --> 00:43:36,715
"LIZ HONEY."

1084
00:43:36,748 --> 00:43:38,850
CAN'T YOU THINK OF
ANYTHING ELSE TO SAY, STUPID?

1085
00:43:38,883 --> 00:43:40,718
GOTTA GET THIS ORDER
OVER TO MS. SHOBY.

1086
00:43:40,752 --> 00:43:42,320
SHE'S ONE OF MY
BETTER CUSTOMERS.

1087
00:43:42,353 --> 00:43:44,155
YOU KNOW, I THINK
THE BLOOM'S OFF THE ROSE.

1088
00:43:44,188 --> 00:43:46,492
YEP.

1089
00:43:46,525 --> 00:43:47,927
I LOVE YA, LIZ BABY.

1090
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:50,295
BUT I LOVE GROCERIES MORE.

1091
00:43:50,328 --> 00:43:51,963
GET OUT.

1092
00:43:51,997 --> 00:43:53,265
GET OUT, YOU FAT PIG!

1093
00:43:53,298 --> 00:43:54,900
NOW WAIT A MINUTE.
I DON'T GO CALLING YOU

1094
00:43:54,933 --> 00:43:57,035
A BEAUTIFUL,
SHAPELY WOMAN, DO I?

1095
00:44:01,573 --> 00:44:04,377
OH. CAP. OKAY.

1096
00:44:04,410 --> 00:44:06,212
CLEANUP IN AISLE THREE,
PLEASE.

1097
00:44:09,915 --> 00:44:11,583
LISTEN, DON'T EVEN ASK.
ALL RIGHT?

1098
00:44:11,617 --> 00:44:14,052
--TROUBLE, DO YA?

1099
00:44:14,085 --> 00:44:15,353
YOU KNOW WOMEN, CAL.

1100
00:44:15,387 --> 00:44:18,790
GOTTA GET THE HAIR DOWN
EVERY NOW AND THEN.

1101
00:44:18,823 --> 00:44:20,925
YOU SURE DO KNOW
AN AWFUL LOT ABOUT FEMALES.

1102
00:44:20,958 --> 00:44:24,095
WELL, I WAS A FEMALE ONCE.

1103
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:26,032
I CAN'T STAND HERE
JAWING, CAL.

1104
00:44:26,065 --> 00:44:27,733
GOTTA SAVE MY JAW
FOR EATIN'.

1105
00:44:27,767 --> 00:44:29,768
--TO MS. SHOBY.

1106
00:44:29,802 --> 00:44:31,270
HERE YOU GO, MS. SHOBY.

1107
00:44:31,303 --> 00:44:34,238
--THIS TIME.
- WELL.

1108
00:44:34,272 --> 00:44:36,442
- [SERVO, MUFFLED]
- --GOT HIMSELF KILLED,

1109
00:44:36,475 --> 00:44:39,043
SHE WANTS ME TO SELL OUT
AND MOVE INTO TOWN.

1110
00:44:39,077 --> 00:44:40,212
AND LEAVE ALL THIS?

1111
00:44:40,245 --> 00:44:42,547
DON'T YOU LET HER
BAMBOOZLE YOU, DAVE.

1112
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:45,850
KEEP HER RIGHT HERE
IN THE STORE.

1113
00:44:45,883 --> 00:44:48,087
AFTER ALL, THE PLACE WOULDN'T
BE THE SAME WITHOUT YOU AROUND.

1114
00:44:48,120 --> 00:44:49,788
WELL, THERE'D BE MORE OXYGEN
FOR THE REST OF US.

1115
00:44:49,822 --> 00:44:51,990
THANKS, CAL.
I'D BETTER GET GOING.

1116
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:53,725
SEE YOU WHEN I GET BACK.

1117
00:44:53,758 --> 00:44:56,062
YEAH, I'LL BE AROUND.

1118
00:44:56,095 --> 00:44:57,562
OH, WHAT A RICH LIFE, HUH?

1119
00:44:57,595 --> 00:45:00,365
FLIPPING A WALNUT
IN A SIEVE ALL DAY.

1120
00:45:00,398 --> 00:45:03,768
HEH HEH, NOW I GET MY PICK
OF THE WICKER BASKETS.

1121
00:45:06,638 --> 00:45:08,440
♪♪ [RADIO PLAYS BIG BAND]

1122
00:45:08,473 --> 00:45:09,675
HEY, WHERE ARE YOUR
OUTBOARD MOTORS?

1123
00:45:09,708 --> 00:45:12,310
- OH, THERE THEY ARE.
- LIZ BABY?

1124
00:45:12,343 --> 00:45:14,880
CORA?

1125
00:45:14,913 --> 00:45:17,115
UH, I'M HERE
ABOUT THE AFFAIR.

1126
00:45:17,148 --> 00:45:19,485
I HAVE AN APPOINTMENT
FOR TWO O'CLOCK WEDNESDAY.

1127
00:45:19,518 --> 00:45:21,853
SAY, COULD YOU
SHOW ME SOME SUNDRIES?

1128
00:45:21,887 --> 00:45:25,657
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1129
00:45:25,690 --> 00:45:27,492
YOU WANT SOMETHING, CAL?

1130
00:45:27,525 --> 00:45:29,762
DO I STILL HAVE
A TAB GOING?

1131
00:45:31,930 --> 00:45:33,298
I SURE DO, HONEY.

1132
00:45:33,332 --> 00:45:36,668
WELL, I'M REAL PARTIAL
TO THEM HORMEL DINNER MEALS.

1133
00:45:36,702 --> 00:45:40,205
WHAT? WHAT?
I'M NOT A MIND-READER.

1134
00:45:40,238 --> 00:45:42,440
WOW.

1135
00:45:54,787 --> 00:45:56,122
WHOO. BOY,
SOME STRONG COFFEE.

1136
00:45:56,155 --> 00:45:58,157
I'M GETTING BUGGED.
MY NECKPLATE'S QUIVERING.

1137
00:45:58,190 --> 00:46:01,193
MY CUTE LITTLE ACRYLIC HANDS
ARE SHAKING AND SWEATY.

1138
00:46:01,227 --> 00:46:02,760
- FILL HER UP, JOEL.
- YEAH, THAT'S IT.

1139
00:46:02,795 --> 00:46:04,463
ANYTHING YOU SAY,
LITTLE AMIGO.

1140
00:46:04,497 --> 00:46:05,697
OOH. SUGAR FOR ME.

1141
00:46:05,730 --> 00:46:08,100
OKAY, I'M RIGHT ON IT,
GYPSY. NO PROBLEM.

1142
00:46:08,133 --> 00:46:09,868
BOY, JOEL,
TODAY'S EXPERIMENT'S GOT BITE.

1143
00:46:09,902 --> 00:46:11,270
IT'S LIKE--

1144
00:46:11,303 --> 00:46:12,972
WELL, IT'S LIKE
A FEVER DREAM, CROW.

1145
00:46:13,005 --> 00:46:14,238
YOU KNOW, OR LIKE
ONE OF THOSE DREAMS

1146
00:46:14,272 --> 00:46:15,440
WHEN YOU GET HOME
AT MIDNIGHT,

1147
00:46:15,473 --> 00:46:17,508
AND YOU WOLF DOWN
A UKRAINIAN SAUSAGE PASTRY

1148
00:46:17,542 --> 00:46:19,612
AND A GROLSCH BEER.
THEN YOU GO STRAIGHT TO BED?

1149
00:46:19,645 --> 00:46:22,080
YEAH, OR WHEN YOU JUST GOT OFF
A 12-HOUR SHIFT AT ARBY'S,

1150
00:46:22,113 --> 00:46:23,515
AND YOU'RE WATCHING T.V.
AT 3:00 AM,

1151
00:46:23,548 --> 00:46:25,183
AND THEN YOU FALL ASLEEP
DURING OMEGA MAN.

1152
00:46:25,217 --> 00:46:26,652
- YEAH.
- DO YOU HAVE ANY MORE
HALF AND HALF?

1153
00:46:26,685 --> 00:46:27,953
YEAH, NO PROBLEM.
YOU KNOW, I HAD

1154
00:46:27,987 --> 00:46:29,320
A REALLY WEIRD DREAM
LAST NIGHT.

1155
00:46:29,353 --> 00:46:30,855
- I DREAM THAT--
- MORE.

1156
00:46:30,888 --> 00:46:32,457
WE ALL GOT BACK TO EARTH,

1157
00:46:32,490 --> 00:46:34,727
AND THEN YOU GUYS GOT
A DUPLEX TOGETHER.

1158
00:46:34,760 --> 00:46:35,993
WELL, YOU KNOW,
JUST LAST NIGHT,

1159
00:46:36,027 --> 00:46:37,762
I DREAMED THAT I HAD
A REALLY NICE GIRLFRIEND

1160
00:46:37,795 --> 00:46:39,463
WITH RED HAIR
AND A BLUE DRESS.

1161
00:46:39,498 --> 00:46:41,833
THEN SHE TURNED INTO A GARGOYLE,
AND I WAS REALLY SCARED.

1162
00:46:41,867 --> 00:46:43,968
BUT THEN JESUS CAME,
AND EVERYTHING WAS OKAY.

1163
00:46:44,002 --> 00:46:45,737
- YOU SAW JESUS?
- WELL, YEAH.

1164
00:46:45,770 --> 00:46:47,873
REAL NICE GUY, TOO.
THINNER THAN YOU MIGHT THINK.

1165
00:46:47,907 --> 00:46:49,708
I DON'T REMEMBER MY DREAMS
TOO OFTEN, JOEL.

1166
00:46:49,742 --> 00:46:51,210
WELL, YOU KNOW,
I NEVER COULD EITHER,

1167
00:46:51,243 --> 00:46:52,912
UNTIL I STARTED
KEEPING A JOURNAL.

1168
00:46:52,945 --> 00:46:55,747
HEY, I'M CURIOUS.
WHAT DO YOU DREAM ABOUT, GYPSY?

1169
00:46:55,780 --> 00:46:58,183
I DREAM I FLY IN COLOR.

1170
00:46:58,217 --> 00:46:59,985
OH, YOU DREAMED YOU FLEW.

1171
00:47:00,018 --> 00:47:01,920
THAT MEANS YOU'RE INTUITIVE.

1172
00:47:01,953 --> 00:47:03,355
- THAT'S REALLY--
- I HAVE ONE DREAM

1173
00:47:03,388 --> 00:47:05,323
ABOUT A LITTLE
FRENCH CAFE IN PARIS.

1174
00:47:05,357 --> 00:47:07,158
RIGHT UP
THE RUE DE FLORENTIN.

1175
00:47:07,192 --> 00:47:09,260
WHAT WAS THAT WAITER'S NAME?

1176
00:47:09,293 --> 00:47:10,828
[BOTS]
JEAN-LUC!

1177
00:47:10,862 --> 00:47:12,363
OH, YOU HAD THAT DREAM TOO?

1178
00:47:12,397 --> 00:47:14,667
WE'VE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

1179
00:47:23,908 --> 00:47:25,643
CAREFUL, I SPILLED
A LITTLE COFFEE.

1180
00:47:25,677 --> 00:47:28,413
- OKAY.
- I AM WIRED.

1181
00:47:28,447 --> 00:47:29,915
[CROW GROWLS]

1182
00:47:29,948 --> 00:47:32,150
I DIDN'T HURT YOU NOW,
DID I?

1183
00:47:32,183 --> 00:47:34,887
WHY, IT'S JUST THAT
YOU'RE SO STRONG.

1184
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:37,322
SMELLING, I MEAN.

1185
00:47:37,355 --> 00:47:39,023
I LIKE A MAN WHO'S STRONG.

1186
00:47:39,057 --> 00:47:42,560
SMELLING, I MEAN.

1187
00:47:42,593 --> 00:47:46,232
YOU SURE PICKED A DOOZY THEN,
MARRYING DAVE.

1188
00:47:46,265 --> 00:47:48,400
I DON'T THINK
HE'S GOT A MUSCLE IN HIM.

1189
00:47:48,433 --> 00:47:50,168
JUST A BIG PIECE OF FLAB.

1190
00:47:50,202 --> 00:47:52,037
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT
THE FLAB I LOVE.

1191
00:47:52,070 --> 00:47:53,638
OH, HON...

1192
00:47:53,672 --> 00:47:55,073
I DIDN'T MEAN
ANYTHING AGAINST YOU.

1193
00:47:55,107 --> 00:47:56,975
I MEAN,
YOU'RE A LITTLE PIECE OF FLAB.

1194
00:47:57,008 --> 00:48:00,578
JUST THAT I CAN'T SEE
A REAL WOMAN LIKE YOU

1195
00:48:00,612 --> 00:48:02,547
TIED IN WITH
A TUB OF LARD LIKE HIM.

1196
00:48:02,580 --> 00:48:06,385
I JUST CAN'T IMAGINE
YOU MAKING LOVE IS ALL.

1197
00:48:06,418 --> 00:48:09,588
YOU WOULDN'T
UNDERSTAND, CAL.

1198
00:48:09,622 --> 00:48:11,088
YOU KNOW, I--

1199
00:48:11,122 --> 00:48:12,690
I'VE WANTED TO TELL HIM.

1200
00:48:12,723 --> 00:48:15,093
I'M THE ROBIN McDONALD
FOR THIS REGION.

1201
00:48:15,127 --> 00:48:16,828
YOU JUST
WOULDN'T UNDERSTAND.

1202
00:48:16,862 --> 00:48:18,597
HEY, TRY ME.

1203
00:48:18,630 --> 00:48:19,932
FREE TRIAL SAMPLE.
TRY ME FOR A WEEK.

1204
00:48:19,965 --> 00:48:22,033
--ALL ABOUT IT.

1205
00:48:22,067 --> 00:48:24,302
SISTER, YOU GOT ROOTS.

1206
00:48:24,335 --> 00:48:26,905
- OOH.
- HUH?

1207
00:48:26,938 --> 00:48:28,773
DID YOU SAY SOMETHING?
I WASN'T LISTENING.

1208
00:48:28,807 --> 00:48:31,310
- --TO ME.
- CLEARLY.

1209
00:48:31,343 --> 00:48:33,445
KIND OF LOOKS LIKE A FOREST
UP THERE IN YOUR NOSE.

1210
00:48:33,478 --> 00:48:34,813
IF YOU TOLD ME
YOU KILLED YOUR PA,

1211
00:48:34,847 --> 00:48:37,715
AND YOUR MA,
AND YOUR WHOLE FAMILY.

1212
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:39,083
I'LL FIGHT TO PROTECT YOU.

1213
00:48:39,117 --> 00:48:42,120
MM-HMM.

1214
00:48:42,153 --> 00:48:43,955
OUCH. MY KEYS.

1215
00:48:43,988 --> 00:48:46,492
HEY, REMEMBER MY PA AND MY MA
AND MY WHOLE FAMILY?

1216
00:48:46,525 --> 00:48:49,160
WELL...

1217
00:48:49,193 --> 00:48:50,962
WE NOW RETURN
TO FAT GUY GOES NUTZOID.

1218
00:48:50,995 --> 00:48:52,397
A TROMA PRESENTATION.

1219
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:54,598
HE'S USING
AN ADULTERAL DECOY.

1220
00:48:54,633 --> 00:48:58,603
COME ON, BABY.
[SMOOCHING SOUNDS]

1221
00:48:58,637 --> 00:49:00,272
MS. SHOBY, I GOT
YOUR GROCERIES HERE.

1222
00:49:00,305 --> 00:49:03,542
DON'T WANT
NO TROUBLE THIS TIME.

1223
00:49:03,575 --> 00:49:06,312
LIKE THAT GUY COULD
SNEAK UP ON SOMEBODY, HUH?

1224
00:49:06,345 --> 00:49:10,215
HONEY, YOU MAKING OUT WITH
ONE OF MY FRIENDS BACK HERE?

1225
00:49:11,317 --> 00:49:14,653
HMM. SWAMP BLANKET BINGO.

1226
00:49:14,687 --> 00:49:16,455
LET'S SEE NOW,
THERE'S SOME TREES

1227
00:49:16,488 --> 00:49:18,423
AND A CAR AND MY WIFE

1228
00:49:18,457 --> 00:49:20,658
MAKING OUT WITH-- OH?

1229
00:49:20,692 --> 00:49:22,393
FIRST HUSBAND WAS
A NO-GOOD BUM.

1230
00:49:22,427 --> 00:49:24,262
SECOND HUSBAND, NO-GOOD BUM.

1231
00:49:24,295 --> 00:49:28,200
THIRD HUSBAND, NO-GOOD BUM.

1232
00:49:28,233 --> 00:49:30,502
USE TO GET LASHED UP,
COME HOME AND BEAT UP ON ME.

1233
00:49:30,535 --> 00:49:32,170
- OH, MERLE HAGGARD.
- HEY.

1234
00:49:32,203 --> 00:49:33,505
OR GEORGE JONES.

1235
00:49:33,538 --> 00:49:35,973
HE MUST'VE BEEN
A PRIZE PIG.

1236
00:49:36,007 --> 00:49:38,577
ONE NIGHT HE TRIED
TO HOLD UP A GAS STATION.

1237
00:49:38,610 --> 00:49:40,378
BUT HE WASN'T VERY STRONG,
AND IT FELL ON HIM.

1238
00:49:40,412 --> 00:49:43,215
--COULDN'T EVEN RUN.

1239
00:49:43,248 --> 00:49:46,183
THEY CAUGHT HIM
LESS THAN A MILE AWAY.

1240
00:49:46,217 --> 00:49:49,020
GOT SET UP.

1241
00:49:49,053 --> 00:49:50,155
I GOT A DIVORCE.

1242
00:49:50,188 --> 00:49:52,090
THEN I DATED DAVID SOUL
FOR A WHILE,

1243
00:49:52,123 --> 00:49:55,193
AND SAME THING.

1244
00:49:55,227 --> 00:49:56,828
AFTER THREE YEARS
LIVING--

1245
00:49:56,862 --> 00:50:00,165
[BOTS SNORE]

1246
00:50:00,198 --> 00:50:03,168
[SERVO SNORES, COUGHS]

1247
00:50:03,202 --> 00:50:06,438
HEY, SHE'S REALLY
OPENING UP TO HIM.

1248
00:50:06,472 --> 00:50:08,240
I WISH IT COULD'VE BEEN ME.

1249
00:50:08,273 --> 00:50:10,575
I'D KNOW HOW TO TAKE CARE
OF A WOMAN LIKE YOU, LIZ.

1250
00:50:10,608 --> 00:50:13,512
- [SERVO GROWLS]
- MAYBE IT'S TOO LATE, CAL.

1251
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:19,317
GOOD THING THEY BROUGHT
A MAKE-OUT TARP.

1252
00:50:19,350 --> 00:50:20,918
MM-HMM.

1253
00:50:20,952 --> 00:50:22,520
I BELIEVE THIS IS MY DANCE.

1254
00:50:22,553 --> 00:50:23,855
YOU'RE WRONG, WOMAN.

1255
00:50:23,888 --> 00:50:26,758
IT'S TOO LATE
FOR THE BOTH OF YOU.

1256
00:50:26,792 --> 00:50:27,958
SHE DROPPED A CONTACT LENS
IN MY MOUTH

1257
00:50:27,992 --> 00:50:29,527
AND WAS TRYING TO GET IT OUT
WITH HER TONGUE.

1258
00:50:29,560 --> 00:50:30,562
YEAH, THAT'S IT, AND--

1259
00:50:30,595 --> 00:50:32,697
NOW, GET UP.

1260
00:50:32,730 --> 00:50:34,933
NOW LOOK, DAVE, I KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE THINKING, BUT--

1261
00:50:34,967 --> 00:50:38,035
I GOT DOUBLE-LARGE SHOT
IN THIS HERE THING.

1262
00:50:39,403 --> 00:50:43,142
YOU GOT TWO SECONDS
BEFORE I PULL THE TRIGGER.

1263
00:50:43,175 --> 00:50:44,943
O-KAY. SO I GUESS

1264
00:50:44,977 --> 00:50:46,445
I'LL BE SEEING YOU
THERE, HUH?

1265
00:50:46,478 --> 00:50:48,313
NO POINT IN
GETTING RILED, DAVE.

1266
00:50:48,347 --> 00:50:50,982
JUST ADVANCING THE FLAP.
NOTHING PERSONAL.

1267
00:50:51,015 --> 00:50:53,385
SHE'S BEEN PESTERING ME
FOR MONTHS TO TAKE HER OUT.

1268
00:50:53,418 --> 00:50:57,188
SURE, CAL. I UNDERSTAND.

1269
00:50:57,222 --> 00:50:58,590
GET HER UP SO I CAN
GET A BETTER LOOK

1270
00:50:58,623 --> 00:51:00,325
AT THE LYING LITTLE TRAMP.

1271
00:51:00,358 --> 00:51:03,995
OH, WHICH ONE OF US
IS THE LYING L-- OH.

1272
00:51:04,028 --> 00:51:05,563
COME ON, GET UP.

1273
00:51:05,597 --> 00:51:08,367
NO! HE'LL KILL ME.
HE'LL KILL ME.

1274
00:51:08,400 --> 00:51:09,968
[CAL MUTTERS]

1275
00:51:10,002 --> 00:51:12,137
WHEN YOUR HUSBAND WANTS
TO TAKE A LOOK AT YOU.

1276
00:51:12,170 --> 00:51:15,840
UH, IS THIS HER?

1277
00:51:15,873 --> 00:51:17,408
YOU-- YOU WALK
ALL THE WAY, DAVE?

1278
00:51:17,442 --> 00:51:21,613
NO, THERE'S A MOTORCYCLE
IN MY PANTS-- WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1279
00:51:21,647 --> 00:51:23,282
- GET OVER THERE!
- OOH.

1280
00:51:23,315 --> 00:51:25,917
NOW-- NOW, DAVID,
AIN'T AS BAD AS YOU THINK.

1281
00:51:25,950 --> 00:51:28,453
- IT'S FANTASTIC.
- SHUT UP!

1282
00:51:28,487 --> 00:51:31,490
- TRAMP.
- WHAT'RE YOU GONNA DO?

1283
00:51:31,523 --> 00:51:35,293
I'M GONNA MAKE YOU
LISTEN TO SUPERTRAMP.

1284
00:51:35,327 --> 00:51:37,228
DAVE, YOU PUT DOWN
THAT GUN BEFORE I GET MAD

1285
00:51:37,262 --> 00:51:39,563
- AND MAKE YOU EAT IT.
- EAT IT? MMM.

1286
00:51:39,597 --> 00:51:41,165
HEY, DON'T TRY
TO DISTRACT ME.

1287
00:51:41,198 --> 00:51:43,100
GO RIGHT AHEAD AND TRY.

1288
00:51:43,135 --> 00:51:45,070
- [GUN BLAST]
- I KNOW WHAT YOU'RE THINKING.

1289
00:51:45,103 --> 00:51:47,972
- DID I FIRE
ONE SHOT OR ONLY ONE?
- MOVE!

1290
00:51:49,808 --> 00:51:52,210
EVERY WEEKEND,
I GO THROUGH THIS.

1291
00:51:52,243 --> 00:51:54,813
SHH.

1292
00:51:54,847 --> 00:51:56,915
OH. JUST WANTED THE TARP.

1293
00:51:59,117 --> 00:52:03,555
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

1294
00:52:03,588 --> 00:52:04,890
[GUNSHOT]

1295
00:52:04,923 --> 00:52:06,323
NOW IT'S
THE MOST DANGEROUS GAME.

1296
00:52:06,357 --> 00:52:08,327
I'LL SAY.

1297
00:52:08,360 --> 00:52:10,428
OH...

1298
00:52:10,462 --> 00:52:12,497
OH...

1299
00:52:15,833 --> 00:52:17,568
THIS IS MORE LIKE
NIGHT OF THE IGUANA

1300
00:52:17,602 --> 00:52:20,872
THAN ATTACK OF
THE GIANT LEECHES.

1301
00:52:20,905 --> 00:52:24,775
[SERVO GRUNTS, PANTS]

1302
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,878
QUICK, LET'S GO
TELL THE CAMP COUNSELOR.

1303
00:52:26,912 --> 00:52:28,613
HE'LL HELP US!

1304
00:52:28,647 --> 00:52:31,182
- COME ON!
- I CAN'T GO ANY FURTHER!

1305
00:52:31,215 --> 00:52:33,218
I GOT NOWHERE ELSE TO GO!

1306
00:52:36,487 --> 00:52:40,158
[CROW PANTS, GRUNTS]

1307
00:52:40,192 --> 00:52:41,660
YOU TWO GO ON WITHOUT ME.

1308
00:52:41,693 --> 00:52:44,997
OH, WAIT A MINUTE.
THAT'S ALL WRONG.

1309
00:52:45,030 --> 00:52:48,065
THUNDER HUSBAND.

1310
00:52:48,098 --> 00:52:51,268
I'LL CATCH YOU,
YOU WASCALLY ADULTEWERS.

1311
00:52:54,172 --> 00:52:55,840
WAIT A MINUTE,
HE'S LOADING HIS GUN

1312
00:52:55,873 --> 00:52:57,408
WITH TOOTSIE ROLLS.

1313
00:52:57,442 --> 00:53:00,045
- MMM.
- MM. [SERVO SMACKS LIPS]

1314
00:53:00,078 --> 00:53:02,613
GO ON! RUN!
RUN TILL YOU DROP!

1315
00:53:02,647 --> 00:53:04,917
LIKE I WILL!

1316
00:53:07,118 --> 00:53:08,920
UH, LET ME GUESS.
SHE BROKE HER HEEL.

1317
00:53:08,953 --> 00:53:10,655
YEAH, SHE'S THE GIRL.
SHE'S SUPPOSED TO.

1318
00:53:10,688 --> 00:53:13,492
MM-HMM.

1319
00:53:13,525 --> 00:53:16,027
NOW WHAT IS WITH THE MUD?
DID WE MISS SOME METAPHOR?

1320
00:53:16,060 --> 00:53:17,995
I DON'T KNOW.

1321
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:20,298
SOLE OF THE SOUL,
OR SOMETHING?

1322
00:53:22,133 --> 00:53:24,335
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
PULL!

1323
00:53:24,368 --> 00:53:28,005
THAT ONE WAS
JUST FOR ME. HAH!

1324
00:53:28,038 --> 00:53:30,175
I CAN'T GO ON ANYMORE!
CALEB, YOU'VE GOT TO LET ME STOP

1325
00:53:30,208 --> 00:53:31,610
- AND REST FOR A MINUTE--
- SHUT UP! [MUTTERS]

1326
00:53:31,643 --> 00:53:35,480
- [GUNSHOT]
- HEY, THAT WAS HIS HEART
BLOWING UP.

1327
00:53:35,513 --> 00:53:37,148
I CAN'T GO ON.

1328
00:53:37,182 --> 00:53:39,150
CALEB!

1329
00:53:40,585 --> 00:53:43,888
[SERVO MIMICS BRANCH SNAPPING]

1330
00:53:43,922 --> 00:53:46,592
THERE'S GOTTA BE A TRAILER PARK
AROUND HERE SOMEWHERE.

1331
00:53:46,625 --> 00:53:48,360
MAN, LOOK AT ALL THE WEED.
WHERE ARE THEY,

1332
00:53:48,393 --> 00:53:51,062
TOMMY CHONG'S BACKYARD?

1333
00:53:51,095 --> 00:53:52,663
[GUNSHOT]

1334
00:53:52,697 --> 00:53:55,033
SUDDENLY,
THEY'RE THE DEFIANT ONES.

1335
00:53:58,035 --> 00:54:00,272
AHH.

1336
00:54:00,305 --> 00:54:04,542
[ALL]
UH-- HUH? HMM? OH--

1337
00:54:04,575 --> 00:54:06,310
WELP, GUESS YOU
CAUGHT UP TO US.

1338
00:54:06,343 --> 00:54:08,347
GO ON. KEEP GOING.

1339
00:54:08,380 --> 00:54:10,715
DAVE. PLEASE,
YOU'VE GOTTA LISTEN.

1340
00:54:10,748 --> 00:54:12,917
IT WASN'T MY FAULT, HONEST.

1341
00:54:12,950 --> 00:54:15,520
SHE KEPT PLAYING UP TO ME
EVERY TIME YOU TURNED YOUR BACK.

1342
00:54:15,553 --> 00:54:17,088
- IT WASN'T MY FAULT!
- I CAN'T BE HELD ACCOUNTABLE!

1343
00:54:17,122 --> 00:54:18,490
AND YOU CALL YOURSELF A MAN!

1344
00:54:18,523 --> 00:54:20,358
SHE'S GOT BOSOMS
AND EVERYTHING!

1345
00:54:20,392 --> 00:54:22,793
YOU AND YOUR MUSCLES!

1346
00:54:22,827 --> 00:54:24,228
- OH, SHE SNAGGED ON HIM.
- SHUT UP, YOU TRAMP!

1347
00:54:24,262 --> 00:54:26,798
IF IT WASN'T FOR YOU,
I WOULDN'T BE IN THIS FIX.

1348
00:54:26,832 --> 00:54:29,233
AND MY OLD FRIEND DAVE WOULDN'T
BE DOING THIS THING TO ME.

1349
00:54:29,267 --> 00:54:31,368
- [SERVO SOBS]
- IT'S ALL YOUR FAULT.

1350
00:54:31,402 --> 00:54:32,837
- OH!
- SHE DID IT AGAIN.

1351
00:54:32,870 --> 00:54:34,538
GET GOING.

1352
00:54:34,572 --> 00:54:36,207
BUT-- BUT DAVE, DAVE,

1353
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:39,610
WE'VE BEEN FRIENDS-- WE'VE BEEN
FRIENDS A LONG TIME, DAVE.

1354
00:54:39,643 --> 00:54:42,847
YOU WOULDN'T KILL
AN OLD FRIEND, DAVE.

1355
00:54:42,880 --> 00:54:45,517
IF YOU DON'T MOVE,
I'LL KILL YA WHERE YOU STAND.

1356
00:54:45,550 --> 00:54:46,985
- BUT DAVE!
- [SERVO SOBS]

1357
00:54:47,018 --> 00:54:49,720
- [GUNSHOT]
- YOU BRAVE, BIG MAN.

1358
00:54:49,753 --> 00:54:52,723
HEY, DID HE JUST KILL HIM,
OR WHAT--

1359
00:54:52,757 --> 00:54:54,725
OH.

1360
00:54:54,758 --> 00:54:57,628
AND AS FOR YOU,
YOUNG LADY, YOU'RE GROUNDED.

1361
00:54:57,662 --> 00:54:59,497
- D'OH!
- THEY'RE MELTING.

1362
00:54:59,530 --> 00:55:01,398
- D'OH!
- [BOTH SCREAM]

1363
00:55:01,432 --> 00:55:05,103
- D'OH NO!
- [CAL SCREAMS]

1364
00:55:05,137 --> 00:55:07,438
- DAVE!
- PLEASE, DAVE!

1365
00:55:07,472 --> 00:55:08,540
I'M SORRY, DAVE!

1366
00:55:08,573 --> 00:55:10,375
DON'T MAKE US
GO IN THE DEEP END!

1367
00:55:10,408 --> 00:55:12,110
WE'RE NOT READY
FOR THE DEEP END YET!

1368
00:55:12,143 --> 00:55:14,645
- NO!
- [LIZ SCREAMS MANICALLY]

1369
00:55:14,678 --> 00:55:16,882
HEY, QUIT LAUGHING!
I'M TRYING TO HUMILIATE YOU.

1370
00:55:16,915 --> 00:55:18,983
--HONEY, I'M SORRY, DAVE!

1371
00:55:19,017 --> 00:55:21,720
I'M SORRY!
I DIDN'T MEAN IT!

1372
00:55:21,753 --> 00:55:23,253
- I DIDN'T MEAN IT!
- PLEASE, DAVE,

1373
00:55:23,287 --> 00:55:25,123
BRING BACK
THE CHICKEN CORDON BLEU!

1374
00:55:25,157 --> 00:55:27,458
PLEASE, DON'T LEAVE ME
TO DIE, DAVE!

1375
00:55:27,492 --> 00:55:28,727
OH!

1376
00:55:28,760 --> 00:55:29,993
YOU THINK
YOU'LL LEARN ENOUGH

1377
00:55:30,028 --> 00:55:32,397
TO STAY AWAY
FROM MY WOMAN, CAL?

1378
00:55:32,430 --> 00:55:35,200
OH! I'LL LEARN PLENTY!
I'LL GET A PhD

1379
00:55:35,233 --> 00:55:37,002
IN STAYING AWAY
FROM YOUR WIFE.

1380
00:55:37,035 --> 00:55:39,803
--I'LL DO ANYTHING
YOU SAY, DAVE. ANYTHING!

1381
00:55:39,837 --> 00:55:42,473
- WOULD YOU ROB A SHOP?
- ♪ ANYTHING ♪

1382
00:55:42,507 --> 00:55:45,543
COME ON OUT OF THERE.

1383
00:55:45,577 --> 00:55:48,312
DAVE! DAVID.
GIVE US A HAND.

1384
00:55:48,345 --> 00:55:50,982
- HMM?
- [CAL MUTTERS]

1385
00:55:51,015 --> 00:55:52,683
- DAVID.
- AYE CARUMBA!

1386
00:55:52,717 --> 00:55:55,018
OH MY GOD.

1387
00:55:55,053 --> 00:55:56,722
LOOK OUT! BEHIND YA!

1388
00:55:56,755 --> 00:55:58,523
- DAVID!
- I AIN'T FALLIN' FOR THAT.

1389
00:55:58,557 --> 00:56:00,058
AAH! OH, DAVE!

1390
00:56:00,092 --> 00:56:01,292
[SERVO MUTTERS]

1391
00:56:01,325 --> 00:56:03,962
UH, DON'T HELP
OR ANYTHING, DAVE.

1392
00:56:03,995 --> 00:56:05,028
[LIZ SCREAMS]

1393
00:56:05,063 --> 00:56:06,363
GEE, IT WAS OKAY
TO SHOOT 'EM,

1394
00:56:06,397 --> 00:56:09,000
BUT THIS. YUCK.

1395
00:56:09,033 --> 00:56:10,735
THINK THEY KNOW WE'RE HERE?

1396
00:56:13,572 --> 00:56:15,707
AIN'T NOTHING
DOWN HERE, SHERIFF.

1397
00:56:15,740 --> 00:56:17,775
'CEPT FOR THESE
DEAD FOLKS.

1398
00:56:17,808 --> 00:56:21,045
WELL, I'M GETTING
TIRED OF THIS.

1399
00:56:21,078 --> 00:56:24,882
COME ON IN, BOYS.

1400
00:56:24,915 --> 00:56:27,318
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

1401
00:56:27,352 --> 00:56:29,287
WELP, IF THERE WAS
ANY BODIES OUT THERE,

1402
00:56:29,320 --> 00:56:31,488
WE'D'VE FOUND THEM.

1403
00:56:31,522 --> 00:56:34,358
I WANT SOME
STRAIGHT ANSWERS, WALTER.

1404
00:56:34,392 --> 00:56:35,927
AND DON'T GIVE ME
ANY MORE OF THAT CRUD

1405
00:56:35,960 --> 00:56:38,062
ABOUT MONSTERS, EITHER.

1406
00:56:38,095 --> 00:56:39,930
WHERE'D YOU HIDE 'EM
AFTER YOU KILLED 'EM?

1407
00:56:39,963 --> 00:56:42,167
[SERVO BELCHES]
SORRY.

1408
00:56:42,200 --> 00:56:44,835
TO TELL YOU
THE TRUTH, SHERIFF,

1409
00:56:44,868 --> 00:56:46,203
I DIDN'T KILL THEM.

1410
00:56:46,237 --> 00:56:47,838
I ATE 'EM.

1411
00:56:47,872 --> 00:56:50,040
JUST WANTED
TO SCARE THEM GOOD.

1412
00:56:50,073 --> 00:56:52,277
OH, DON'T CRY.
I HATE IT WHEN YOU CRY.

1413
00:56:52,310 --> 00:56:54,712
--LIZ.

1414
00:56:54,745 --> 00:56:57,548
I WOULDN'T DO
ANYTHING TO HURT HER.

1415
00:56:57,582 --> 00:56:58,817
I LOVED HER.

1416
00:56:58,850 --> 00:57:01,018
I LOVED HER MORE THAN
TWICE-BAKED POTATOES.

1417
00:57:01,052 --> 00:57:03,187
YOU LOVED HER.
THAT'S WHY YOU CHASED HER

1418
00:57:03,220 --> 00:57:05,055
THROUGH THE SWAMP
WITH A SHOTGUN.

1419
00:57:05,088 --> 00:57:06,590
WELL, IT'S TOUGH LOVE,
ADMITTEDLY.

1420
00:57:06,623 --> 00:57:10,195
COME ON, WALKER.
WHERE'D YOU HIDE THE BODIES?

1421
00:57:10,228 --> 00:57:11,495
WON'T YOU BELIEVE ME?

1422
00:57:11,528 --> 00:57:13,430
IT WAS SOME MONSTERS, THEY--

1423
00:57:13,465 --> 00:57:17,302
TAKE HIM OUT OF HERE
BEFORE I LOSE MY TEMPER.

1424
00:57:17,335 --> 00:57:19,137
- GARY COOPER IN A CAMEO ROLE.
- [JOEL CLAPS]

1425
00:57:19,170 --> 00:57:20,505
- GARY COOPER,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.
- [CROW WHISTLES]

1426
00:57:20,538 --> 00:57:23,140
- GARY COOPER.
- YUP.

1427
00:57:23,173 --> 00:57:24,575
HEY, IT'S BARTLES
AND JAYMES.

1428
00:57:24,608 --> 00:57:26,043
COUNTY PAY A REWARD

1429
00:57:26,077 --> 00:57:28,178
IF'N SOMEONE FINDS
A BODY, SHERIFF?

1430
00:57:28,212 --> 00:57:30,815
- REWARD.
- $50.

1431
00:57:30,848 --> 00:57:32,350
AND YOU GET
TO KEEP THE BODY.

1432
00:57:32,383 --> 00:57:33,818
THOSE EXTRA JEANS
YOU NEED.

1433
00:57:33,852 --> 00:57:37,755
- EACH?
- YEAH.

1434
00:57:37,788 --> 00:57:39,490
- SOUNDS LIKE AFRICA.
- [CROW SQUAWKS]

1435
00:57:39,523 --> 00:57:42,993
YOU KNOW, I NEVER
THOUGHT THAT OF OLD DAVE.

1436
00:57:43,027 --> 00:57:45,197
OF COURSE, EVERYBODY KNOWS
THAT CAL AND LIZ HAD

1437
00:57:45,230 --> 00:57:46,597
A HANKERING FOR EACH OTHER.

1438
00:57:46,630 --> 00:57:48,700
I THINK IT WENT
WAY BEYOND HANKERING.

1439
00:57:48,733 --> 00:57:51,702
- MM-HMM.
- DURN FOOLS.

1440
00:57:51,735 --> 00:57:54,305
GRAPPLIN' OUT THERE
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE WATER.

1441
00:57:54,338 --> 00:57:56,407
IF'N THEM IS STILL IN THERE,

1442
00:57:56,440 --> 00:57:58,710
YOU CAN BET
SOME OLD BULL GATOR'S

1443
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:01,112
GOT 'EM STUFFED
IN HIS CAVE UNDER THE BANK

1444
00:58:01,145 --> 00:58:04,048
- EW.
- LETTIN' 'EM RIPEN UP
FOR A FEW DAYS.

1445
00:58:04,082 --> 00:58:06,250
JEB, YOU GOT
A REAL DARK SIDE.

1446
00:58:06,283 --> 00:58:08,452
WELL, WHAT WE NEED NOW

1447
00:58:08,485 --> 00:58:10,087
IS SOME LONG CYPRUS POLES

1448
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:11,455
TO GO IN THERE
AND PULL 'EM--

1449
00:58:11,488 --> 00:58:12,790
WE'LL DRINK
THE PALM DRY, AND--

1450
00:58:12,823 --> 00:58:14,325
NO, NO, NO.

1451
00:58:14,358 --> 00:58:18,228
OTIS, YOUR QUISP IS READY.

1452
00:58:18,262 --> 00:58:20,732
- [SERVO WHISTLES]
- HE'S STUCK TO THE CEILING.

1453
00:58:20,765 --> 00:58:22,967
OH GREAT, A SWINGER.
ALWAYS ON MY SHIFT.

1454
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:27,372
- CAN WE EAT THE QUISP?
- FOR CRYIN' OUT LOUD.

1455
00:58:27,405 --> 00:58:28,740
I JUST LOVE THESE HUMMELS.

1456
00:58:28,773 --> 00:58:31,008
I'M SORRY, DOC.
I CAN'T DO IT.

1457
00:58:31,042 --> 00:58:32,343
WELL, I'D HAVE
TO DO IT MYSELF.

1458
00:58:32,377 --> 00:58:33,978
WOULDN'T WANNA
HAVE TO ARREST YOU, DOC,

1459
00:58:34,012 --> 00:58:35,980
BUT I WILL IF I FIND YOU
NEAR THE PRESERVE

1460
00:58:36,013 --> 00:58:38,015
- WITH ANY EXPLOSIVES.
- STEVE.

1461
00:58:38,048 --> 00:58:39,850
I'M SORRY, NAN,
THAT'S THE WAY IT'S GOTTA BE.

1462
00:58:39,883 --> 00:58:41,987
- I'M A JERK.
- HE'S RIGHT, NAN.

1463
00:58:42,020 --> 00:58:44,288
IT'S HIS JOB
TO PROTECT WILDLIFE.

1464
00:58:44,322 --> 00:58:46,723
- WHAT ABOUT HUMAN LIFE?
- HMM?

1465
00:58:46,757 --> 00:58:49,227
THREE PEOPLE HAVE BEEN KILLED
IN THAT GAME PRESERVE.

1466
00:58:49,260 --> 00:58:50,962
- YEAH? SO?
- DOESN'T THAT MEAN
ANYTHING TO YOU?

1467
00:58:50,995 --> 00:58:52,597
NAN, TRY TO UNDERSTAND.

1468
00:58:52,630 --> 00:58:54,398
- I'M A JERK.
- --SOMETHING IN THE SWAMP

1469
00:58:54,432 --> 00:58:56,200
WAS RESPONSIBLE
FOR THOSE DEATHS,

1470
00:58:56,233 --> 00:58:58,368
I WOULDN'T HESITATE
A MINUTE.

1471
00:58:58,402 --> 00:59:00,638
WE'VE BEEN TOGETHER
THE LAST THREE DAYS.

1472
00:59:00,672 --> 00:59:02,640
WE DIDN'T SEE
A TRACE OF ANYTHING UNUSUAL.

1473
00:59:02,673 --> 00:59:04,108
EXCEPT FOR
THAT TEN-FOOT LEECH.

1474
00:59:04,142 --> 00:59:06,310
NOT SO MUCH AS A SUGGESTION
OF ANY FORM OF LIFE

1475
00:59:06,343 --> 00:59:07,978
- UNKNOWN TO US.
- STEVE--

1476
00:59:08,012 --> 00:59:09,713
WHOA. EASY-LIFT
NEEDS ADJUSTING.

1477
00:59:09,747 --> 00:59:11,715
ALL RIGHT,
I'LL ADMIT SAWYER'S DEATH

1478
00:59:11,748 --> 00:59:13,785
LEFT A LOT OF QUESTIONS
UNANSWERED.

1479
00:59:13,818 --> 00:59:15,353
BUT YOU CAN BET
YOUR BOTTOM DOLLAR

1480
00:59:15,387 --> 00:59:18,122
THE OTHER DIED FROM
DAVE WALKER'S SHOTGUN.

1481
00:59:18,155 --> 00:59:19,557
DO YOU REALLY BELIEVE THAT?

1482
00:59:19,590 --> 00:59:21,625
FIGURE IT OUT, NAN.
WALKER ADMITTED

1483
00:59:21,658 --> 00:59:23,628
CHASING HIS WIFE AND CAL
INTO THE SWAMPS AFTER

1484
00:59:23,662 --> 00:59:25,430
- HE FOUND THEM TOGETHER.
- A COW?

1485
00:59:25,463 --> 00:59:26,965
SHOT THEM, AND HE TRIED
TO PLACE THE BLAME

1486
00:59:26,998 --> 00:59:28,900
ON SAWYER'S D.T.'S.

1487
00:59:28,933 --> 00:59:30,635
- IF SAWYER TOLD
OF SEEING...
- HMM.

1488
00:59:30,668 --> 00:59:33,037
PURPLE GIRAFFES
WITH POLKA-DOT TAILS--

1489
00:59:33,070 --> 00:59:34,905
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.
BACK UP A BIT, THERE.

1490
00:59:34,938 --> 00:59:37,075
THERE'S ONE ARGUMENT
AGAINST THAT, STEVE.

1491
00:59:37,108 --> 00:59:38,677
DAVE WALKER WASN'T
THE KIND OF A MAN

1492
00:59:38,710 --> 00:59:41,545
- TO HANG HIMSELF--
- NAH, HE'S A BLADE MAN

1493
00:59:41,578 --> 00:59:44,815
I TALKED WITH DAVE
LESS THAN AN HOUR BEFORE
HE KILLED HIMSELF.

1494
00:59:44,848 --> 00:59:47,152
- MAYBE THAT'S WHY.
- THAT MAN WAS IN
A STATE OF SHOCK.

1495
00:59:47,185 --> 00:59:48,853
- I'VE SEEN--
- [JOEL YAWNS]

1496
00:59:48,887 --> 00:59:50,822
- MMM. HI.
- BUT I'VE NEVER SEEN

1497
00:59:50,855 --> 00:59:51,888
ANYTHING TO COMPARE
WITH THE HORROR

1498
00:59:51,922 --> 00:59:54,525
AND THE FEAR
IN WALKER'S EYES.

1499
00:59:54,558 --> 00:59:55,927
WELL, HE REALIZED
WHAT HE'D DONE.

1500
00:59:55,960 --> 00:59:57,962
HE KILLED TWO PEOPLE.
ONE HIS WIFE.

1501
00:59:57,995 --> 00:59:59,730
- ONE HIS COW.
- NOW LOOK, DOC.

1502
00:59:59,763 --> 01:00:01,432
NAN AND I WERE
ALL OVER THAT SWAMP.

1503
01:00:01,465 --> 01:00:04,002
- AND EACH OTHER.
- WHY DIDN'T THESE MONSTERS
ATTACK US?

1504
01:00:04,035 --> 01:00:05,737
I'VE BEEN THINKING
ABOUT THAT.

1505
01:00:05,770 --> 01:00:07,272
THEY'RE PROBABLY
NIGHT CREATURES.

1506
01:00:07,305 --> 01:00:09,407
THEY CAN'T STAND THE LIGHT.
THEY STAY DOWN NEAR THE BOTTOM

1507
01:00:09,440 --> 01:00:11,508
- DURING THE DAY.
- OH, LIKE COMEDIANS.

1508
01:00:11,542 --> 01:00:13,477
A SMALL CHARGE
WOULD STUN THEM.

1509
01:00:13,510 --> 01:00:15,112
BRING 'EM TO THE SURFACE.

1510
01:00:15,145 --> 01:00:16,747
CAN'T BUY IT, DOC.

1511
01:00:16,780 --> 01:00:19,117
YOU'RE-- PIG-HEADED,
STEVE BENTON.

1512
01:00:19,150 --> 01:00:20,485
NO, IT'S STEVE-HEADED
PIG BENTON.

1513
01:00:20,518 --> 01:00:22,520
STUBBORN AND PIG-HEADED.

1514
01:00:22,553 --> 01:00:23,955
YOU JUST DON'T
UNDERSTAND, DO YOU?

1515
01:00:23,988 --> 01:00:25,088
I'M A JERK.

1516
01:00:25,122 --> 01:00:26,523
OH, I'LL GO
MAKE SOME COFFEE.

1517
01:00:26,557 --> 01:00:29,127
SHE DOESN'T UNDERSTAND.
I'M A JERK, SIR.

1518
01:00:29,160 --> 01:00:32,563
YEAH. SURE. WHATEVER.

1519
01:00:32,597 --> 01:00:34,998
- GOOD NIGHT, DOC.
- GOOD NIGHT, JERK.

1520
01:00:37,435 --> 01:00:39,937
I'M A BEAVER, AND THIS IS
THE VIEW FROM MY LIVING ROOM.

1521
01:00:39,970 --> 01:00:41,272
ENJOY.

1522
01:00:41,305 --> 01:00:43,107
♪ HOME ♪

1523
01:00:45,042 --> 01:00:47,212
HI, I'M BACK.

1524
01:00:48,813 --> 01:00:51,515
♪ O SOLE MIO ♪

1525
01:00:57,555 --> 01:00:59,557
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

1526
01:01:02,460 --> 01:01:06,263
OH. GOT ANY
DEEP-WOODS OFF THERE?

1527
01:01:06,297 --> 01:01:09,067
WELL, AT LEAST WE'S PADDLIN'
IN THE SAME DIRECTION NOW.

1528
01:01:10,802 --> 01:01:12,137
RIGHT OVER THERE
IN THEM REEDS--

1529
01:01:12,170 --> 01:01:16,040
IS WHERE MY DADDY
MET MY PAPPY.

1530
01:01:16,073 --> 01:01:17,775
I WISH WE COULD SEE HIM.
YOU CAN'T PERSONALIZE

1531
01:01:17,808 --> 01:01:20,210
A MONSTER LIKE THIS.

1532
01:01:23,247 --> 01:01:24,682
OOH, HEY, LOOK,
A LOT OF GOLF BALLS

1533
01:01:24,715 --> 01:01:26,117
DOWN IN THERE.

1534
01:01:28,618 --> 01:01:30,488
JUST CAN'T FIGURE
OLD DAVE OUT.

1535
01:01:30,522 --> 01:01:31,988
WELP, HE'S A COMPLEX FELLOW.

1536
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:34,892
--CAL, WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

1537
01:01:34,925 --> 01:01:36,160
I HADN'T THOUGHT OF THAT.

1538
01:01:36,193 --> 01:01:38,295
I HADN'T THOUGHT OF
ANYTHING, EVER.

1539
01:01:38,328 --> 01:01:40,063
RIGHT OVER THERE
IN THEM REEDS--

1540
01:01:40,097 --> 01:01:42,433
- YEAH, JERRY REED. REX REED.
- MM-HMM. MM-HMM.

1541
01:01:42,467 --> 01:01:44,735
- WILLIS REED. DONNA REED.
- MM-HMM. MM-HMM.

1542
01:01:44,768 --> 01:01:46,837
- LOU REED. REED RICHARDS.
- MM-HMM. MM-HMM.

1543
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:48,907
- ROBERT REED.
- MMM.

1544
01:01:48,940 --> 01:01:51,508
THESE GUYS ARE
AGGRESSIVELY INCOMPETENT.

1545
01:01:55,245 --> 01:01:57,248
DON'T LOOK NOW.
I THINK THEY FOUND JIMMY HOFFA!

1546
01:01:57,282 --> 01:01:59,217
[SERVO GROANS]

1547
01:02:00,785 --> 01:02:02,620
OH, TAKE ME

1548
01:02:02,653 --> 01:02:04,755
TO THE SWEET
MUSHROOM PALACE,

1549
01:02:04,788 --> 01:02:07,258
- MY FRIEND, BOOZE.
- BOY, THIS IS SURE A HOT ONE.

1550
01:02:07,292 --> 01:02:09,360
THAT'S THE SUNTAN LOTION!

1551
01:02:09,393 --> 01:02:11,095
[CROW COUGHS, GASPS]

1552
01:02:11,128 --> 01:02:13,965
YOU EVER FEEL LIKE CRYIN',
AND YOU DON'T KNOW WHY?

1553
01:02:16,167 --> 01:02:18,302
- SURE IS FUNNY.
- HUH?

1554
01:02:18,335 --> 01:02:20,170
GALLAGHER.
SAID HE SURE IS FUNNY.

1555
01:02:20,203 --> 01:02:21,905
- NOTICED ANYTHING?
- LIKE WHAT?

1556
01:02:21,938 --> 01:02:23,842
WE'VE BEEN PRODDIN'
AROUND HERE ALL MORNING.

1557
01:02:23,875 --> 01:02:26,177
- HUH?
- WE AIN'T RUN ACROSS
A SINGLE GATOR.

1558
01:02:26,210 --> 01:02:28,178
AND I DON'T HAVE
NO PANTS ON.

1559
01:02:28,212 --> 01:02:31,215
BY RIGHTS, THIS POOL SHOULD BE
CRAWLING WITH 'EM.

1560
01:02:31,248 --> 01:02:32,950
I'M CRAWLING
WITH SOMETHING.

1561
01:02:32,983 --> 01:02:36,087
- SURE FUNNY.
- THAT IS FUNNY.

1562
01:02:36,120 --> 01:02:37,622
I DON'T LIKE
THE LOOKS OF THIS.

1563
01:02:37,655 --> 01:02:38,957
AND I DON'T LIKE
THE LOOKS OF YOU!

1564
01:02:38,990 --> 01:02:40,892
- LET'S CALL IT A DAY.
- WELL NOW, WAIT A MINUTE.

1565
01:02:40,925 --> 01:02:42,960
WE AIN'T POLED THE GATOR HOLES
AROUND THE BEND YET.

1566
01:02:42,993 --> 01:02:44,828
DO WHAT YOU WANNA DO, BOY.

1567
01:02:44,862 --> 01:02:47,965
JUST GET ME ON DRY LAND!
AND RIGHT QUICK!

1568
01:02:47,998 --> 01:02:49,533
- DON'T EVER
GET OFF THE BOAT.
- ALL RIGHT, NO USE

1569
01:02:49,567 --> 01:02:52,068
GETTING ALL HEAD UP.
LET'S GO.

1570
01:02:54,105 --> 01:02:57,375
ALL RIGHT, NOW MAKE THAT
MOTORBOAT NOISE AGAIN, CALEB.

1571
01:02:57,408 --> 01:02:59,277
♪♪ [SERVO MIMICS MOTOR]

1572
01:02:59,310 --> 01:03:01,378
[MUTTERS]

1573
01:03:01,412 --> 01:03:03,013
BY THE WAY, CAN I BORROW
YOUR FONDUE SET?

1574
01:03:03,047 --> 01:03:04,648
SARAH AND HER MOTHER
ARE COMING OVER LATER.

1575
01:03:04,682 --> 01:03:06,117
OH.

1576
01:03:06,150 --> 01:03:08,652
OUT HERE,
IT'S A WILD GOOSE CHASE.

1577
01:03:15,358 --> 01:03:16,460
HEY.

1578
01:03:16,493 --> 01:03:19,097
- [SCREAMS]
- OOH. YEAH.

1579
01:03:19,130 --> 01:03:21,965
THIS IS THE MOST FANTASTIC
UNDERSEA ODYSSEY EVER FILMED!

1580
01:03:21,998 --> 01:03:23,800
UH-HUH.

1581
01:03:23,835 --> 01:03:26,337
OH, I JUST LOVE
UNDERWATER LOVE SCENES.

1582
01:03:29,673 --> 01:03:31,908
OH, GREAT, THE LEECHES
HAVE A LITTLE FORT.

1583
01:03:31,942 --> 01:03:35,245
HELLO, BONES.
SORRY ABOUT THE FORMALITY.

1584
01:03:40,652 --> 01:03:42,052
THIS ONE'S A KEEPER.

1585
01:03:42,085 --> 01:03:43,687
WE EAT TONIGHT.

1586
01:03:43,720 --> 01:03:45,255
HEY STEVE,
YOU EVER FEEL LIKE

1587
01:03:45,288 --> 01:03:49,193
YOU'RE IN
A GARY LARSON CARTOON?

1588
01:03:49,227 --> 01:03:52,297
LEECHES ARE JUST
GUYS IN FANCY PONCHOS.

1589
01:03:52,330 --> 01:03:54,198
THEY'RE NOT LEECHES,
THEY'RE SCIENTOLOGISTS!

1590
01:03:54,232 --> 01:03:56,333
THEY'RE SEARS PONCHOS.

1591
01:03:56,367 --> 01:03:58,702
OH LOOK, JIM HENSON'S
CRACKER BABIES.

1592
01:03:58,735 --> 01:03:59,803
HUH?

1593
01:03:59,837 --> 01:04:02,673
[SCREAMS]

1594
01:04:02,707 --> 01:04:05,843
HEY, KEEP IT DOWN.
WE'RE TRYING TO SLEEP OVER HERE.

1595
01:04:05,877 --> 01:04:07,245
WE STILL HAVEN'T
GOT IT RIGHT.

1596
01:04:07,278 --> 01:04:08,678
WE DON'T WANT
HILLBILLIES WITH GOOD TASTE.

1597
01:04:08,712 --> 01:04:10,080
WE WANT HILLBILLIES
THAT TASTE GOOD.

1598
01:04:10,113 --> 01:04:11,848
HILLBILLY RED.

1599
01:04:18,388 --> 01:04:21,692
HONEY, WAKE UP.
THEY'RE BACK.

1600
01:04:21,725 --> 01:04:24,195
WOW. HE IS GONNA HAVE
ONE IMMENSE HICKEY.

1601
01:04:24,228 --> 01:04:25,597
HE'S GONNA HAVE TO WEAR
A TURTLENECK.

1602
01:04:25,630 --> 01:04:28,933
- MM-HMM.
- [LIZ SCREAMS]

1603
01:04:28,967 --> 01:04:31,835
HOW AM I GONNA
EXPLAIN THIS TO MY HUSBAND?

1604
01:04:31,868 --> 01:04:34,072
NOW THIS SIDE.

1605
01:04:44,682 --> 01:04:45,983
OH, PUPPIES.

1606
01:04:46,017 --> 01:04:48,385
♪ YOU...
YOU'VE BLOWN IT ALL ♪

1607
01:04:48,418 --> 01:04:50,253
♪ SKY-HIGH ♪

1608
01:04:50,287 --> 01:04:51,588
YOU KNOW,
IF I DIDN'T KNOW BETTER,

1609
01:04:51,622 --> 01:04:53,190
I'D SAY WE'RE IN
THE DULLEST PART OF THE MOVIE

1610
01:04:53,223 --> 01:04:54,625
- RIGHT NOW.
- PROBABLY.

1611
01:04:54,658 --> 01:04:56,793
♪ WITHOUT A REASON WHY ♪

1612
01:04:56,827 --> 01:04:58,997
♪ THERE'S A MADMAN
ACROSS THE WATER THERE ♪

1613
01:04:59,030 --> 01:05:00,430
OOH, BUZZ BOMB REFERENCE.

1614
01:05:00,463 --> 01:05:01,932
HEY, BAB, YOU KNOW,
I'M THINKING ABOUT

1615
01:05:01,965 --> 01:05:03,733
GETTIN' ME ONE OF THEM
SPEEDO SWIMSUITS,

1616
01:05:03,767 --> 01:05:07,137
- WHAT DO YOU THINK?
- LOOK GOOD, SWEET PETE.

1617
01:05:07,170 --> 01:05:08,572
CAN WE BREAK FOR A SNACK?

1618
01:05:08,605 --> 01:05:11,608
DAVE WOULD'VE WANTED US TO.

1619
01:05:11,642 --> 01:05:14,512
WE'RE UNDER HERE.
YOU CAN'T SEE US.

1620
01:05:14,545 --> 01:05:16,747
♪♪ [MIMICS UNDERWATER VOICE]

1621
01:05:16,780 --> 01:05:18,348
WHOOP, THINK MY PANTS
ARE SHRINKING.

1622
01:05:18,382 --> 01:05:21,285
[SERVO CHUCKLES, COUGHS]

1623
01:05:21,318 --> 01:05:23,320
WE'RE ALL CLEAR!

1624
01:05:23,353 --> 01:05:25,255
EH.

1625
01:05:25,288 --> 01:05:27,558
IT'S CLEAR OVER HERE.

1626
01:05:27,592 --> 01:05:31,095
I'LL BE THE JUDGE OF THAT.

1627
01:05:31,128 --> 01:05:33,330
- [DOG BARKS]
- HEY, THAT'S NOT A SCENT!

1628
01:05:33,363 --> 01:05:34,765
THAT'S THE OTHER DOG
YOU'RE SNIFFIN'!

1629
01:05:34,798 --> 01:05:36,567
THESE DOGS HAVE BEEN
TRACKIN' EACH OTHER!

1630
01:05:36,600 --> 01:05:39,170
LIBERTY! CHECKERS! NO.

1631
01:05:39,203 --> 01:05:40,938
IS IT HOT HERE,
OR IS IT JUST ME?

1632
01:05:40,972 --> 01:05:45,475
- AAH.
- [FRANKENSTEIN GROWL]

1633
01:05:45,508 --> 01:05:47,143
WHOA. OUTTA HERE.

1634
01:05:47,177 --> 01:05:48,445
FEETS, DON'T FEEL ME NOW.

1635
01:05:48,478 --> 01:05:50,715
STAY TOGETHER, CHEEKS.

1636
01:05:53,717 --> 01:05:57,020
WELL, THIS SCENE ISN'T
PANNING OUT LIKE I'D HOPED.

1637
01:05:57,053 --> 01:05:59,690
HEY, SPREAD OUT.
THIS IS MY SPOT.

1638
01:05:59,723 --> 01:06:02,927
[DOG HOWLS]

1639
01:06:05,028 --> 01:06:06,930
YEAH, YEAH, WE KNOW.
YOU SAW THE BEST MINDS

1640
01:06:06,963 --> 01:06:08,965
OF YOUR GENERATION
DESTROYED BY MADNESS.

1641
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:10,500
- WE KNOW.
- ALL RIGHT,
LET'S KEEP MOVING.

1642
01:06:10,533 --> 01:06:12,268
TO ANOTHER FILM?

1643
01:06:12,302 --> 01:06:14,405
CHAMP! REX! SPOT! OTTO!

1644
01:06:14,438 --> 01:06:16,607
[SERVO MUTTERS]

1645
01:06:21,845 --> 01:06:24,582
I CLAIM THIS-A LAND
FOR THE QUEEN OF SPAIN.

1646
01:06:25,817 --> 01:06:27,352
♪ WOULDN'T YOU
LIKE TO GLIDE ♪

1647
01:06:27,385 --> 01:06:30,287
♪ IN MY BEAUTIFUL BALLOON ♪

1648
01:06:30,320 --> 01:06:32,255
YEAH, THEY'RE REALLY
HAVING TROUBLE WITH THIS SCENE.

1649
01:06:32,288 --> 01:06:33,923
YEAH. YEAH.
IT'S GOING NOWHERE.

1650
01:06:33,957 --> 01:06:35,258
- WELL, WE CAN'T DO
ANY MORE TONIGHT.
- [JOEL MUTTERS]

1651
01:06:35,292 --> 01:06:36,593
MIGHT AS WELL START BACK.

1652
01:06:36,627 --> 01:06:38,762
RECKON AIN'T NO USE
HURRYING NOW, MR. BENTON.

1653
01:06:38,795 --> 01:06:41,565
- OH, YOU RECKON, DO YOU?
- IF REED AND OLD SAM WAS ALIVE,

1654
01:06:41,598 --> 01:06:44,468
THEY'D'VE LET US KNOW
WITH A HOLLER OR SOMETHING.

1655
01:06:44,502 --> 01:06:45,903
YEAH, IT KIND OF
LOOKS THAT WAY.

1656
01:06:45,937 --> 01:06:47,237
- YEP.
- YOU FELLAS

1657
01:06:47,270 --> 01:06:48,938
NOTICE ANYTHING
ABOUT THIS LAKE?

1658
01:06:48,972 --> 01:06:50,473
- UH, IT'S WET?
- I MEAN, THE GATORS.

1659
01:06:50,507 --> 01:06:52,510
- WHAT ABOUT 'EM?
- THEY AIN'T HERE.

1660
01:06:52,543 --> 01:06:54,612
PIECE OF WATER THIS SIZE
USUALLY HAS MAYBE

1661
01:06:54,645 --> 01:06:57,080
50, 60 BIG ONES AROUND.

1662
01:06:57,113 --> 01:06:58,415
WHOLE LOT OF LITTLE ONES.

1663
01:06:58,448 --> 01:07:00,985
WELL, I COULD GO FOR
A PIECE OF WATER MYSELF.

1664
01:07:01,018 --> 01:07:03,053
WELL, MAYBE OUR TORCH'LL
SCARE THEM AWAY.

1665
01:07:03,087 --> 01:07:06,223
NOTHING SCARES THE GATORS.
NOTHING.

1666
01:07:06,257 --> 01:07:07,625
ANIMAL OR HUMAN.

1667
01:07:07,658 --> 01:07:10,693
BUT KEEP IN MIND,
I'M INTENSELY STUPID.

1668
01:07:10,728 --> 01:07:12,630
WELL, WE MIGHT AS WELL
GET OUT OF HERE.

1669
01:07:12,663 --> 01:07:15,632
T.G.I.F., HUH, FELLAS?

1670
01:07:15,665 --> 01:07:17,935
MM, HMONG FOLK ART.

1671
01:07:17,968 --> 01:07:21,605
WE'RE WORRIED ABOUT
YOUR NOT-SMOKING, CHAD.

1672
01:07:21,638 --> 01:07:22,940
YOU GOT SOMETHING
IN MIND, STEVE?

1673
01:07:22,973 --> 01:07:24,608
YEAH, REMEMBER
BUB'S DADDY GUM?

1674
01:07:24,642 --> 01:07:26,777
I'M THINKING OF WHAT EVAN SAID
ABOUT THE GATORS.

1675
01:07:26,810 --> 01:07:28,112
YEAH, HE SAID, "AAH!"

1676
01:07:28,145 --> 01:07:30,915
HE SAID, "ANIMAL OR HUMAN."

1677
01:07:30,948 --> 01:07:32,282
AND YET,
SOMETHING MADE THEM LEAVE.

1678
01:07:32,315 --> 01:07:33,617
- MAYBE A...
- COURT ORDER?

1679
01:07:33,650 --> 01:07:35,652
A MINERAL CONTAMINATION.

1680
01:07:35,685 --> 01:07:37,253
I GUESS I'D BETTER RUN
SOME WATER SAMPLES.

1681
01:07:37,287 --> 01:07:39,223
- THROUGH MYSELF.
- COME ON, YOU TWO.
DRINK YOUR COFFEE.

1682
01:07:39,257 --> 01:07:41,825
WELL, I WAS JUST TALKIN'
ABOUT COFFEE A MOMENT AGO.

1683
01:07:41,858 --> 01:07:43,893
AND SUPPOSING
THERE IS NO CONTAMINATION?

1684
01:07:43,927 --> 01:07:45,262
WELL, WE'LL ADD SOME.

1685
01:07:45,295 --> 01:07:47,532
THEN I'LL SEND OVER
TO EASTPORT FOR A DIVING RIG

1686
01:07:47,565 --> 01:07:49,233
AND GO DOWN TO LOOK FOR
THIS MONSTER OF YOURS.

1687
01:07:49,267 --> 01:07:51,368
NO, STEVE,
DON'T EVEN JOKE LIKE THAT.

1688
01:07:51,402 --> 01:07:52,703
YOU DON'T KNOW
HOW TO TELL 'EM.

1689
01:07:52,737 --> 01:07:54,037
I'M NOT JOKING, NAN.
I HAD SOME TRAINING

1690
01:07:54,070 --> 01:07:55,505
WITH AN AQUALUNG
WHILE I WAS IN THE NAVY.

1691
01:07:55,538 --> 01:07:57,307
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS "AQUALUNG"]

1692
01:07:57,340 --> 01:07:59,042
- ♪♪ [JOEL DRUMS KNEES]
- TWO BODIES WE KNOW FOR SURE

1693
01:07:59,075 --> 01:08:00,677
ARE DOWN THERE.
MAYBE FOUR.

1694
01:08:00,710 --> 01:08:02,178
THEY'VE GOT TO BE
BROUGHT UP.

1695
01:08:02,212 --> 01:08:03,813
WAIT A MINUTE.

1696
01:08:03,847 --> 01:08:06,117
THERE ARE NO ALLIGATORS IN
THAT PART OF THE SWAMP, RIGHT?

1697
01:08:06,150 --> 01:08:07,885
- SO?
- NO SIGN OF ANY

1698
01:08:07,918 --> 01:08:09,753
- FISH OR SNAKES?
- SO?

1699
01:08:09,787 --> 01:08:11,888
NO. WHAT ARE YOU
GETTING AT, DOC?

1700
01:08:11,922 --> 01:08:13,390
WOULD YOU PASS THE JELLY?

1701
01:08:13,423 --> 01:08:15,025
WELL, THERE GOES
YOUR ARGUMENT ABOUT
SETTING OFF

1702
01:08:15,058 --> 01:08:16,727
A DYNAMITE CHARGE
UNDERWATER.

1703
01:08:16,760 --> 01:08:18,828
- HMM.
- IT'D BRING THE BODIES
TO THE SURFACE.

1704
01:08:18,862 --> 01:08:20,530
- HMM.
- GET IT OUT OF YOUR MIND, DOC.

1705
01:08:20,563 --> 01:08:22,132
I'M NOT USING
ANY EXPLOSIVES

1706
01:08:22,165 --> 01:08:23,733
AS LONG AS
THERE'S ANOTHER WAY.

1707
01:08:23,767 --> 01:08:25,268
- WHY MUST YOU BE SUCH A--
- STUD.

1708
01:08:25,302 --> 01:08:27,103
- STUBBORN PIG-HEAD?
- EXACTLY.

1709
01:08:27,137 --> 01:08:29,473
- THAT TOO.
- I'LL TELL YOU WHY.

1710
01:08:29,507 --> 01:08:30,773
NUMBER ONE,
THERE'S BOUND TO BE

1711
01:08:30,808 --> 01:08:32,042
SOME AQUARIUM LIFE
IN THAT SECTION

1712
01:08:32,075 --> 01:08:34,110
EVEN IF THE BIGGER FORMS
HAVE ABANDONED IT.

1713
01:08:34,145 --> 01:08:35,512
GET IT?

1714
01:08:35,545 --> 01:08:38,015
AN EXPLOSION UNDERWATER WOULD
DESTROY EVERY LIVING THING

1715
01:08:38,048 --> 01:08:39,750
AND WRECK WHAT NATURE
TOOK YEARS TO BUILD UP.

1716
01:08:39,783 --> 01:08:41,252
YEARS OF IN-BREEDING,
DESTROYED.

1717
01:08:41,285 --> 01:08:42,385
NUMBER TWO,
I'M PAID TO PREVENT

1718
01:08:42,418 --> 01:08:44,053
THE USELESS SLAUGHTER
OF WILDLIFE.

1719
01:08:44,087 --> 01:08:45,522
UH, WHAT WAS ONE AGAIN?

1720
01:08:45,555 --> 01:08:47,692
NUMBER THREE,
I'D HAVE TO GET AUTHORIZATION.

1721
01:08:47,725 --> 01:08:49,560
TO GET THAT AUTHORIZATION,
I'D HAVE TO COME UP WITH

1722
01:08:49,593 --> 01:08:51,995
- A HECK OF A REASON.
- NUMBER FOUR, YOU'RE A JERK.

1723
01:08:52,028 --> 01:08:53,463
SATISFIED?

1724
01:08:53,497 --> 01:08:55,332
NO, I COULD USE MORE COFFEE.

1725
01:08:55,365 --> 01:08:57,233
FINISH UP, DAD.
I WANNA GO HOME.

1726
01:08:57,267 --> 01:09:00,103
- I THOUGHT YOU WERE HOME.
- STEVE...

1727
01:09:00,137 --> 01:09:01,772
HOW LONG WOULD IT TAKE
TO GET THIS DIVING EQUIPMENT

1728
01:09:01,805 --> 01:09:04,040
- FROM EASTPORT?
- IS THIS A RIDDLE?

1729
01:09:04,073 --> 01:09:06,477
A COUPLE OF DAYS, WHY?

1730
01:09:06,510 --> 01:09:07,545
OH, NOTHING.

1731
01:09:07,578 --> 01:09:08,778
THEN WHY BRING IT UP?

1732
01:09:08,812 --> 01:09:11,315
I WAS DELIBERATELY
WASTING YOUR TIME.

1733
01:09:11,348 --> 01:09:13,150
TAKE CARE OF YOURSELF,
STEVE.

1734
01:09:13,183 --> 01:09:16,087
OR SOMEONE MIGHT
STAB YOU IN YOUR SLEEP.

1735
01:09:16,120 --> 01:09:20,023
WAIT, I DON'T LIVE HERE,
WHAT THE-- OH.

1736
01:09:20,057 --> 01:09:21,458
WELL, HERE'S HOPIN'.

1737
01:09:21,492 --> 01:09:23,160
DAD.

1738
01:09:23,193 --> 01:09:25,295
CAN'T YOU THROW
THE DYNAMITE IN FROM HERE?

1739
01:09:25,328 --> 01:09:26,997
NO, I WANNA GET IT OUT
INTO THE MIDDLE.

1740
01:09:27,030 --> 01:09:28,232
IN THE DEEPEST PART.

1741
01:09:28,265 --> 01:09:30,800
'CAUSE PEPPERIDGE FARM
REMEMBERS.

1742
01:09:30,833 --> 01:09:33,070
NOW IT'S TIME FOR
TROUT-BLASTING IN AMERICA

1743
01:09:33,103 --> 01:09:34,605
WITH YOUR HOST,
DICK BRAUTIGAN.

1744
01:09:34,638 --> 01:09:36,107
♪ OH-DEE-DOH,
I'M A DANGER ♪

1745
01:09:36,140 --> 01:09:37,642
♪ TO MYSELF AND OTHERS ♪

1746
01:09:37,675 --> 01:09:39,543
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

1747
01:09:42,680 --> 01:09:45,515
WELL, GOODBYE FOREVER.
I MEAN, DAD.

1748
01:09:45,548 --> 01:09:48,185
DAD.

1749
01:09:48,218 --> 01:09:49,453
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

1750
01:09:49,487 --> 01:09:51,955
OH, I'M DRAINED.

1751
01:09:51,988 --> 01:09:53,223
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1752
01:09:53,257 --> 01:09:55,858
MMM. THAT FIRST SAUNA.
BIG TIME.

1753
01:09:59,497 --> 01:10:02,800
LOOKS LIKE
THE CAVE OF DR. CALAMARI.

1754
01:10:02,833 --> 01:10:05,602
KIND OF FUN.

1755
01:10:05,635 --> 01:10:07,972
I KNOW, I KNOW,
YOU GET USED TO IT.

1756
01:10:10,942 --> 01:10:12,475
♪ LOVE IN AN ELEVATOR ♪

1757
01:10:12,508 --> 01:10:14,512
♪ LIVIN' IT UP
WHILE I'M GOING DOWN ♪

1758
01:10:18,515 --> 01:10:21,818
EH, SUCK ON THAT,
YOU DARN SON OF A...

1759
01:10:21,852 --> 01:10:25,122
I PRAY I WAS ADOPTED.

1760
01:10:25,155 --> 01:10:26,857
WELL, HONEY, I THREW IT
UNDER THE BOAT,

1761
01:10:26,890 --> 01:10:29,225
WHERE IT WOULD DO
THE MOST-- AAH!

1762
01:10:31,562 --> 01:10:33,297
PARKING AT THE SWAMP
SURE IS CONVENIENT.

1763
01:10:33,330 --> 01:10:35,432
- YEP.
- HE'S AT IT AGAIN.

1764
01:10:35,465 --> 01:10:37,467
ISN'T HE? SAD, REALLY.

1765
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:40,570
WELL, LET'S GO GET HIM.

1766
01:10:42,272 --> 01:10:44,975
GEE.

1767
01:10:45,008 --> 01:10:47,343
COME ON, DUMMY.
BACK TO THE HOME WITH YA.

1768
01:10:49,913 --> 01:10:52,617
LOOK, NOW SHE'S WEARING
HER BEAUTY OPERATOR OUTFIT.

1769
01:10:54,418 --> 01:10:55,953
IT SHOULD GO ANY MINUTE.

1770
01:10:55,987 --> 01:10:57,120
YEAH, RIGHT.

1771
01:10:57,153 --> 01:10:59,390
WHAT A LOON.

1772
01:10:59,423 --> 01:11:01,758
I'M NOT A LOON.

1773
01:11:01,792 --> 01:11:04,528
NEXT WEEK, ON MACGYVER.

1774
01:11:04,562 --> 01:11:06,163
EVERYBODY INTO THE POOL!

1775
01:11:06,197 --> 01:11:07,397
[ALL GUFFAW]

1776
01:11:07,430 --> 01:11:10,467
WELL, GEE, IT WORKED
ON THE GOPHERS IN MY YARD.

1777
01:11:14,103 --> 01:11:15,838
[ALL]
HUH?

1778
01:11:19,275 --> 01:11:21,178
[SERVO MAKES BOBBING SOUND]

1779
01:11:23,380 --> 01:11:25,948
WHAT'S THAT?

1780
01:11:25,983 --> 01:11:27,417
HEY, THAT'S BOB THERE!

1781
01:11:27,450 --> 01:11:29,920
- OH.
- GET IT? BOB!

1782
01:11:29,953 --> 01:11:32,488
SORRY.

1783
01:11:32,522 --> 01:11:33,757
WELL, LET ME TELL YOU,
IF I COULD TAKE

1784
01:11:33,790 --> 01:11:35,658
ONE DUMB THING BACK
IN MY LIFE.

1785
01:11:35,692 --> 01:11:36,960
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

1786
01:11:36,993 --> 01:11:39,463
SAY, ARE THOSE
BUGLE BOY JEANS?

1787
01:11:42,598 --> 01:11:44,200
- HMM.
- UH.

1788
01:11:44,233 --> 01:11:47,037
- I'VE SEEN BETTER.
- MM-HMM.

1789
01:11:47,070 --> 01:11:49,238
JUST CAN'T FIGURE IT OUT.

1790
01:11:55,878 --> 01:11:57,147
[ALL LAUGH]

1791
01:11:57,180 --> 01:11:58,748
BRING IT DOWN THERE, GYPSY.

1792
01:11:58,782 --> 01:11:59,883
YOU KNOW, FELLAS.

1793
01:11:59,917 --> 01:12:02,252
IT'S NOT EASY
BEING A SOCIAL MISFIT

1794
01:12:02,285 --> 01:12:04,622
AND THEN GETTING
THE ADDED RESPONSIBILITY

1795
01:12:04,655 --> 01:12:07,692
OF DRAGNETTIN' THE SWAMP
FOR MISSIN' TOWNSFOLK,

1796
01:12:07,725 --> 01:12:09,258
AND I CAN'T EVEN
BUTTON MY OWN SHIRT!

1797
01:12:09,292 --> 01:12:11,062
I HEAR YA, GUNTHER.

1798
01:12:11,095 --> 01:12:13,463
OH, ISN'T IT AMAZING
HOW WE INFERIOR TYPES

1799
01:12:13,497 --> 01:12:15,598
KEEP GETTING ASKED
TO DO DANGEROUS WORK

1800
01:12:15,632 --> 01:12:17,902
THAT SHOULD GO TO MEN
MORE STABLE THAN US.

1801
01:12:17,935 --> 01:12:20,270
REALLY IS A MIRACLE.
HOOTER?

1802
01:12:20,303 --> 01:12:23,240
UH, DUH, YUP.
WHAT NEXT?

1803
01:12:23,273 --> 01:12:24,608
WHAT DID HE SAY, SILAS?

1804
01:12:24,642 --> 01:12:26,343
WELL, I THINK WHAT
OUR BRIGHT YOUNG FRIEND'S

1805
01:12:26,377 --> 01:12:27,945
TRYING TO SAY HERE IS

1806
01:12:27,978 --> 01:12:29,447
THE REASON
WE THREE GOOFUSES

1807
01:12:29,480 --> 01:12:31,182
ARE ASKED TO DO
THESE HAZARDOUS TASKS

1808
01:12:31,215 --> 01:12:33,683
OUTSIDE THE PERIMETER
OF NORMAL SOCIETY'S RATIONALE

1809
01:12:33,717 --> 01:12:36,487
IS WE'RE A DANGER
TO OURSELVES AND OTHERS.

1810
01:12:36,520 --> 01:12:38,155
OH, KINDA REMINDS ME

1811
01:12:38,188 --> 01:12:40,457
OF DARWIN'S THEORY
OF NATURAL SELECTION.

1812
01:12:40,490 --> 01:12:43,393
YEAH, IF YOU'RE DUMB,
YOU DIE!

1813
01:12:43,427 --> 01:12:46,197
THAT'S, I SAY,
THAT'S A RICH ONE THERE,
HOOTER.

1814
01:12:46,230 --> 01:12:47,998
[ALL]
WHOO.

1815
01:12:48,032 --> 01:12:50,233
♪ OH, I'M A DANGER
TO MYSELF AND OTHERS ♪

1816
01:12:50,267 --> 01:12:52,068
♪ MY COUSINS ARE
AS CLOSE AS BROTHERS ♪

1817
01:12:52,102 --> 01:12:55,172
♪ I STAY OUT IN THE RAIN
ALL THE TIME ♪

1818
01:12:55,205 --> 01:12:57,440
♪ HE'S A DANGER
TO HIMSELF AND OTHERS ♪

1819
01:12:57,473 --> 01:12:59,443
♪ ONLY LIKES SHOWS
WITH SALLY STRUTHERS ♪

1820
01:12:59,477 --> 01:13:01,612
♪ I CAN'T EVEN THINK
OF A WORD THAT RHYMES ♪

1821
01:13:01,645 --> 01:13:03,013
[JOEL AND SERVO]
BUT YOU DID.

1822
01:13:03,047 --> 01:13:04,515
HOW DUMB ARE YOU, UNCLE DAD?

1823
01:13:04,548 --> 01:13:06,583
WELL, PRETTY DUMB,
THAT'S FOR SURE.

1824
01:13:06,617 --> 01:13:08,185
HOW DUMB ARE YOU, UNCLE DAD?

1825
01:13:08,218 --> 01:13:09,987
WELL, THIS PIPE'S
FILLED WITH MANURE.

1826
01:13:10,020 --> 01:13:11,822
[ALL]
♪ WE'RE A DANGER
TO OURSELVES AND OTHERS ♪

1827
01:13:11,855 --> 01:13:13,857
♪ SCREW THE EARTH
AND STEAL OUR MOTHERS ♪

1828
01:13:13,890 --> 01:13:16,960
♪ LEAVE US IN THE WOODS,
AND WE'RE JUST FINE ♪

1829
01:13:16,993 --> 01:13:19,128
♪ WE'RE A DANGER
TO OURSELVES AND OTHERS ♪

1830
01:13:19,162 --> 01:13:20,997
♪ GOOD LIVESTOCK
WITH BETTER LOVERS ♪

1831
01:13:21,030 --> 01:13:23,867
♪ HUNTIN' LEECHES,
WHAT WE CALL A GOOD TIME ♪

1832
01:13:23,900 --> 01:13:27,237
[ALL]
WHOO!

1833
01:13:27,270 --> 01:13:28,872
OH, BOY.

1834
01:13:28,905 --> 01:13:31,675
I'D LIKE TO SHAKE HANDS WITH
ANY GIANT LEECHES AFTER THAT.

1835
01:13:31,708 --> 01:13:33,877
WHAT, THE DYNAMITE,
OR THAT CRAPPY SONG?

1836
01:13:33,910 --> 01:13:35,778
- ♪♪ [GUITAR OUTRO]
- WOO-HOO!

1837
01:13:42,987 --> 01:13:46,257
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

1838
01:13:46,290 --> 01:13:47,657
GOOD STUFF.

1839
01:13:47,690 --> 01:13:49,325
WALKER'S WIFE.
WHY DIDN'T HER BODY

1840
01:13:49,358 --> 01:13:50,660
COME TO THE SURFACE?

1841
01:13:50,693 --> 01:13:52,062
- HMM.
- I DON'T KNOW.

1842
01:13:52,095 --> 01:13:54,698
MAYBE HER SHOES WERE
TOO HEAVY.

1843
01:13:54,732 --> 01:13:58,002
I THINK I'D BETTER WALK OVER
TO THE CORONER'S OFFICE.

1844
01:13:58,035 --> 01:13:59,903
WHAT'S THE MATTER,
MR. BENTON?

1845
01:13:59,937 --> 01:14:02,705
FEEL AWKWARD ABOUT ARRESTING
MY FATHER IN HIS OWN HOME?

1846
01:14:02,738 --> 01:14:04,207
- NO.
- I WARNED HIM I'D ARREST HIM

1847
01:14:04,240 --> 01:14:07,443
- IF HE USED DYNAMITE.
- NICE OF YOU.

1848
01:14:07,477 --> 01:14:09,547
JEEZ. I DON'T GET WOMEN.

1849
01:14:09,580 --> 01:14:13,050
WELL, THE AUTOPSY SHOULD
BE OVER BY NOW.

1850
01:14:13,083 --> 01:14:15,985
OH, HI. YOU GOT THE RIGHT
TO REMAIN SILENT--

1851
01:14:16,018 --> 01:14:17,553
I THOUGHT YOU'D BE HERE.

1852
01:14:17,587 --> 01:14:18,855
I WAS WISHING YOU WEREN'T.

1853
01:14:18,888 --> 01:14:21,325
I DON'T WANT TO HAVE
TO DO THIS, DOCTOR.

1854
01:14:21,358 --> 01:14:22,860
DO WE HAVE TIME FOR
A CUP OF COFFEE FIRST?

1855
01:14:22,893 --> 01:14:25,062
- [SERVO LAUGHS]
- SURE.

1856
01:14:25,095 --> 01:14:26,397
DO YOU MIND, HONEY?

1857
01:14:26,430 --> 01:14:27,663
NO, I'LL MAKE
SOME SANDWICHES.

1858
01:14:27,697 --> 01:14:29,567
I'LL MAKE
SOME COFFEE SANDWICHES.

1859
01:14:29,600 --> 01:14:31,835
SHE'S GOING TO HIS PLACE
TO MAKE SANDWICHES.

1860
01:14:35,905 --> 01:14:37,908
AHH. YOU KNOW,
LIQUOR MAKES EVERYTHING RIGHT.

1861
01:14:37,942 --> 01:14:40,310
- FROM THE LIQUOR COUNCIL.
- IT'S WHAT YOUR BODY'S
THIRSTY FOR.

1862
01:14:40,343 --> 01:14:41,678
--FOR ALL THE GOOD
IT WILL DO NOW.

1863
01:14:41,712 --> 01:14:43,247
LET ME SHOW YOU
MY APPENDIX SCAR.

1864
01:14:43,280 --> 01:14:46,250
--HELP,
HE DIDN'T SHOOT CAL.

1865
01:14:46,283 --> 01:14:47,617
UH, I'LL GET MORE COFFEE.

1866
01:14:47,683 --> 01:14:49,720
I'VE JUST COME FROM
THE AUTOPSIES.

1867
01:14:49,753 --> 01:14:52,022
KOVIS TRIED TO KEEP ME OUT.

1868
01:14:52,055 --> 01:14:53,423
I TOLD HIM
I'D RAISE A STINK

1869
01:14:53,457 --> 01:14:54,725
THEY'D SMELL
ALL THE WAY TO THE CAPITOL

1870
01:14:54,758 --> 01:14:56,025
- IF HE DID.
- OH, DON'T DOUBT THAT.

1871
01:14:56,058 --> 01:14:57,862
WELL THEN,
WHAT KILLED HIM, DOC?

1872
01:14:57,895 --> 01:14:59,630
- NOT DROWNING.
- NO.

1873
01:14:59,663 --> 01:15:01,398
AND CAL WASN'T SHOT, EITHER.

1874
01:15:01,432 --> 01:15:03,067
AND HE WASN'T
BEAT UP BY CLOWNS.

1875
01:15:03,100 --> 01:15:05,435
EVERY DROP OF BLOOD WAS
DRAINED OUT OF THEIR BODIES.

1876
01:15:05,468 --> 01:15:07,070
TURNS OUT I DID IT.
FUNNY, HUH?

1877
01:15:07,103 --> 01:15:09,172
AND THEY HAD WOUNDS
ON THEIR THROATS.

1878
01:15:09,205 --> 01:15:10,740
SUCTION WOUNDS.

1879
01:15:10,773 --> 01:15:12,042
LIKE A...

1880
01:15:12,075 --> 01:15:13,577
LIKE A GIGANTIC LEECH
MIGHT MAKE.

1881
01:15:13,610 --> 01:15:14,978
OR A HOOVER.

1882
01:15:15,012 --> 01:15:16,580
AND THERE'S SOMETHING
EVEN MORE INCREDIBLE.

1883
01:15:16,613 --> 01:15:19,015
- I'M SKIPPY THE CHIMP.
- --WAS SUPPOSED
TO HAVE BEEN KILLED

1884
01:15:19,048 --> 01:15:20,683
SEVERAL DAYS AGO.

1885
01:15:20,717 --> 01:15:23,687
SAM AND REED HAVE BEEN MISSING
A MATTER OF 48 HOURS.

1886
01:15:23,720 --> 01:15:25,055
- MM-HMM.
- ALL THREE OF THEM,

1887
01:15:25,088 --> 01:15:26,523
AS FAR AS WE KNOW,
WERE IN THAT LAKE

1888
01:15:26,557 --> 01:15:29,025
A MINIMUM OF TWO DAYS.

1889
01:15:29,058 --> 01:15:31,495
NOW, I'D STAKE
MY REPUTATION AS A DOCTOR--

1890
01:15:31,528 --> 01:15:33,197
- OR WHAT'S LEFT OF IT--
- THAT CAL HADN'T BEEN DEAD

1891
01:15:33,230 --> 01:15:35,798
MORE THAN TWO OR THREE HOURS
WHEN WE FOUND HIM.

1892
01:15:35,832 --> 01:15:38,002
AND THE OTHER TWO
LESS THAN THAT.

1893
01:15:38,035 --> 01:15:40,870
FIRST STAGE RIGOR MORTIS
STARTED IN DURING THE AUTOPSY.

1894
01:15:40,903 --> 01:15:43,840
BUT HOW COULD THAT BE, DOC?
IT'S IMPOSSIBLE.

1895
01:15:43,873 --> 01:15:45,475
THE CORONER WILL CONFIRM IT.

1896
01:15:45,508 --> 01:15:46,710
CIGARETTE?

1897
01:15:46,743 --> 01:15:48,412
WHATEVER KILLED THEM
IS STILL IN THAT LAKE,

1898
01:15:48,445 --> 01:15:50,913
AND IT'S GONNA TAKE MORE THAN
DYNAMITE TO GET IT OUT.

1899
01:15:50,947 --> 01:15:52,182
[CROW AS STRANGELOVE]
I THINK WE SHOULD USE

1900
01:15:52,215 --> 01:15:53,483
MY NEW A-BOMB!

1901
01:15:53,517 --> 01:15:55,052
CONCUSSION FROM THOSE CHARGES
WOULD'VE KILLED

1902
01:15:55,085 --> 01:15:56,520
A FULL-GROWN WHALE.

1903
01:15:56,553 --> 01:15:58,455
THAT'S IT! WE'LL PUT
A FULL-GROWN WHALE DOWN THERE!

1904
01:15:58,488 --> 01:16:01,090
- OH.
- THAT EXPLAINS HOW
CAL AND THE OTHERS LIVED

1905
01:16:01,123 --> 01:16:03,260
AFTER THEY WERE
SUPPOSED TO BE DROWNED.

1906
01:16:03,293 --> 01:16:04,628
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1907
01:16:04,662 --> 01:16:07,430
WELL, THIS WHOLE REGION IS
RIDDLED BY CAVES AND CAVERNS

1908
01:16:07,463 --> 01:16:09,900
CUT OUT BY THE OCEAN
THOUSANDS OF YEARS AGO.

1909
01:16:09,933 --> 01:16:11,702
- I LOVE RIDDLES.
- IF THERE ARE CAVES
ABOVE THE WATER,

1910
01:16:11,735 --> 01:16:14,003
THEN THERE MUST BE CAVES
UNDER THE WATER.

1911
01:16:14,037 --> 01:16:16,238
- GO ON.
- NO. MAKE ME.

1912
01:16:16,273 --> 01:16:17,807
MIKE AND I HAD
A CHANCE TO FOOL AROUND

1913
01:16:17,840 --> 01:16:19,108
WITH SOME FROGMAN EQUIPMENT

1914
01:16:19,142 --> 01:16:20,643
CAPTURED FROM
THE ITALIAN NAVY.

1915
01:16:20,677 --> 01:16:23,080
YEAH, THEN WE WENT ON
TO SHOWGIRL COSTUMES.

1916
01:16:23,113 --> 01:16:24,848
--THROUGH A SUNKEN TRANSPORT
OFF SALERNO.

1917
01:16:24,882 --> 01:16:26,350
BUTTER COOKIE?

1918
01:16:26,383 --> 01:16:28,552
WHEN THE SHIP WENT DOWN,
IT TRAPPED SOME AIR

1919
01:16:28,585 --> 01:16:30,387
- INSIDE THE HULL.
- MM-HMM.

1920
01:16:30,420 --> 01:16:32,855
WE'D GO DOWN. COME UP
INSIDE THE OFFICER'S LOUNGE.

1921
01:16:32,888 --> 01:16:34,490
TAKE OFF
OUR FACE MASKS AND...

1922
01:16:34,523 --> 01:16:36,493
SORT OF SAMPLE SOME OF
THE BOTTLES FLOATING AROUND.

1923
01:16:36,527 --> 01:16:38,095
YEAH, THAT'S NICE--
IS THERE A POINT TO YOUR STORY?

1924
01:16:38,128 --> 01:16:39,428
--DRIVING US CRAZY
TRYING TO FIGURE OUT

1925
01:16:39,462 --> 01:16:42,098
HOW WE WERE
GETTING THE STUFF.

1926
01:16:42,132 --> 01:16:44,300
YOU MEAN YOU THINK
THAT THERE'S AN OUTPOCKET

1927
01:16:44,333 --> 01:16:46,068
OR A CAVE
UNDERNEATH THE LAKE?

1928
01:16:46,102 --> 01:16:47,972
RIGHT. GOTTA BE.
HOW ELSE COULD THOSE PEOPLE

1929
01:16:48,005 --> 01:16:49,673
HAVE LIVED DOWN THERE?
NOT ONLY THAT,

1930
01:16:49,707 --> 01:16:51,642
IT EXPLAINS HOW
WHATEVER IT IS DOWN THERE

1931
01:16:51,675 --> 01:16:53,143
LIVED THROUGH
THE CONCUSSION.

1932
01:16:53,177 --> 01:16:55,045
- STEVE.
- [AS SHATNER] STEVE!

1933
01:16:55,078 --> 01:16:56,380
SPOCK!

1934
01:16:56,413 --> 01:16:58,815
- LIZ WALKER.
- I STOOD UP TOO FAST, WHOO.

1935
01:16:58,848 --> 01:17:01,518
SHE MIGHT STILL
BE DOWN THERE.

1936
01:17:01,552 --> 01:17:03,020
ALIVE.

1937
01:17:03,053 --> 01:17:04,320
BUT MUSTY.

1938
01:17:04,353 --> 01:17:05,788
EW.

1939
01:17:05,822 --> 01:17:09,325
WHAT?

1940
01:17:09,358 --> 01:17:10,927
- [SERVO SIGHS]
- [LIZ SIGHS]

1941
01:17:10,960 --> 01:17:13,197
CALGON, TAKE ME AWAY.

1942
01:17:13,230 --> 01:17:16,600
- I THINK IT DID.
- YEAH.

1943
01:17:16,633 --> 01:17:18,102
THIS MUST BE
THE SWIMSUIT EDITION

1944
01:17:18,135 --> 01:17:19,535
OF LEECH ILLUSTRATED.

1945
01:17:19,568 --> 01:17:21,003
NO... NO.

1946
01:17:21,037 --> 01:17:22,638
- NO!
- LICK OF PAINT,
SOME NICE CURTAINS,

1947
01:17:22,672 --> 01:17:24,540
THIS PLACE WOULD BE OKAY.

1948
01:17:24,573 --> 01:17:28,645
MEANWHILE,
ON HOLLYWOOD BOULEVARD.

1949
01:17:28,678 --> 01:17:31,682
WE NOW RETURN TO HAWAII 5-0.

1950
01:17:31,715 --> 01:17:34,117
LOOKS LIKE THE CAMERAMAN
CAN'T FIND THE CAST.

1951
01:17:34,150 --> 01:17:35,985
OH.

1952
01:17:36,018 --> 01:17:39,288
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

1953
01:17:39,322 --> 01:17:41,358
SKIPPER!

1954
01:17:41,392 --> 01:17:43,127
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

1955
01:17:43,160 --> 01:17:46,430
[CROW AS JULIA CHILD]
NOW YOU BRING THE SWAMP
TO A ROLLING BOIL.

1956
01:17:47,663 --> 01:17:49,700
HEY, IT LOOKS LIKE
THE DAD FROM FLIPPER.

1957
01:17:49,733 --> 01:17:54,370
[CROW MIMICS DOLPHIN]

1958
01:17:54,403 --> 01:17:55,972
HEY. LOOKS LIKE
THE WHOLE TOWN

1959
01:17:56,005 --> 01:17:57,340
CAME OUT
TO WATCH HIM SUIT UP.

1960
01:17:57,373 --> 01:17:58,708
WELL, THEY DON'T HAVE
A MOVIE HOUSE.

1961
01:17:58,742 --> 01:18:00,677
YEAH, YUP.

1962
01:18:00,710 --> 01:18:01,945
- COMFORTABLE?
- YEAH.

1963
01:18:01,978 --> 01:18:03,480
MAKE A NICE LIVING.

1964
01:18:03,513 --> 01:18:05,315
YOU SURE YOU DON'T WANT ME
TO GO DOWN BEFORE YOU, MIKE?

1965
01:18:05,348 --> 01:18:07,283
YOU HAVEN'T HAD
ONE OF THESE THINGS ON
FOR A LONG TIME,

1966
01:18:07,317 --> 01:18:09,618
WHILE ME, EVERY OTHER DAY
I'VE BEEN PLAYING FISH.

1967
01:18:09,652 --> 01:18:11,388
REMEMBER THE FIRST TIME
WE HAD ONE OF THESE ON?

1968
01:18:11,422 --> 01:18:14,657
NOT THIS TIME, MIKE.

1969
01:18:14,690 --> 01:18:17,127
YOU ASK ME, THEY OUGHTA
HAVE THEIR HEADS EXAMINED.

1970
01:18:17,160 --> 01:18:18,728
GIANT LEECHES.

1971
01:18:18,762 --> 01:18:20,463
[ALL GROAN]

1972
01:18:20,497 --> 01:18:22,032
I'M WILLIN'
TO BET A MONTH'S PAY

1973
01:18:22,065 --> 01:18:24,367
THEY DON'T COME UP WITH
NOTHIN' MORE THAN EXCUSES.

1974
01:18:24,400 --> 01:18:26,368
- WHOA, I COULD USE TEN BUCKS!
- IT'S CRAZY.

1975
01:18:26,403 --> 01:18:29,438
HIM, THE DOC,
AND HIS BRIDE TOO.

1976
01:18:29,472 --> 01:18:32,142
JUST WAIT'LL I GET ON
THE PHONE TO THE CAPITOL.

1977
01:18:32,175 --> 01:18:34,043
I'LL GUARANTEE
SOMEBODY'LL WISH THEY KEPT

1978
01:18:34,077 --> 01:18:36,078
THEIR NOSE OUT OF
OTHER PEOPLE'S BUSINESS.

1979
01:18:36,112 --> 01:18:40,083
- AND OUT OF MY
UNDERWEAR DRAWER.
- I GUARANTEE IT.

1980
01:18:40,117 --> 01:18:43,620
[ALL GROAN]

1981
01:18:43,653 --> 01:18:46,355
FOOL.

1982
01:18:46,388 --> 01:18:49,425
- STEVE.
- I'M GOING WITH YOU.

1983
01:18:49,492 --> 01:18:51,193
BE CAREFUL, PLEASE?

1984
01:18:51,227 --> 01:18:53,062
DON'T WORRY. MIKE'LL BE READY
IF ANYTHING GOES WRONG.

1985
01:18:53,097 --> 01:18:54,530
DON'T WORRY ABOUT STEVE.

1986
01:18:54,563 --> 01:18:56,098
NOW, IF HE WERE
GOING AFTER A BARRACUDA,

1987
01:18:56,132 --> 01:18:57,633
YOU MIGHT HAVE
A TINY BIT TO WORRY ABOUT.

1988
01:18:57,667 --> 01:18:59,635
♪♪ [ALL HUM
HEART'S "BARRACUDA"]

1989
01:19:03,673 --> 01:19:05,675
SURE YOU DON'T
WANT SOME COFFEE?

1990
01:19:09,378 --> 01:19:11,313
GOODBYE, GILLIGAN.
GOODBYE, SKIPPER.

1991
01:19:11,347 --> 01:19:14,852
SURE HOPE THOSE
COCONUT AIR TANKS HOLD OUT.

1992
01:19:14,885 --> 01:19:17,520
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

1993
01:19:20,290 --> 01:19:21,725
THEY'RE DEAD-- GOODBYE!

1994
01:19:21,758 --> 01:19:23,960
THEY DON'T HAVE A CHANCE--
SO SEE YOU LATER, GOOD LUCK!

1995
01:19:23,993 --> 01:19:26,428
WE'LL DRAG 'EM OUT TOMORROW--
GOOD LUCK OUT THERE!

1996
01:19:26,463 --> 01:19:29,800
IT'S THE STAR OF
RALPH BELLAMY, RALPH BELLAMY,
RALPH BELLAMY.

1997
01:19:33,403 --> 01:19:35,572
I SEE LONDON, I SEE FRANCE,

1998
01:19:35,605 --> 01:19:39,175
I SEE LITTLE STEVE-O'S
UNDERPANTS.

1999
01:19:39,208 --> 01:19:40,843
[LIZ SIGHS]

2000
01:19:40,877 --> 01:19:42,912
GOOD NEWS.
WE'RE HAVING FISH TODAY.

2001
01:19:42,945 --> 01:19:44,580
[CROW CHUCKLES]
FISH.

2002
01:19:44,613 --> 01:19:46,248
EH, SORRY.

2003
01:19:46,282 --> 01:19:47,550
NO, NO, PLEASE STAY AWAY.

2004
01:19:47,583 --> 01:19:49,085
NO. YOU SUCKED
THE LIFE OUT OF ME.

2005
01:19:49,118 --> 01:19:50,787
I HAVE NOTHING MORE TO GIVE.

2006
01:19:50,820 --> 01:19:53,157
PLEASE.

2007
01:19:53,190 --> 01:19:55,658
NOT EXACTLY INVITING, IS IT?

2008
01:19:55,692 --> 01:19:57,260
- YEAH.
- NO, IT SURE ISN'T.

2009
01:19:57,293 --> 01:20:00,997
HEY, LET'S STAY IN THE BOAT
AND JUST EAT SANDWICHES, OKAY?

2010
01:20:01,030 --> 01:20:04,067
AND UH, LOOK, I'LL SPIT
IN MY OWN MASK THIS TIME.

2011
01:20:06,435 --> 01:20:09,505
RIGHT TO THE BOTTOM.
WELP, LET'S TRY THE OTHER ONE.

2012
01:20:09,538 --> 01:20:11,007
OH JEEZ, IT'S NOT DEEP.

2013
01:20:11,040 --> 01:20:13,943
IT WAS FILMED IN
CORMAN'S SWIMMING POOL.

2014
01:20:13,977 --> 01:20:17,113
EH. DARN FOOL KIDS.

2015
01:20:19,348 --> 01:20:21,417
OH, WATCH THAT END.
BOONK! OH, SORRY.

2016
01:20:21,450 --> 01:20:23,353
IT'LL STOP ANYTHING
UP TO A TIGER SHARK.

2017
01:20:23,387 --> 01:20:25,655
BUT YOU GOTTA HIT.
MISSES DON'T COUNT.

2018
01:20:25,688 --> 01:20:27,257
NOW, ANYTHING GOES WRONG,

2019
01:20:27,290 --> 01:20:29,158
JUST YANK ON THE LINE.
I'LL BE DOWN IN A HURRY.

2020
01:20:29,192 --> 01:20:31,995
AND YANK REAL HARD.
I MIGHT HAVE THE RADIO ON.

2021
01:20:36,567 --> 01:20:39,835
[ALL GROAN]

2022
01:20:50,180 --> 01:20:54,083
♪ I'D LIKE TO BE
UNDER THE SEA ♪

2023
01:20:54,117 --> 01:20:56,518
...OUTSIDE,
THERE'S A LITTLE MAILBOX

2024
01:20:56,553 --> 01:20:57,853
THAT READS "I AM A LEECH."

2025
01:20:57,887 --> 01:21:02,358
THIS MUST BE HIS PLACE. AH.

2026
01:21:02,392 --> 01:21:05,128
WHAT A JERK.

2027
01:21:11,033 --> 01:21:14,370
♪♪ [ALL HUM]

2028
01:21:16,405 --> 01:21:18,242
YANK! YANK YANK!

2029
01:21:18,275 --> 01:21:20,110
HELLO! IS THIS THING ON?

2030
01:21:20,143 --> 01:21:22,778
OH! BIG THING! OH!

2031
01:21:22,812 --> 01:21:25,382
HUH?

2032
01:21:26,683 --> 01:21:29,920
AAH! UPPIES! I WANT UPPIES!

2033
01:21:29,953 --> 01:21:33,523
[SERVO SOBS]

2034
01:21:33,557 --> 01:21:35,025
EH, GOT A BIG ONE.

2035
01:21:35,058 --> 01:21:36,627
[CROW GASPS]

2036
01:21:36,660 --> 01:21:38,262
COULD YOU HAND ME
ANOTHER SPEAR?

2037
01:21:38,295 --> 01:21:39,662
YOU SURE YOU DON'T
WANT ME TO GO DOWN

2038
01:21:39,695 --> 01:21:41,330
AND FINISH IT OFF
FOR YOU, STEVE?

2039
01:21:41,363 --> 01:21:42,832
NO THANKS, MIKE, I--

2040
01:21:42,865 --> 01:21:45,768
I THINK I HURT IT
PRETTY BAD.

2041
01:21:45,802 --> 01:21:49,638
CAREFUL NOW. ANYTHING HURT
IS TEN TIMES AS DANGEROUS.

2042
01:21:49,672 --> 01:21:52,075
YEAH, I'LL FIGURE THAT OUT
UNDERWATER, FRIEND.

2043
01:21:52,108 --> 01:21:53,810
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

2044
01:21:53,843 --> 01:21:56,045
HE WOUNDED IT!
HE'S GONNA FINISH IT OFF!

2045
01:21:56,078 --> 01:21:57,580
I'D START THE GRILL
IF I WERE YOU!

2046
01:21:57,613 --> 01:22:00,117
DOES HE HAVE
TO GO UNDER AGAIN?

2047
01:22:00,150 --> 01:22:01,652
HE'S GOT TO
MAKE SURE, HONEY.

2048
01:22:01,685 --> 01:22:03,353
THIS IS WHAT
THERAPY'S ALL ABOUT.

2049
01:22:03,387 --> 01:22:05,622
WHERE COULD IT HAVE
COME FROM?

2050
01:22:05,655 --> 01:22:07,523
I WISH I KNEW.

2051
01:22:07,557 --> 01:22:09,025
WE'LL HAVE TO
MAKE SOME TESTS.

2052
01:22:09,058 --> 01:22:10,593
- LIKE S.A.T.?
- MAYBE THE PROXIMITY

2053
01:22:10,627 --> 01:22:12,762
OF CAPE CANAVERAL'S
GOT SOMETHING TO DO WITH IT.

2054
01:22:12,795 --> 01:22:14,230
THE ROCKET STATION?

2055
01:22:14,263 --> 01:22:15,732
WELL, THEY USE
ATOMIC ENERGY--

2056
01:22:15,765 --> 01:22:17,667
- ♪♪ [JOEL HUMS]
- --IN THE FIRST STAGES
OF LAUNCHES.

2057
01:22:17,700 --> 01:22:19,768
NOT ALL OF THEM
HAVE BEEN SUCCESSFUL.

2058
01:22:19,802 --> 01:22:21,437
YOU THINK THAT
IF SOME ANIMAL LIFE

2059
01:22:21,470 --> 01:22:23,540
WAS CLOSE BY,
NOT CLOSE ENOUGH TO BE KILLED

2060
01:22:23,573 --> 01:22:25,575
BUT CLOSE ENOUGH
TO FEEL THE EFFECTS

2061
01:22:25,608 --> 01:22:27,110
OF A RADIOACTIVE
ENERGY THAT'S--

2062
01:22:27,143 --> 01:22:29,178
A MUTATION.
A TYPE OF GIGANTISM

2063
01:22:29,212 --> 01:22:31,547
- [SERVO SNORES]
- --OF SOME COMMON ANIMAL.

2064
01:22:31,580 --> 01:22:34,650
SPEAKING OF COMMON ANIMALS,
HOW'RE YOU AND STEVE GETTING ON?

2065
01:22:34,683 --> 01:22:36,887
--I HOPE HE'S ABLE
TO BRING IT UP.

2066
01:22:36,920 --> 01:22:39,522
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
EH, I COULD BRING MY LUNCH UP.

2067
01:22:39,555 --> 01:22:43,360
LET'S GO SEE WHAT
STEVE THE JERK IS UP TO.

2068
01:22:43,393 --> 01:22:45,828
HEY, I CAN'T SEE.

2069
01:22:51,768 --> 01:22:54,170
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2070
01:22:54,203 --> 01:22:56,707
OH, FEEL LIKE
I'M IN HEF'S GROTTO.

2071
01:22:56,740 --> 01:22:58,775
[SIGHS]

2072
01:22:58,808 --> 01:23:01,643
[SERVO SIGHS]

2073
01:23:01,678 --> 01:23:03,112
OH, THERE SHE GOES.

2074
01:23:03,145 --> 01:23:05,882
BUH-BYE NOW, BUH-BYE.

2075
01:23:10,520 --> 01:23:12,888
OH, I'VE SEEN THIS
IN DEMENTIA-13.

2076
01:23:16,458 --> 01:23:17,927
OH. I SEE LONDON,
I SEE FRANCE--

2077
01:23:17,960 --> 01:23:19,595
HEY, COME ON. SHE'S DEAD.

2078
01:23:19,628 --> 01:23:21,497
- OH, SORRY.
- GAH...

2079
01:23:24,300 --> 01:23:26,535
HEY. GOOD JOB.
THEY FOUND HER.

2080
01:23:31,640 --> 01:23:33,242
[SERVO GRUNTS]

2081
01:23:33,275 --> 01:23:35,178
I'LL JUST PUT HER
ON THE STRINGER.

2082
01:23:35,212 --> 01:23:38,415
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]
- THAT CAN'T BE LIZ.

2083
01:23:38,448 --> 01:23:39,782
HMM.

2084
01:23:39,815 --> 01:23:41,683
I DON'T REMEMBER
LIZ BEING DEAD

2085
01:23:41,718 --> 01:23:43,118
WITH GIANT HICKEYS
ON HER CHEEKS.

2086
01:23:43,152 --> 01:23:44,787
WHAT-- WHAT COULD'VE
DONE THAT?

2087
01:23:44,820 --> 01:23:48,425
- STEVEN TYLER?
- LOOK AT HER FACE.

2088
01:23:48,458 --> 01:23:49,692
MAYBE.

2089
01:23:52,162 --> 01:23:53,863
THE ABYSS.

2090
01:23:53,897 --> 01:23:57,000
OH, OWIE, I JUST GOT
SUCH A BIG BLOOD BLISTER.

2091
01:23:57,033 --> 01:23:58,635
AND IT'S SO NICE AND JUICY.

2092
01:23:58,668 --> 01:24:00,903
AND I FEEL SO NAUGHTY.

2093
01:24:00,937 --> 01:24:03,973
AND-- OH, I SURE HOPE
A BIG LEECH DOESN'T COME AROUND.

2094
01:24:04,007 --> 01:24:06,275
OH, THAT WOULD BE
JUST TERRIBLE.

2095
01:24:06,308 --> 01:24:08,412
SUCKER!
WAIT A MINUTE, THAT'S ME.

2096
01:24:08,445 --> 01:24:10,313
[CROW LAUGHS]
AH, I DIG ME.

2097
01:24:14,150 --> 01:24:16,652
NOW IT LOOKS LIKE
A SEA TURTLE.

2098
01:24:22,658 --> 01:24:24,627
UH, THINK LIZ'LL BE OKAY
ON THE BOAT ALONE?

2099
01:24:24,660 --> 01:24:26,062
HMM.

2100
01:24:26,095 --> 01:24:28,297
STEVE WAS IN TROUBLE.
I HAD TO ACT FAST.

2101
01:24:28,330 --> 01:24:30,633
I HAD TO GET MY SONS
IN THE SERIES.

2102
01:24:34,670 --> 01:24:37,707
[SERVO AS JOE PESCI]
HEY MA, I'D LIKE TO BORROW
YOUR BUTCHER KNIFE, OKAY?

2103
01:24:39,608 --> 01:24:41,177
WAIT A MINUTE,
ARE THERE TWO OF THEM NOW?

2104
01:24:41,210 --> 01:24:43,045
- WHAT'S GOING ON?
- OH, IT'S A MESS.

2105
01:24:43,078 --> 01:24:45,515
IT'S CONFUSING.

2106
01:24:45,548 --> 01:24:48,083
DOESN'T MATTER, HUH?

2107
01:24:48,117 --> 01:24:50,120
W-- DON'T TOUCH HIM!
THAT'S MY PAL!

2108
01:24:50,153 --> 01:24:51,487
HE'S TRYING TO STAB
THE CAMERAMAN.

2109
01:24:51,520 --> 01:24:53,222
DID YOU SEE THAT?

2110
01:24:53,255 --> 01:24:55,225
[SERVO STRAINS]
NOT ME, YOU IDIOT!

2111
01:24:55,258 --> 01:24:58,093
THE LEECH! THE LEECH!

2112
01:24:58,127 --> 01:24:59,395
YEAH, SO THERE'S
TWO OF YOU, HUH?

2113
01:24:59,428 --> 01:25:00,763
COME ON, COME ON,
I'VE SUCKED BLOOD

2114
01:25:00,797 --> 01:25:03,733
FROM GUYS BIGGER THAN
THE BOTH OF YOU.

2115
01:25:03,767 --> 01:25:05,468
THEN IT WAS
BACK TO THE LODGE

2116
01:25:05,502 --> 01:25:07,803
FOR A SMOOTH CANADIAN CLUB.

2117
01:25:09,738 --> 01:25:12,408
WHA-- OH, IT'S A MANATEE.

2118
01:25:12,442 --> 01:25:15,412
[ALL GROAN]

2119
01:25:15,445 --> 01:25:17,113
I'VE BEEN AROUND HERE FOR YEARS.
I NEVER SAW NOTHING

2120
01:25:17,147 --> 01:25:19,748
- LIKE THAT BEFORE.
- I'M A PROFESSIONAL SKEPTIC.

2121
01:25:21,985 --> 01:25:24,820
TOMMY BARTLETT INVITES YOU
TO RID THE WILD LEECH.

2122
01:25:26,923 --> 01:25:29,625
COME ON, LET'S ALL RIDE 'EM!
HOO-HOO!

2123
01:25:29,658 --> 01:25:33,128
DAVID JANSSEN.

2124
01:25:33,162 --> 01:25:34,597
MIGHT WANNA
MEASURE AND WEIGH HER.

2125
01:25:34,630 --> 01:25:37,533
I THINK SHE'S A KEEPER.
SHE'S A RECORD, ALL RIGHT.

2126
01:25:40,803 --> 01:25:43,573
WELP, THERE SURE GOES LIZ.

2127
01:25:48,343 --> 01:25:50,847
WELL, HAVE TO GO DIVING
MORE OFTEN.

2128
01:25:52,782 --> 01:25:54,383
- I'LL CARRY HER.
- NO, I'LL CARRY HER.

2129
01:25:54,417 --> 01:25:57,420
- NO, I'LL CARRY HER.
- I'LL GET HER.

2130
01:25:57,453 --> 01:26:00,557
AND WHAT OF EMILY
AND HER LOVE FOR CHAD?

2131
01:26:00,590 --> 01:26:02,925
AND WHAT OF THE HAIR
ON CHUCK'S CHEST?

2132
01:26:02,958 --> 01:26:05,462
STAY TUNED.

2133
01:26:05,495 --> 01:26:08,532
EPILOGUE.

2134
01:26:12,802 --> 01:26:14,570
- MM-HMM.
- WELL, WHO'S THIS GUY?

2135
01:26:14,603 --> 01:26:16,672
A ROADIE FROM SEA HUNT?

2136
01:26:16,705 --> 01:26:20,677
- JEEZ.
- WISH I WOULD'VE
THOUGHT OF THAT.

2137
01:26:20,710 --> 01:26:22,512
♪♪ [ALL WHISTLE]

2138
01:26:22,545 --> 01:26:24,813
- [JOEL SIGHS]
- OKAY, ANY TIME NOW!

2139
01:26:24,847 --> 01:26:26,248
- GEE, I HOPE THAT'S RIGHT.
- --THEY MUST BE

2140
01:26:26,282 --> 01:26:28,450
LICKING THEIR WOUNDS.

2141
01:26:28,483 --> 01:26:30,353
YOU SURE YOU USED ENOUGH STUFF
TO DO THE JOB, MIKE?

2142
01:26:30,387 --> 01:26:32,388
I USED A HUNDRED STICKS
TO 40%.

2143
01:26:32,422 --> 01:26:35,023
- ENOUGH TO KILL ALL OF US.
- BLOW THE BOTTOM RIGHT OUT.

2144
01:26:35,057 --> 01:26:37,227
- ALL RIGHT, LET 'ER GO.
- OH NO.

2145
01:26:37,260 --> 01:26:39,028
I'VE DONE ENOUGH
OF YOUR DIRTY WORK.

2146
01:26:39,062 --> 01:26:41,530
HELP YOURSELF.

2147
01:26:41,563 --> 01:26:43,498
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
NO, I'M NOT FALLING
FOR THAT OLD ONE.

2148
01:26:43,532 --> 01:26:45,668
HMM, NOW LET'S SEE.
HOW DO YOU WORK THIS OLD THING?

2149
01:26:45,702 --> 01:26:47,803
LET'S SEE IF MY MEMORY
SERVES ME CORRECTLY.

2150
01:26:47,837 --> 01:26:49,338
- OH YEAH.
- [BOTS MIMIC PLUNGER]

2151
01:26:49,372 --> 01:26:52,308
- OH! OOH.
- I BLEW MY BLANKET CLEAN OFF!

2152
01:26:55,143 --> 01:26:59,048
[ALL]
ONE.

2153
01:26:59,082 --> 01:27:00,850
WELL, I'LL BE HOG-TIED

2154
01:27:00,883 --> 01:27:04,220
IN A BACK ROOM
WITH A BIG OLD--

2155
01:27:04,253 --> 01:27:06,322
- FISH-FRY TONIGHT.
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]

2156
01:27:06,355 --> 01:27:09,825
[ALL]
TWO.

2157
01:27:09,858 --> 01:27:11,660
I'D HOPED THAT'D BE
MORE EXCITING.

2158
01:27:11,693 --> 01:27:13,195
WELL, LET'S GO BACK
TO TOWN-- OH, WAIT.

2159
01:27:13,228 --> 01:27:14,630
THERE IS NO TOWN.

2160
01:27:14,663 --> 01:27:16,332
UH, WHO'S HUNGRY
FOR BLOOD SAUSAGE?

2161
01:27:16,365 --> 01:27:20,337
JUST KIDDING! HA-HAH!

2162
01:27:20,370 --> 01:27:21,670
WELL, I'M GONNA MISS 'EM.

2163
01:27:21,703 --> 01:27:25,073
NOW WE GOTTA GO HANG OUT
AT THE GROCERY STORE AGAIN.

2164
01:27:25,107 --> 01:27:26,742
[SERVO SIGHS]

2165
01:27:26,775 --> 01:27:29,478
I FEEL EMPTY.
KIND OF A LET-DOWN, REALLY.

2166
01:27:32,048 --> 01:27:36,285
BUT FOR THE LOWLY DETONATOR.

2167
01:27:36,318 --> 01:27:38,922
- OH!
- LOST YOUR HEAD.
- MY HEAD! MY HEAD, GRAB IT!

2168
01:27:38,955 --> 01:27:42,158
GOTTA FIGURE OUT
HOW THIS GONNA END HERE.

2169
01:27:52,468 --> 01:27:53,770
THERE WE GO.
THERE WE GO, YEAH.

2170
01:27:53,803 --> 01:27:55,872
JOEL, I CAN'T HELP
BUT FEEL THAT THAT FILM

2171
01:27:55,905 --> 01:27:57,240
WAS FLAWED IN CERTAIN WAYS.

2172
01:27:57,273 --> 01:27:58,708
WELL, WHAT DO YOU MEAN
BY THAT?

2173
01:27:58,742 --> 01:28:00,677
WELL, I DON'T KNOW.
I GUESS I JUST FELT THAT

2174
01:28:00,710 --> 01:28:01,943
CORMAN FAILED TO DELIVER

2175
01:28:01,978 --> 01:28:05,247
ON CONCEPTS AND IDEAS
PROMISED US IN FILMS LIKE

2176
01:28:05,280 --> 01:28:06,815
VIKING WOMEN
AND THE SEA SERPENT.

2177
01:28:06,848 --> 01:28:08,517
YOU KNOW, I HAD PROBLEMS
WITH IT TOO, JOEL.

2178
01:28:08,550 --> 01:28:10,487
LIKE, I CAN'T FIGURE OUT
IF THOSE LEECH CREATURES

2179
01:28:10,520 --> 01:28:12,755
WERE SMART
OR JUST BIG DUMB MONSTERS.

2180
01:28:12,788 --> 01:28:15,558
WELL, THEY WERE SMART ENOUGH
TO TAKE HOSTAGES.

2181
01:28:15,592 --> 01:28:17,093
YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.

2182
01:28:17,127 --> 01:28:19,562
AND WHEN THAT DRUNK POACHER
FINGERED ONE OF THE LEECHES,

2183
01:28:19,595 --> 01:28:21,797
THEY SENT A CONTRACT MAN
OUT TO KILL HIM.

2184
01:28:21,830 --> 01:28:23,700
YEAH, YOU KNOW, SO MAYBE

2185
01:28:23,733 --> 01:28:25,602
THEY KEPT EVERYBODY BUSY
AT THE SWAMP

2186
01:28:25,635 --> 01:28:27,637
WHILE THEY WENT INTO TOWN
AND STOLE EVERYBODY'S ANTIQUES.

2187
01:28:27,670 --> 01:28:29,972
- OH.
- WELL, I DON'T KNOW
IF THEY WERE THAT SMART.

2188
01:28:30,005 --> 01:28:31,973
I MEAN, LET'S REMEMBER,
THEY DID GET CAUGHT.

2189
01:28:32,008 --> 01:28:34,410
I THINK THEY JUST WENT ON
KILLING AND KILLING

2190
01:28:34,443 --> 01:28:36,812
UNTIL IT WAS
ALL ABOUT KILLING,

2191
01:28:36,845 --> 01:28:39,348
AND IT WASN'T
ABOUT FUN ANYMORE.

2192
01:28:39,382 --> 01:28:41,750
KNOWING WHAT I KNOW,
I GUESS THAT

2193
01:28:41,783 --> 01:28:43,720
THEY'RE SMARTER
THAN A SEA TURTLE

2194
01:28:43,753 --> 01:28:46,688
BUT DUMBER THAN
DANISH PHYSICIST NIELS BOHR.

2195
01:28:46,722 --> 01:28:48,190
YEAH, LIKE,
I CAN SEE THEM GOING

2196
01:28:48,223 --> 01:28:49,858
TO FOUR OF
THE POLICE ACADEMY MOVIES

2197
01:28:49,892 --> 01:28:51,360
BEFORE THEY STOP
SHELLING OUT THE DOUGH

2198
01:28:51,393 --> 01:28:53,128
AND WAITING FOR THEM
TO COME OUT ON SHOWTIME.

2199
01:28:53,162 --> 01:28:54,963
RIGHT.
THEY'RE THE KIND OF LEECHES

2200
01:28:54,997 --> 01:28:57,200
THAT WOULD PROBABLY
THINK OF CHILI'S

2201
01:28:57,233 --> 01:28:58,702
AS THEIR FAVORITE
RESTAURANT.

2202
01:28:58,735 --> 01:29:01,237
AND IT WOULD NEVER REALLY DAWN
ON THEM THAT IT WAS A CHAIN.

2203
01:29:01,270 --> 01:29:03,572
YEAH. OR THEY'D BE THE TYPE
TO WATCH PAID PROGRAMMING

2204
01:29:03,605 --> 01:29:05,375
AND NEVER FIGURE OUT
THAT IT WAS AN AD.

2205
01:29:05,408 --> 01:29:06,908
YEAH. [SERVO CHUCKLES]

2206
01:29:06,942 --> 01:29:08,410
WELL, THIS IS
A LOT OF FUN, YOU GUYS,

2207
01:29:08,443 --> 01:29:10,212
BUT I THINK IT'S TIME
TO READ A LETTER.

2208
01:29:10,245 --> 01:29:12,782
- OH BOY.
- LET'S PUT THIS UP ON
STILL STORE, CAMBOT.

2209
01:29:12,815 --> 01:29:16,652
UH, THIS ONE COMES FROM...

2210
01:29:16,685 --> 01:29:19,022
JEAN-- JEAN A. DUNN,

2211
01:29:19,055 --> 01:29:20,690
AND SHE WRITES,
"DEAR JOEL,

2212
01:29:20,723 --> 01:29:23,225
"I AM POSITIVELY CRAZY
ABOUT YOUR SHOW.

2213
01:29:23,258 --> 01:29:24,927
"WHEN I CAN FIND IT ON TV,

2214
01:29:24,960 --> 01:29:27,297
"I TAPE IT AND PLAY IT OVER
SO I DON'T MISS

2215
01:29:27,330 --> 01:29:29,632
"ANY OF YOUR
SARCASTIC REMARKS.

2216
01:29:29,665 --> 01:29:32,000
"I KEEP RECOMMENDING YOUR SHOW
TO EVERYONE I CAN.

2217
01:29:32,033 --> 01:29:35,270
"EVERYONE WHO IS
LUCKY TO CATCH IT LOVES IT.

2218
01:29:35,303 --> 01:29:36,805
"P.S. I AM 59 YEARS OLD,

2219
01:29:36,838 --> 01:29:38,808
AND I'VE NEVER WRITTEN
A FAN LETTER IN MY LIFE."

2220
01:29:38,842 --> 01:29:42,778
WELL, THANK YOU,
JEAN A. DUNN.

2221
01:29:42,812 --> 01:29:44,813
OH, BLESS YOU, JEE-A-AN.

2222
01:29:44,847 --> 01:29:47,217
- JEANNA DUNN.
- NICE LIFE GOAL.

2223
01:29:47,250 --> 01:29:48,650
JEAN-NEAN-EAN.

2224
01:29:48,683 --> 01:29:50,285
- JEAN.
- WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2225
01:29:50,318 --> 01:29:54,023
[LEECH SLURPS]

2226
01:29:54,057 --> 01:29:55,390
OH, SORRY, FRANK.

2227
01:29:55,425 --> 01:29:57,893
I LEFT THE LEECH ON
TOO LONG.

2228
01:29:57,927 --> 01:30:01,297
WELL, FRANK. FRANK?

2229
01:30:01,330 --> 01:30:03,232
WELL, NOW THAT
YOU'VE SUCKED ALL THE BLOOD

2230
01:30:03,265 --> 01:30:04,733
OUT OF FRANK,
WHAT'RE YOU GONNA DO NOW?

2231
01:30:04,767 --> 01:30:07,503
OH, WRITE, PRODUCE.
BE AS CREATIVE AS I CAN.

2232
01:30:07,537 --> 01:30:09,772
HAVE YOU THOUGHT ABOUT
THE MAD SCIENTIST GAME?

2233
01:30:09,805 --> 01:30:11,507
HAH! DON'T GET ME STARTED.

2234
01:30:11,540 --> 01:30:13,608
YOU KNOW, I GOT SOME IDEAS.
MAYBE WE COULD DO LUNCH.

2235
01:30:13,642 --> 01:30:15,177
- SURE.
- OH--

2236
01:30:15,210 --> 01:30:17,580
YOU THINK YOU COULD PICK IT UP?
I'M FLAT BUSTED.

2237
01:30:17,613 --> 01:30:19,682
YOU KNOW, I'D REALLY
LOVE TO PRODUCE YOU.

2238
01:30:19,715 --> 01:30:22,652
I HAD THIS CONCEPT
THAT MAYBE WE COULD GO...
